	# ---------------------------------------------------------------- structure
	"cx_bolt": ["螺栓", "BOLT"],
	"cx_bolt_a": ["可拆的固定点，维护工具拧下即松开，零件完好。", "A fixing made to come undone: the wrench backs it out and the part stays whole."],
	"cx_bolt_b": ["最后一颗松开，零件就没东西拉住，会带着惯性漂走。", "Take the last one out and nothing holds the part: it drifts off with whatever motion it had."],
	"cx_bolt_c": ["先用抓钩稳住，再松最后一颗。", "Steady it with the grapple first, then the last bolt."],
	"cx_bolt_x": ["船上的螺栓多是 M12–M24 的高强度螺栓，靠预紧力把两件压在一起，承受剪切和拉力的是摩擦面而不是螺杆本身。拧松它不改变零件本身，所以“能拧就别切”：螺栓拆下的设备保留全部价值，切开的只值废金属价。失重下没有地板替你接住东西，一件 0.5 t 的板只要 0.1 m/s 的余速，十秒后就离开一米。", "Ship bolts are mostly high-strength M12–M24, preloaded so the friction between the faces carries the load, not the shank. Backing one out changes nothing about the part, hence the rule \"unbolt before you cut\": unbolted equipment keeps its full value, cut equipment is scrap. In free fall nothing catches what you loosen: a 0.5 t plate with 0.1 m/s left on it is a metre away ten seconds later."],
	"cx_weld": ["焊缝", "WELD"],
	"cx_weld_a": ["两件金属熔成一体的连接，扳手拧不开。", "Two pieces of metal fused into one. No wrench undoes it."],
	"cx_weld_b": ["只能切。切开的位置决定剩下的东西还值多少。", "Only the laser parts it, and where you cut decides what the pieces are worth."],
	"cx_weld_c": ["沿焊缝或标线切，别切进设备本体。", "Cut along the seam or a marked line, never through the equipment itself."],
	"cx_weld_x": ["结构焊缝的强度和母材相当，激光要把整个截面熔透才算切开。切割速度由材料决定：普通钢板快，装甲和厚梁慢，冰和复合材料各有自己的规矩。激光前沿只按材料的限速追着光标走，贴着边慢慢推才提交切口——急着来回扫只会烧出一道浅沟。", "A structural weld is as strong as the plate around it; the beam has to melt the whole section through before it parts. How fast depends on the material: thin steel quick, armour and heavy beams slow, ice and composites with rules of their own. The cut front follows the cursor only as fast as the material lets it, and commits when it reaches the edge — sweeping back and forth just burns a shallow groove."],
	"cx_lock": ["锁扣", "LOCK"],
	"cx_lock_a": ["带锁销的快拆固定件，常藏在别的件后面。", "A quick-release fixing with a locking pin, often hidden behind something else."],
	"cx_lock_b": ["漏掉一个锁扣硬拽，零件会被扯坏或扯断锁扣弹开。", "Miss one and pull, and the part tears or the lock snaps and lets it fly."],
	"cx_lock_c": ["拽之前看光标提示还剩几个固定点。", "Before you pull, read how many fixings the cursor says are left."],
	"cx_lock_x": ["锁扣用在需要快速更换的地方：检修盖、可更换单元、货物托盘。它和螺栓一样能用维护工具打开，但拉力过大时会先于零件失效——所以抓钩硬拽时，被扯断的是锁扣，被撕坏的可能是零件的安装耳。拉扯只会扯断锁扣和管线，螺栓不会断。", "Locks go where things are meant to come out fast: service covers, replaceable units, cargo pallets. The wrench opens them like bolts, but under a big enough pull they fail before the part does — so when the grapple yanks, what snaps is the lock, and what tears may be the part's mounting ear. A pull only ever breaks locks and lines; bolts don't give."],
	"cx_clamp": ["船坞夹具", "BERTH CLAMP"],
	"cx_clamp_a": ["船坞的液压夹爪，把整艘船固定在泊位上。", "The berth's hydraulic jaws holding the whole ship in place."],
	"cx_clamp_b": ["夹具只夹某几件结构：把它们拆走，整艘船会松脱漂移。", "They grip a few structural pieces: take those away and the ship comes loose and drifts."],
	"cx_clamp_c": ["最后再拆夹具咬着的那几件。", "Leave whatever the clamps bite on until last."],
	"cx_clamp_x": ["夹具通常咬在龙骨或底板上。一艘几百吨的船只要获得 0.05 m/s，撞上泊位端墙时的冲量就足以撞坏舱内松动的设备。夹具咬着的件在蓝图里有标记，拆到后半程时先确认剩下的船体还有夹具抓着。", "The clamps usually bite the keel or the floor plates. A few hundred tonnes of ship picking up 0.05 m/s hits the berth's end wall hard enough to wreck anything loose inside. The pieces the clamps hold are marked on the drawing; late in a job, check what's left is still held."],
	"cx_hull": ["外壳板", "HULL PLATE"],
	"cx_hull_a": ["船的外皮，也是舱室的气密边界。", "The ship's skin, and the airtight wall of the rooms behind it."],
	"cx_hull_b": ["舱里还有气就切开，舱压会把板和里面的东西一起喷出去。", "Cut it with air still inside and the pressure blows the plate out, and what's behind it with it."],
	"cx_hull_c": ["先测舱压，放气到 5 kPa 以下再动它。", "Measure the room, vent it below 5 kPa, then work on it."],
	"cx_hull_x": ["一个标准大气压是 101 kPa，也就是每平方米 10 吨的力。一块 1 × 2 m 的舱壁板背后有 100 kPa，就有 20 吨在推它；切出一条缝，气流在缝口达到音速，几秒内把松动的零件和碎屑带出去。舱室低于 5 kPa 视为安全。", "One atmosphere is 101 kPa, ten tonnes on every square metre. A 1 × 2 m panel with 100 kPa behind it has twenty tonnes pushing on it; open a slit and the flow through it goes sonic, carrying loose parts and debris out within seconds. Below 5 kPa a room counts as safe."],
	"cx_bulkhead": ["舱壁", "BULKHEAD"],
	"cx_bulkhead_a": ["把船分成独立气密舱的内部隔墙。", "An internal wall dividing the ship into separate airtight rooms."],
	"cx_bulkhead_b": ["两侧压力不同时切开，高压一侧的气体和东西冲向低压一侧。", "Cut it with different pressures each side and the high side's air and loose things rush through."],
	"cx_bulkhead_c": ["两侧舱室都测一遍压力，先放气或平衡。", "Measure the rooms on both sides; vent or equalise first."],
	"cx_bulkhead_x": ["舱壁让一个舱的事故不扩散到全船，也让你可以分舱处理：一个舱放完气，隔壁可能还满着。压差才是危险的来源——两侧都是 100 kPa 时切开舱壁不会爆，但两个舱从此变成一个，放气时要一起放。", "Bulkheads keep one room's trouble out of the next, and let you work room by room: one emptied, the next may still be full. The danger is the difference: with 100 kPa on both sides a cut doesn't blow, but the two rooms become one and have to be vented together."],
	"cx_frame": ["承力结构", "LOAD-BEARING FRAME"],
	"cx_frame_a": ["龙骨、肋骨、纵梁、支撑杆：船的骨架。", "Keel, frames, longitudinals, struts: the ship's skeleton."],
	"cx_frame_b": ["切断还在承重的骨架，它托着的部分会坠落、弹开或扭断。", "Cut a member still carrying load and what it held drops, springs or twists off."],
	"cx_frame_c": ["先卸掉它托着的重量，最后再拆骨架。", "Take the weight off it first; the frame comes out last."],
	"cx_frame_x": ["失重下没有重力载荷，但还有预紧、惯性和船坞夹具传来的力：一根梁可能正把两台几十吨的设备撑在原位。骨架件通常很重，常超过抓钩 3 t 的上限，要沿标线切成段再运走。", "Free fall takes gravity away, not preload, inertia or the clamps' grip: a beam may be what keeps two machines of tens of tonnes in place. Frame pieces are heavy, often past the grapple's 3 t, and go out in sections cut along their marked lines."],
	"cx_door": ["舱门与货舱门", "DOORS AND HATCHES"],
	"cx_door_a": ["通往舱室的门，多数靠总线供电开关。", "The way into a room; most open on power from the ship's bus."],
	"cx_door_b": ["舱里有气就开门，门会被气压推开爆开；断电后有些门打不开。", "Open it with air inside and the pressure blows it open; with the power cut some won't open at all."],
	"cx_door_c": ["先放气再开门；要开的门，在断电前开。", "Vent the room before the door; open the doors you need before you cut the power."],
	"cx_door_x": ["一扇 2 m² 的门背后 60 kPa，就有 12 吨压在门上，电机打不开，锁一松就会被整扇推飞。货舱大门常由电机或液压驱动：先断了电池，它就只能切开。船坞的外部供电插座可以在断船电后给门临时供电。", "A 2 m² door with 60 kPa behind it carries twelve tonnes: no motor opens that, and the moment the latch gives the whole leaf flies. Big cargo doors run on motors or hydraulics: kill the battery first and the only way through is the laser. The berth's external power socket can feed a door once the ship's own power is off."],
	"cx_rail": ["轨道", "RAIL"],
	"cx_rail_a": ["货物、吊车或滑架沿着走的导轨。", "A guide rail cargo, cranes or cradles run along."],
	"cx_rail_b": ["切到还托着东西的轨道，那件东西会被扯坏或掉下去。", "Cut a rail still carrying something and that thing is torn or dropped."],
	"cx_rail_c": ["先把轨道上的东西运走，再拆轨道。", "Move what's on the rail off it first, then the rail."],
	"cx_rail_x": ["导轨把载荷分散到很多个支座上；切断一段，载荷全落到断口两边的支座，常常超出它们的能力。锁轨货物要从轨道上开出去，不能用扳手卸——见各船的锁轨条目。", "A rail spreads its load over many mounts; cut a length and the whole load falls on the two either side of the gap, usually more than they take. Rail-locked cargo is driven off its rail, not unbolted — see the rail-locked cargo entry."],
	"cx_film": ["薄膜", "FILM"],
	"cx_film_a": ["几微米厚的聚酰亚胺膜：帆面、气囊壁、遮阳膜。", "Polyimide a few microns thick: sail panels, gasbag walls, sunshades."],
	"cx_film_b": ["绷紧时一切就撕，裂口会沿张力方向跑开。", "Under tension it doesn't cut, it tears, and the tear runs along the load."],
	"cx_film_c": ["先松掉张力，再整块拆下。", "Slack it first, then take it off in whole panels."],
	"cx_film_x": ["薄膜的抗撕裂强度只有每米几牛，而张紧的帆面每米承受几十牛的膜应力。激光切出的切口是一个尖锐的裂纹源，在张力下以接近声速扩展。薄膜几乎没有质量，不挡碰撞也不挡路径，但会挡光、带静电。", "Film resists tearing at a few newtons per metre; a tensioned sail panel carries tens of newtons per metre of membrane stress. A laser kerf is a sharp crack start, and under tension it runs at close to the speed of sound. Film has next to no mass and doesn't block the drone, but it shades light and holds static charge."],
	"cx_cable": ["电缆", "CABLE"],
	"cx_cable_a": ["设备和电网之间的供电线，两端是可拔的接头。", "A power line from a device to the grid, with a plug at each end."],
	"cx_cable_b": ["带电拔或切会起弧，伤到无人机和设备。", "Pull or cut it live and it arcs, hurting the drone and the equipment."],
	"cx_cable_c": ["验电确认 0 V，再拔接头带走设备。", "Test it to 0 V, then unplug it and take the equipment."],
	"cx_cable_x": ["30 V 以下的电不会伤到无人机；船上的总线常在 28–400 V 之间，电容组可达上千伏。直流电弧不会像交流那样每秒过零 100 次自行熄灭，一旦拉起来就会一直烧。设备的电缆没拔，抓钩拉它会被拉住——拉力大了，扯断的是接头。", "Under 30 V can't hurt the drone; ship buses run 28 to 400 V and capacitor banks reach a thousand and more. A DC arc doesn't go out by itself a hundred times a second like AC does; drawn once, it keeps burning. A device still plugged in is held by its cable — pull hard enough and the plug is what tears."],
	"cx_pipe_line": ["管线", "PIPE"],
	"cx_pipe_line_a": ["冷却液、燃料或气体的管路，两端有接头。", "A line for coolant, fuel or gas, with a coupling at each end."],
	"cx_pipe_line_b": ["满管切开会漏，燃料会成可燃云，热管会烫伤。", "Cut a full line and it leaks: fuel makes a flammable cloud, a hot line burns."],
	"cx_pipe_line_c": ["从低点排放口抽空，测温不烫，再拔或切。", "Draw it off at the low-point drain, check it's not hot, then uncouple or cut."],
	"cx_pipe_line_x": ["管路系统里，阀门关了不等于管子空了：两阀之间总留着一段液体（死腿）。失重下漏出来的液体不会流到地上，而是变成漂浮的液团，碰到带电件就短路。60 °C 以上的管路会伤到抓取它的无人机。", "In a piping system a shut valve doesn't make the pipe empty: there's always a length trapped between two valves (a dead leg). In free fall what leaks doesn't run to the floor; it floats off in globules that short whatever live thing they touch. Lines over 60 °C hurt the drone that grabs them."],
	"cx_cut_line": ["标线（分段线）", "MARKED CUT LINE"],
	"cx_cut_line_a": ["超重设备上预先标出的切分位置。", "Where a piece too heavy to move is meant to be cut apart."],
	"cx_cut_line_b": ["随便切会切进内部零件，价值大减；整件又超出抓钩上限。", "Cut anywhere else and you cut into its insides; whole, it's beyond the grapple."],
	"cx_cut_line_c": ["沿标线切成几段，每段都在抓钩上限以内。", "Cut along the marked lines; each section is within the grapple's limit."],
	"cx_cut_line_x": ["抓钩额定 3 t（升级后 5 t）。超过它的设备在设计时就留了可分段的位置：法兰、模块接缝、无管线穿过的地方。沿标线切开，每段仍按设备回收；乱切的切口会穿过绕组、管束或电路板，剩下的只值废金属。", "The grapple is rated 3 t (5 t upgraded). Equipment heavier than that was built with places it can come apart: flanges, module seams, spans no pipe or cable crosses. Cut on the lines and each section still counts as equipment; a cut anywhere else goes through windings, tube bundles or boards, and what's left is scrap."],
	"cx_glass": ["玻璃与舷窗", "GLASS AND WINDOWS"],
	"cx_glass_a": ["压条螺栓固定的舷窗或精密玻璃罩板。", "A window or precision glass panel held in by clamping strips."],
	"cx_glass_b": ["背后有压力时拆会被推出去碎掉；附近动激光会烤裂。", "Unbolted with pressure behind it, it's blown out and shatters; a laser nearby cracks it."],
	"cx_glass_c": ["先泄压，远离它切割，拧下压条整块取出。", "Vent first, cut well away from it, unbolt the strips and lift it out whole."],
	"cx_glass_x": ["玻璃抗压不抗拉，表面的划痕和局部热应力都会成为裂纹源。激光在 0.7 m 内工作，辐射和溅射的热能让玻璃两面温差超过 100 °C，热应力足以让它开裂。完整的光学玻璃价值远高于碎玻璃（几乎为零）。", "Glass takes compression, not tension; a scratch or a hot spot is where a crack starts. With the laser working within 0.7 m, the heat thrown off can put a hundred degrees between its faces, enough thermal stress to craze it. Whole optical glass is worth a great deal; broken, next to nothing."],
	"cx_armor": ["装甲", "ARMOUR"],
	"cx_armor_a": ["厚的防护板：分层装甲、隔热瓦、屏蔽层。", "Thick protective plate: layered armour, heat tiles, shielding."],
	"cx_armor_b": ["切得极慢，热量会积在切口附近，烤坏贴着它的东西。", "It cuts very slowly, and the heat building up at the kerf cooks what's behind it."],
	"cx_armor_c": ["能拆螺栓就拆，切口选在远离设备的地方。", "Unbolt where you can; cut where nothing sits behind it."],
	"cx_armor_x": ["装甲靠厚度和硬度吸收能量，切割速度可低到普通钢板的十分之一。屏蔽层（钨、氢化锂）则是挡辐射用的，重而脆。外挂装甲条常用螺栓挂在船体上，拆下来比切穿快得多。", "Armour soaks up energy with thickness and hardness; it may cut ten times slower than plain plate. Shielding (tungsten, lithium hydride) stops radiation, heavy and brittle. Add-on armour strips usually hang on bolts — much faster off than through."],
	"cx_insul": ["隔热层", "INSULATION"],
	"cx_insul_a": ["两层蒙皮夹泡沫芯的隔热壁，或多层隔热毯。", "Foam core between two skins, or multilayer insulation blanket."],
	"cx_insul_b": ["破了隔热，冷舱回温、低温罐升压就会加快。", "Break it and a cold room warms, a cryogenic tank's pressure climbs, much faster."],
	"cx_insul_c": ["冷的东西没处理完之前，别动它的隔热层。", "Leave the insulation alone until what it keeps cold is dealt with."],
	"cx_insul_x": ["真空中的多层隔热毯靠几十层镀铝膜反射热辐射，漏热只有每平方米零点几瓦；划开一道口，那一块的漏热可以高十倍以上。低温货物的回温和蒸发速率直接由隔热完好度决定。", "In vacuum, multilayer insulation stops heat with tens of aluminised films, letting through a fraction of a watt per square metre; slit it and that patch leaks ten times more. How fast cold cargo warms or boils off comes straight from how sound its insulation is."],
	"cx_cover": ["检修盖与护板", "SERVICE COVERS"],
	"cx_cover_a": ["挡住后面设备或固定件的盖板。", "A panel over the equipment or fixings behind it."],
	"cx_cover_b": ["盖板后面的螺栓看不见、拧不到，常被漏掉。", "The bolts behind it can't be seen or reached, and get missed."],
	"cx_cover_c": ["先拆盖板，再找它后面的固定点。", "Take the cover off first, then look for what's behind it."],
	"cx_cover_x": ["工程图会画出盖板后面的东西，但图纸是设计时画的，不一定和现在的船对得上。被盖住的固定点在光标上不会显示，只有盖板拆走之后才可操作。", "The drawing shows what's behind a cover, but it was drawn at design time and may not match the ship now. Hidden fixings don't show under the cursor; they can only be worked once the cover is off."],
	"cx_port": ["接口（测压口 / 回收口）", "PORT"],
	"cx_port_a": ["接测量工具或回收软管的接口，接在某个舱、罐或管路上。", "A connection for the meter or the recovery hose, on a room, a tank or a line."],
	"cx_port_b": ["它测的是它连着的那一段：中间的阀关着，读数是零也不代表舱里没气。", "It reads what it's connected to: with a valve shut in between, zero doesn't mean the room is empty."],
	"cx_port_c": ["打开工程图，确认接口和目标之间的阀门是开的。", "Open the drawing and check every valve between the port and what you want is open."],
	"cx_port_x": ["测压口后面常有一段短管和阀门，阀门关着时，你测到的是这段短管（死腿）里的压力。回收口用软管把气体或液体抽进船坞的回收泵：气体按价值计入合同，抽的速度由接口的口径和泵的能力决定。", "Behind a pressure port there's often a short pipe and a valve; with the valve shut, what you read is that stub (the dead leg). A recovery port takes the hose to the berth's recovery pump: the gas or liquid is paid into the contract, as fast as the port's bore and the pump allow."],
	"cx_valve": ["阀门", "VALVE"],
	"cx_valve_a": ["开关一段管路或两个容积之间通路的手动阀。", "A hand valve that opens or shuts the way between two volumes."],
	"cx_valve_b": ["关着的阀会骗过测量；卡死的阀接不上软管。", "A shut valve fools your meter; a jammed one won't take the hose."],
	"cx_valve_c": ["维护工具开关它；卡死的先用扳手拧开。", "Turn it with the wrench; free a jammed one with the wrench first."],
	"cx_valve_x": ["阀门把系统分成段：每一段的压力、液位可以完全不同。查管路时顺着工程图从接口走到目标，每遇到一个阀门问一句：它现在是开还是关？", "Valves split a system into sections, each with its own pressure and level. Trace the drawing from the port to what you want and at every valve ask: is it open or shut right now?"],
	"cx_switch": ["开关", "SWITCH"],
	"cx_switch_a": ["电路的隔离开关、待发开关、刹车或锁的控制。", "A circuit isolator, an arming switch, a brake or a lock control."],
	"cx_switch_b": ["断一个开关只断一路：别的电源、蓄能还在。", "One switch kills one path: the other sources and stored energy are still there."],
	"cx_switch_c": ["断开后再验电或读表，确认真的归零。", "Switch it, then test or read the gauge to see it really went to zero."],
	"cx_switch_x": ["“关机不等于断电”：主开关只断主电源，备用电池、独立电源、电容组各自还可能带电。专项机制里的开关常有顺序（先冷却后刹车，先泄压后拔销），顺序错了比不动更糟。", "\"Off isn't dead\": the main switch isolates the main supply; backup batteries, independent supplies and capacitor banks may each still be live. The switches of a ship's special mechanisms often have an order (cooling before the brake, pressure off before the pins), and the wrong order is worse than none."],
	"cx_test": ["验电点", "TEST POINT"],
	"cx_test_a": ["电网上可以用测量工具读电压的点。", "A point on the grid where the meter reads the voltage."],
	"cx_test_b": ["它读的是它所在那段总线；别的支路可能另有电源。", "It reads its own stretch of bus; another branch may have its own supply."],
	"cx_test_c": ["断电、放电之后，再测一次确认 0 V。", "After isolating and discharging, test again for 0 V."],
	"cx_test_x": ["读数会过期：你测完之后开关一动，旧读数就不再是现在的状态。安全的流程是“断开—放电—验电”三步，最后一步必须在前两步之后。", "A reading goes stale: switch anything after you measured and the old number is no longer the truth. The safe sequence is isolate, discharge, verify — and the verify has to come after the other two."],
	"cx_probe": ["探头", "PROBE"],
	"cx_probe_a": ["读温度、液位、剂量、张力、转速等的传感器。", "A sensor reading temperature, level, dose, tension, speed and the like."],
	"cx_probe_b": ["不读就不知道：危险往往藏在数字里。", "Unread, you don't know: the danger is usually in the number."],
	"cx_probe_c": ["动手前用测量工具读一遍，动手后再读一遍。", "Read it with the meter before you work, and again after."],
	"cx_probe_x": ["专项机制几乎都有一个探头：线圈储能、飞轮转速、钻杆扭矩、罐压、氧浓度、剂量率、炉芯温度。读数告诉你还要等多久，或者哪一步还没做完。", "Nearly every special mechanism has its probe: a coil's stored energy, a flywheel's speed, a drill string's torque, a tank's pressure, oxygen, dose rate, a core's temperature. The reading says how long to wait, or which step isn't done."],
	"cx_socket": ["外部插座", "EXTERNAL SOCKET"],
	"cx_socket_a": ["船坞的临时供电、供冷或地线接口。", "Where the berth plugs in temporary power, cooling or an earth."],
	"cx_socket_b": ["断了船电，有些系统还需要外来的电或冷才能安全收尾。", "With the ship's own power off, some systems still need outside power or cooling to finish safely."],
	"cx_socket_c": ["断船电之前先把船坞的那一路接上。", "Plug the berth's supply in before you kill the ship's."],
	"cx_socket_x": ["船坞供电让门、泵、制冷机在船电断开后还能工作；船坞供冷让冷链货舱不回温；地线把帆面这类大面积带电体的静电导走。插座在外部面板上，接上后才算有效。", "Berth power keeps doors, pumps and chillers working after the ship's own is off; berth cooling keeps a cold hold from warming; an earth drains the static off a big charged surface like a sail. The sockets are on the outside panel and count once plugged."],
	"cx_discharge": ["放电点", "DISCHARGE POINT"],
	"cx_discharge_a": ["让电容组经电阻受控放电的开关。", "A switch that bleeds a capacitor bank through a resistor."],
	"cx_discharge_b": ["电容断电后仍能存着上千焦的能量，碰一下就是电弧。", "Isolated, a capacitor still holds kilojoules; touch it and it arcs."],
	"cx_discharge_c": ["打开放电，等到电量归零，再验电。", "Open the discharge, wait for it to reach zero, then test."],
	"cx_discharge_x": ["电容储能 E = ½CV²：一组 0.1 F 的电容在 400 V 下存 8 kJ。经电阻放电时电压按 e^(−t/RC) 衰减，大约五个时间常数后降到 1% 以下。放电点通常在设备附近的接线盒上。", "A capacitor stores E = ½CV²: a 0.1 F bank at 400 V holds 8 kJ. Through the resistor its voltage falls as e^(−t/RC), under 1 % after about five time constants. The discharge point is usually on a junction box near the equipment."],
	"cx_seal": ["密封盖", "SEAL"],
	"cx_seal_a": ["把生物危险品封进密封袋或密封盖的控件。", "The control that closes a biohazard item into its seal."],
	"cx_seal_b": ["没封就搬或切，污染会散进整个舱室的空气。", "Moved or cut unsealed, it spills contamination into the room's air."],
	"cx_seal_c": ["先封好，再整件送危险品口。", "Seal it first, then take it whole to the hazard mouth."],
	"cx_seal_x": ["生物污染随空气流动：舱门打开、舱壁切开，污染就扩散到隔壁舱。被污染舱室里的完好设备要走洗消，价值降四分之一。", "Contamination travels with the air: open a door or cut a bulkhead and it spreads to the next room. Whole equipment in a contaminated room has to be decontaminated and loses a quarter of its value."],
	# ---------------------------------------------------------------- systems
	"cx_s_gas": ["舱压", "ROOM PRESSURE"],
	"cx_s_gas_a": ["每个密封舱里还留着的空气或工艺气体。", "The air or process gas still held in each sealed room."],
	"cx_s_gas_b": ["带压开口会爆开：门、板和舱里的东西一起喷出去。", "Open it under pressure and it blows: door, plate and contents thrown out."],
	"cx_s_gas_c": ["从接口测压，接软管放气到 5 kPa 以下，再开口。", "Measure at a port, hose it down below 5 kPa, then open it."],
	"cx_s_gas_x": ["舱压由舱里气体的量和舱的容积决定（pV = nRT）。回收泵从接口把气抽走，压力按指数下降：舱越大、接口越小，越慢；大舱可能要几十秒。舱壁一旦有了开口，气体就从开口流向压力低的一侧，相连的几个舱会变成一个。抽走的气体按价值计入合同。", "A room's pressure comes from how much gas is in it and its volume (pV = nRT). The recovery pump draws it off through a port and the pressure falls away exponentially: the bigger the room and the smaller the port, the slower; a big hold can take tens of seconds. Once a wall has an opening, gas flows to the low side and connected rooms become one. Recovered gas is paid into the contract."],
	"cx_s_stale": ["读数会过期", "READINGS GO STALE"],
	"cx_s_stale_a": ["测到的数字只代表测的那一刻。", "A reading is true only for the moment you took it."],
	"cx_s_stale_b": ["之后开了阀、断了电，旧读数就不是现在的状态。", "Open a valve or cut a supply afterwards and the old number is no longer the state."],
	"cx_s_stale_c": ["改动之后重新测一次；过期的读数会变灰。", "After any change, measure again; stale readings grey out."],
	"cx_s_stale_x": ["压力变化超过 2 kPa（或 4%），或者电路的连接关系改变，读数就标为过期。船上的面板和总览屏显示的是“上一次记录”，同样可能早已过期——永远以自己刚测的为准。", "A pressure reading goes stale when the pressure moves more than 2 kPa (or 4 %); a voltage reading when the circuit's connections change. Panels and overview screens on board show their last record, which may be long out of date — trust only what you just measured."],
	"cx_s_power": ["电网与多路电源", "POWER AND ITS SOURCES"],
	"cx_s_power_a": ["发电机、电池、电容、独立电源经总线供给设备。", "Generators, batteries, capacitors and independent supplies feed the equipment over the bus."],
	"cx_s_power_b": ["主电源关了，备用电池、独立电源、电容还能让设备带电。", "Main power off, a backup battery, an independent supply or a capacitor can still keep it live."],
	"cx_s_power_c": ["找出每一路电源：逐个断开、放电，再验电。", "Find every source: isolate each, discharge, then test."],
	"cx_s_power_x": ["工程图的电路层画出每条电缆和它连到哪里。独立电源（无人机电池、门锁备用电源、仪器的不间断电源）只供它那一小片，主开关管不到它；接在总线上的独立电源还会反过来给整条总线供电。超过 30 V 的设备拔线、切割会起弧。", "The drawing's circuit layer shows every cable and where it goes. An independent supply (a drone's battery, a door lock's backup, an instrument's UPS) feeds its own little patch, beyond the main switch's reach; one tied to the bus feeds the whole bus back. Over 30 V, unplugging or cutting draws an arc."],
	"cx_s_heat": ["热管线与余热", "HEAT"],
	"cx_s_heat_a": ["发动机、反应堆、炉子停了以后还热着的管线和设备。", "Lines and machines still hot after an engine, reactor or furnace stopped."],
	"cx_s_heat_b": ["60 °C 以上抓取会伤无人机；骤冷会让热件开裂。", "Over 60 °C they hurt the drone; quenched suddenly, hot parts crack."],
	"cx_s_heat_c": ["测温，让冷却系统把它带下来，冷透再拆。", "Measure, let the cooling bring it down, take it out cold."],
	"cx_s_heat_x": ["真空里没有对流，热只能靠辐射和传导散掉：一件几百度的设备自然冷却可能要几个小时。冷却回路有电、有液时才能带走热量；先断冷却再等，等于把它关在保温瓶里。", "In vacuum there's no convection; heat leaves only by radiation and conduction, and a machine at a few hundred degrees may take hours to cool alone. The cooling loop carries heat off only while it has power and coolant; cut it first and wait, and you've shut it in a vacuum flask."],
	"cx_s_cloud": ["推进剂云", "PROPELLANT CLOUD"],
	"cx_s_cloud_a": ["漏出的燃料蒸气在舱里或船外聚成的一团。", "Leaked fuel vapour gathering in a room or outside the hull."],
	"cx_s_cloud_b": ["激光扫进去就点燃，起火、爆燃。", "Sweep the laser into it and it lights: fire, a flash."],
	"cx_s_cloud_c": ["先回收燃料、等云散开，再在附近切割。", "Recover the fuel and let the cloud disperse before cutting near it."],
	"cx_s_cloud_x": ["燃料蒸气只在一定浓度范围内能燃烧（肼约 4.7–100%，氢约 4–75%），太稀太浓都点不着；但云团边缘总有一圈正好在范围内。真空里云团会慢慢扩散变稀，舱里有空气时散得慢得多。", "Fuel vapour burns only within a band of concentration (hydrazine about 4.7–100 %, hydrogen 4–75 %), too lean or too rich won't light — but the edge of a cloud is always somewhere in the band. In vacuum the cloud spreads and thins; in a room with air it lingers much longer."],
	"cx_s_fire": ["火灾", "FIRE"],
	"cx_s_fire_a": ["燃料只在有空气的舱里、或碰到氧化剂时才烧；真空里它只会蒸发、结冰、漂走。", "Fuel burns only in a room with air, or where it meets an oxidiser; in vacuum it just boils off, freezes and drifts."],
	"cx_s_fire_b": ["激光、电弧、带电电缆的火花、短路、刚切的红热切口、尾焰、爆炸都能点着；火逐团蔓延，舱压可升到 8 倍冲开舱门。", "Laser, arc, live-cable spark, short, fresh hot cut, thruster, blast: any lights it. It spreads; room pressure can rise 8x and blow the doors."],
	"cx_s_fire_c": ["先把舱抽成真空再动激光；着火的舱别开门补氧，等它把氧耗光。", "Vent the room to vacuum before the laser; don't open a burning room's door to feed it air, let it use its oxygen up."],
	"cx_s_fire_x": ["火需要燃料、氧气和点火源三样。失重下火焰没有浮力，成一个缓慢的球，靠扩散补氧。火把舱里的氧耗光会自己灭，但燃料还在，补进空气、再来一个火星就会复燃。封闭舱里的燃烧把气体加热到几千度，压力跟着升到原来的数倍。", "Fire needs fuel, oxygen and a spark. Without gravity a flame has no buoyancy: it sits in a slow sphere fed by diffusion. A fire that uses up a room's oxygen goes out on its own, but the fuel is still there: let air in, add a spark, and it lights again. In a closed room the burning heats the gas to thousands of degrees and the pressure rises several times over."],
	"cx_s_liquid": ["失重液体", "LIQUIDS IN FREE FALL"],
	"cx_s_liquid_a": ["漏出的液体在失重下变成漂浮的液团。", "Liquid let loose in free fall becomes drifting globules."],
	"cx_s_liquid_b": ["碰到带电设备会短路，燃料遇激光起火，低温液体冻裂设备。", "A globule shorts live equipment, fuel lights under the laser, cryogens crack what they touch."],
	"cx_s_liquid_c": ["接软管从接口抽空，再切管或拆罐。", "Draw it off through a port with the hose before cutting the line or moving the tank."],
	"cx_s_liquid_x": ["没有重力，液体靠表面张力收成球，保持动量直线漂移，碰到表面要么溅开、要么摊成液膜跟着那件走。液氢、液氦一出来就闪蒸掉一部分，其余边漂边沸；水在真空里几秒内结成冰球；燃料慢慢挥发，蒸气汇进可燃云；钻井泥浆落哪粘哪。", "With no gravity, surface tension pulls liquid into balls that drift in straight lines and either splash or wet the surface they meet, then travel with it. Liquid hydrogen and helium flash part away on release and boil as they drift; water freezes into a ball of ice within seconds in vacuum; fuel evaporates slowly into a flammable cloud; drilling mud sticks wherever it lands."],
	"cx_s_hose": ["回收软管", "RECOVERY HOSE"],
	"cx_s_hose_a": ["气液回收工具接上接口，把气体或液体抽进船坞的泵。", "The recovery tool on a port, drawing gas or liquid into the berth's pump."],
	"cx_s_hose_b": ["接错接口会混料；抽干了还开着，有些泵会干转损坏。", "The wrong port mixes the media; left running dry, some pumps wreck themselves."],
	"cx_s_hose_c": ["接上后看读数下降，到量后摘下软管。", "Hose on, watch the reading fall, take it off when it's done."],
	"cx_s_hose_x": ["一条软管同时只接一个接口。抽速随压力（或液位）降低而变慢，按住 = 会加速时间。回收的气体和液体按市价计入合同；危险介质要接到对应的回收口，不能放到太空。", "One hose, one port at a time. The draw slows as the pressure or level drops; hold = to speed time up. What's recovered is paid into the contract at market price; hazardous media have to go to their own recovery, never to space."],
	"cx_s_free": ["脱离与惯性", "FREE PIECES AND INERTIA"],
	"cx_s_free_a": ["最后一个固定点松开，零件就成了自由漂浮的刚体。", "With its last fixing gone a part becomes a free-floating body."],
	"cx_s_free_b": ["它保持原来的速度和转动，撞上别的东西会撞坏。", "It keeps its speed and spin, and whatever it runs into gets damaged."],
	"cx_s_free_c": ["用抓钩接住，慢慢送进回收口。", "Catch it with the grapple and ease it into a mouth."],
	"cx_s_free_x": ["失重下没有摩擦帮你停下：推一下就一直走，停下来要同样大的反推。重的件动量大，0.5 m/s 的 3 t 设备和 1.5 m/s 的 1 t 设备撞起来一样狠。船坞边缘的牵引场会把漂出去的东西慢慢拉回来。", "Free fall has no friction to stop things: a push goes on forever, and stopping takes the same push the other way. Heavy pieces carry momentum — 3 t at 0.5 m/s hits as hard as 1 t at 1.5 m/s. The tractor field at the berth's edge slowly pulls back what drifts out."],
	"cx_s_grapple": ["磁力抓钩", "MAGNETIC GRAPPLE"],
	"cx_s_grapple_a": ["无人机抓住、拖动零件的工具。", "The drone's tool for holding and towing parts."],
	"cx_s_grapple_b": ["超过额定质量拖不动；拉还连着的件会扯断锁扣和管线。", "Over its rating it can't move a load; pulling something still fixed tears its locks and lines."],
	"cx_s_grapple_c": ["先看质量和剩余固定点，再拖。", "Check the mass and the fixings left before you tow."],
	"cx_s_grapple_x": ["抓钩额定 3 t（升级 5 t）。无人机的推力有限，拖着重物时加速慢、刹车也慢，要提前减速。还连着的件被拉时，光标会显示剩几个固定点；拉力越大，越先断的是锁扣和管线。", "Rated 3 t (5 t upgraded). The drone's thrust is limited: towing, it speeds up slowly and stops slowly, so start braking early. Pulling something still fixed, the cursor shows the fixings left; pull harder and the locks and lines go first."],
	"cx_s_furnace": ["熔炉与废料口", "THE FURNACE"],
	"cx_s_furnace_a": ["泊位底部的废料口：废金属进去，熔成钢锭按吨付钱。", "The scrap mouth in the berth's floor: scrap goes in, is melted to ingots and paid by the tonne."],
	"cx_s_furnace_b": ["危险品、带电或带压的东西进炉会炸。完整设备进炉只值废金属价。", "Hazards, live or pressurised things go off in it. Whole equipment sent in is paid as scrap."],
	"cx_s_furnace_c": ["只送纯金属废料；6–8 m 外对准长槽甩进去就行。", "Only plain scrap; from 6–8 m out, line it up with the trough and let it go."],
	"cx_s_furnace_x": ["炉口下面：料仓把废料压实，螺旋给料机送进一台真空感应炉。坩埚以 45 rpm 旋转，离心力把熔池压在炉衬上（约 1.4 g）。水冷铜线圈产生交变磁场，在金属里感应涡流加热（集肤深度 δ = 503·√(ρ/μf)）；炉温升到 1640 °C 出钢，倒进水冷铜锭模。真空本身就是熔炼条件。", "Under the mouth a bunker compacts the scrap and a screw feeder charges a vacuum induction furnace. The crucible spins at 45 rpm so the melt is held against the lining at about 1.4 g. A water-cooled copper coil drives eddy currents in the metal (skin depth δ = 503·√(ρ/μf)); at 1,640 °C it taps into water-cooled copper ingot moulds. The vacuum is the berth's own."],
	"cx_s_equip_mouth": ["设备回收口", "EQUIPMENT BAY"],
	"cx_s_equip_mouth_a": ["收完整设备的回收口，从下方送入。", "The mouth for whole equipment, fed from below."],
	"cx_s_equip_mouth_b": ["损坏或切开的设备按成色折价，带电带液的会出事。", "Damaged or cut equipment is marked down; live or wet equipment causes trouble."],
	"cx_s_equip_mouth_c": ["断电、排空、拔线之后整件送进来。", "Isolated, drained and unplugged, then in whole."],
	"cx_s_equip_mouth_x": ["设备按“价值 × 成色”付钱：撞击、过热、短路、污染都会降成色。合同里的指定件必须完整送达这里。离口太远时，设备口会把接收环移向你。", "Equipment pays its value times its condition: knocks, heat, shorts and contamination all lower the condition. A contract's named items must arrive here whole. Far from the bay, it moves its receiving ring towards you."],
	"cx_s_hazard_mouth": ["危险品口", "HAZARD MOUTH"],
	"cx_s_hazard_mouth_a": ["收燃料罐、电池、火工品、放射源等危险品的回收口。", "The mouth for fuel tanks, batteries, pyrotechnics, radioactive parts."],
	"cx_s_hazard_mouth_b": ["危险品送进熔炉会爆炸或污染。", "A hazard sent to the furnace explodes or contaminates."],
	"cx_s_hazard_mouth_c": ["光标显示“危险品”的件，只送这里。", "Anything the cursor calls a hazard goes here and nowhere else."],
	"cx_s_hazard_mouth_x": ["危险品口按危险处理津贴付钱，不按金属价。它的口子小，要慢慢对准；拖着危险品靠近熔炉时，指导会提醒你。", "The hazard mouth pays a handling allowance, not the metal price. Its opening is small, so line up slowly; towing a hazard near the furnace draws a warning."],
	"cx_s_field": ["牵引场", "TRACTOR FIELD"],
	"cx_s_field_a": ["泊位开放边缘的力场，把漂出去的东西拉回来。", "The field along the berth's open edges, pulling back what drifts out."],
	"cx_s_field_b": ["它只拉回，不刹车：高速漂出的件仍会撞上东西。", "It pulls back, it doesn't brake: something fast still hits what's in its way."],
	"cx_s_field_c": ["别指望它救场，脱离前先抓住。", "Don't count on it; catch things before they go."],
	"cx_s_field_x": ["泊位是半开放的：底部平台、塔架和悬臂，上方和右侧开放。牵引场在内框以外起作用，越往外拉力越大。船坞扩建时，场的边界会先外推到新的端部之外。", "The berth is half open: floor, tower and boom, open above and to the right. The field acts outside the inner frame and pulls harder the further out you go. When the berth is extended, the field's edge is pushed out past the new end first."],
	"cx_s_berth_ext": ["船坞扩建", "BERTH EXTENSION"],
	"cx_s_berth_ext_a": ["买下的扩建在现场按真实的在轨桁架施工流程建起来。", "A bought extension is built on site the way a real in-space truss job runs."],
	"cx_s_berth_ext_b": ["施工时工区封闭，任何东西进去都会被牵引场推开。", "During the works the zone is closed; the field pushes anything out of it."],
	"cx_s_berth_ext_c": ["看着它建，或任意键跳过。", "Watch it go up, or skip with any key."],
	"cx_s_berth_ext_x": ["流程：工区隔离 → 拖船推入折叠桁架盒 → 铰接桁架从储筒逐节展开（每节 0.6 m，横撑锁正后再展下一节）→ 每个模块接口先钩爪锁紧、再上 M20 10.9 级螺栓（预紧 125 kN）→ 电子束焊接缝（电子束焊需要真空，泊位本身就是）→ 管路用氦气加压到 1.5 倍工作压力检漏，同时新地板承受 1.25 倍设计载荷（挠度限值 L/800）→ 调试认证。高船进坞时，塔架顶升加节、平台同步下放。", "Close the work zone → a tug pushes in the folded truss cassettes → the articulated truss deploys bay by bay out of its canister (0.6 m a bay, each squared and locked before the next) → each module interface latched, then bolted with M20 grade 10.9 bolts at 125 kN preload → the seams electron-beam welded (EB welding needs a vacuum, which the berth is) → the lines proof-pressurised with helium at 1.5 × working pressure and leak-checked while the new floor carries 1.25 × its design load (deflection limit L/800) → commissioned. For a tall ship, the tower is jacked up section by section and the platform lowered in step."],
	"cx_s_blueprint": ["工程图", "THE DRAWING"],
	"cx_s_blueprint_a": ["船的设计图：管路、电路、舱室和固定件。", "The ship's design drawing: pipes, circuits, rooms and fixings."],
	"cx_s_blueprint_b": ["图是设计时画的，船是后来出事的：两者不一定对得上。", "It was drawn at design time; the ship had its accident later. They may not agree."],
	"cx_s_blueprint_c": ["用它找东西、查走向；东西现在的状态自己测。", "Use it to find things and trace lines; check their state yourself."],
	"cx_s_blueprint_x": ["Tab 打开。图上能看到盖板后面的设备、阀门在哪条管线上、每台设备的电从哪里来。改装、事故、维修留下的变化不在图上：多出来的电源、被堵的接口、补过的管子，只有现场测得出来。", "Tab opens it. It shows the equipment behind covers, which line a valve sits on, where each machine's power comes from. What modifications, accidents and repairs changed isn't on it: an extra supply, a blocked port, a patched pipe — only measuring on site finds those."],
	"cx_s_scope": ["分段与抢救合同", "PART-SHIP CONTRACTS"],
	"cx_s_scope_a": ["只拆指定区段，或只取指定设备的合同。", "A contract for one section only, or only for named equipment."],
	"cx_s_scope_b": ["动了范围外的件，损坏或拆走都要按违约扣钱。", "Damage or take anything outside the scope and you pay for it."],
	"cx_s_scope_c": ["看清界面上画出的区段边界，范围外的不碰。", "Read the section boundary drawn on screen; leave what's outside alone."],
	"cx_s_scope_x": ["分段拆解只买区段内的零件，不买气体和液体；抢救单按件付固定报酬，送齐即结束，船体其余部分由拖船拖走。光标会对范围外的件标“范围外”。", "A section job buys the pieces inside it, not the gas or fluids; a salvage job pays a fixed sum per named item and ends when they're in, the rest of the hull towed away. The cursor marks out-of-scope pieces."],
	"cx_s_hauler": ["搬运无人机", "HAULING DRONE"],
	"cx_s_hauler_a": ["船坞悬臂上的辅助机，把标记的零件运进回收口。", "The helper on the boom that carries marked pieces to the mouths."],
	"cx_s_hauler_b": ["它只运你标记的件，不检查危险：带电带液的照样搬。", "It carries what you mark without checking: live or wet, it moves it."],
	"cx_s_hauler_c": ["处理完危险再右键标记，让它去运。", "Make a piece safe, then mark it (right click) and let it carry it."],
	"cx_s_hauler_x": ["搬运无人机按标记顺序排队，自己找路、选回收口。它省掉的是重复的拖运，不省判断：哪件已经安全、哪件该进哪个口，仍然由你决定。", "The hauler queues marked pieces in order, finds its own way and picks the mouth. It saves the repetitive towing, not the judgement: which piece is safe and where it goes is still yours."],
	"cx_s_impact": ["撞击", "IMPACT"],
	"cx_s_impact_a": ["漂浮的零件、无人机或整段船体撞上别的东西。", "A floating piece, the drone or a section of hull running into something."],
	"cx_s_impact_b": ["撞击按速度变化折损两边的成色，精密件最怕。", "An impact marks down both sides by the change in speed; precision parts suffer worst."],
	"cx_s_impact_c": ["拖运时慢一点、提前刹车，别让东西自己漂。", "Tow slowly, brake early, don't let things drift on their own."],
	"cx_s_impact_x": ["撞击的伤害取决于速度变化（Δv）和件的易损度。1 m/s 的撞击对钢结构无所谓，对光学玻璃或芯片就是致命的。拖着重物刹不住时，松开抓钩反而更糟：它会带着全部动量继续走。", "Damage comes from the change in speed (Δv) and how fragile the piece is. 1 m/s means nothing to steel and everything to optical glass or a chip. Towing something you can't stop, letting go is worse: it carries all its momentum on."],
	# ---------------------------------------------------------------- devices: power
	"cx_swb": ["配电盘", "SWITCHBOARD"],
	"cx_swb_a": ["母排、仪表和一排塑壳断路器：全船电力在这里分路。", "Busbars, meters and a stack of moulded-case breakers: where the ship's power is split up."],
	"cx_swb_b": ["它是电网的汇点，任何一路电源都可能让它带电。", "Every source on the ship can make it live; it's where they all meet."],
	"cx_swb_c": ["先断所有电源，在它的验电点测到 0 V 再拆。", "Isolate every source, test 0 V at its test point, then remove it."],
	"cx_swb_x": ["上部是三相母排室，下面每个分段一块仪表板和一列断路器，电缆从底部的格兰板进线。断路器断开的是负载侧：母排上游只要有一路电源没断，整块盘依然带电。母排之间的电弧温度可达上万度。", "Along the top the three-phase busbar chamber; below it each section's meter panel and a column of breakers, the cables rising through the gland plate. A breaker opens the load side only: while any source upstream is live, the whole board is. An arc between busbars runs at over ten thousand degrees."],
	"cx_battery": ["电池组", "BATTERY PACK"],
	"cx_battery_a": ["串联的电芯模块、汇流排、冷板和电池管理板。", "Modules of cells in series, busbars, a cooling plate and the battery management board."],
	"cx_battery_b": ["断不掉的电源：开关只断外部，电芯里的能量一直在。", "A source you can't switch off inside: the switch isolates its output, not the cells."],
	"cx_battery_c": ["断开它的隔离开关，拔掉输出线，整件送危险品口。", "Open its isolator, unplug its output, take it whole to the hazard mouth."],
	"cx_battery_x": ["一组 50 kWh 的锂电池在满电时储存 180 MJ。电芯短路或穿刺会热失控：电芯温度在几秒内升到 600 °C 以上，释放可燃气体并引燃相邻电芯。主接触器在模块一端，断开后电池端子之间仍有全电压。", "A 50 kWh lithium pack holds 180 MJ when full. A shorted or punctured cell runs away thermally: past 600 °C in seconds, venting flammable gas and lighting its neighbours. The main contactor sits at one end; open, the pack's own terminals still carry full voltage."],
	"cx_cap": ["电容组", "CAPACITOR BANK"],
	"cx_cap_a": ["一排电容罐、汇流排和放电电阻，储能供脉冲用电。", "A row of capacitor cans, busbars and a discharge resistor, storing energy for pulse loads."],
	"cx_cap_b": ["断电后仍保持高压，碰一下就是电弧。", "Isolated it still holds its voltage; touch it and it arcs."],
	"cx_cap_c": ["找到它的放电点，放到 0 再验电。", "Find its discharge point, bleed it to zero, then test."],
	"cx_cap_x": ["E = ½CV²：0.1 F 在 400 V 下存 8 kJ，发射系统的电容组可达兆焦级。电容没有“关”：只能放电。放电电阻按 RC 时间常数把能量变成热，约五个时间常数降到 1%。", "E = ½CV²: 0.1 F at 400 V holds 8 kJ, and a launcher's bank holds megajoules. A capacitor has no off, only discharged. The resistor turns its energy to heat on the RC time constant, under 1 % after five of them."],
	"cx_gen": ["发电机组", "GENERATING SET"],
	"cx_gen_a": ["发动机拖动的发电机，带散热器、励磁机和控制屏。", "An engine driving an alternator, with radiator, exciter and control panel."],
	"cx_gen_b": ["停机不等于断电：别的电源会经总线倒送到它的出线端。", "Stopped isn't dead: other sources feed back to its terminals through the bus."],
	"cx_gen_c": ["确认停机，断开它的出线，验电后拆。", "Confirm it's stopped, isolate its output, test, then remove."],
	"cx_gen_x": ["发电机的转子是凸极磁极，定子槽里嵌着绕组；转起来时，即使励磁断开，剩磁也能发出几十伏。机组质量常在 1–3 t，底座有减振器，螺栓都在底座上。", "The rotor carries salient poles, the windings sit in the stator slots; spinning, even unexcited, the residual magnetism gives tens of volts. A set weighs 1–3 t; its bolts are on the base frame, under the anti-vibration mounts."],
	"cx_panel": ["控制箱", "CONTROL ENCLOSURE"],
	"cx_panel_a": ["墙挂的电气控制箱：门、指示灯窗、端子和格兰。", "A wall-hung electrical enclosure: door, indicator window, terminals and glands."],
	"cx_panel_b": ["箱子小，接进来的电源可能不止一路。", "Small box, possibly more than one supply into it."],
	"cx_panel_c": ["按工程图找全它的进线，逐一断开再拆。", "Find every incoming line on the drawing, isolate each, then remove it."],
	"cx_panel_x": ["控制箱里多是继电器、PLC 和端子排，自身价值不高但接线密集；拆它之前把每根进线都处理掉，比拆完再一根根找省事。", "Inside are relays, a PLC and terminal rails: not worth much, but densely wired. Deal with every incoming line before removing it rather than chasing them afterwards."],
	"cx_junction": ["接线盒", "JUNCTION BOX"],
	"cx_junction_a": ["四角螺钉的盒盖、接地螺柱、进出线格兰。", "A lid on four corner screws, an earth stud, cable glands in and out."],
	"cx_junction_b": ["多条电缆在这里分支，常有验电点或放电点。", "Cables branch here; test points and discharge points often sit on it."],
	"cx_junction_c": ["在这里验电和放电，再处理它连着的设备。", "Test and discharge here, then deal with what it feeds."],
	"cx_junction_x": ["接线盒是电路的“路口”：查一台设备的电从哪来，从它的接线盒倒着找最快。", "A junction box is a crossroads of the circuit: to find where a device's power comes from, work back from its junction box."],
	"cx_transformer": ["变压器", "TRANSFORMER"],
	"cx_transformer_a": ["三柱铁芯、高低压绕组和夹紧框架的干式变压器。", "A dry-type transformer: three-limb core, low- and high-voltage windings, clamping frame."],
	"cx_transformer_b": ["一侧有电，另一侧就有电：从低压侧倒送也会升出高压。", "Live on one side means live on the other: back-fed from the low side it puts out high voltage."],
	"cx_transformer_c": ["高低压两侧都断开、验电，再拆。", "Isolate and test both sides before removing it."],
	"cx_transformer_x": ["绕组匝比决定电压比，10:1 的变压器从低压侧倒送 400 V，高压侧就是 4 kV。干式变压器很重，铁芯占了大半质量，常要沿夹件分开运。", "The turns ratio sets the voltage ratio: back-feed 400 V into a 10:1 transformer's low side and its high side sits at 4 kV. It's heavy, most of it core, and often has to come apart at its clamps to move."],
	"cx_inverter": ["逆变器", "INVERTER"],
	"cx_inverter_a": ["IGBT 模块、散热器、直流母线电容和输出电抗器。", "IGBT modules on a heat sink, DC-link capacitors and an output choke."],
	"cx_inverter_b": ["断电后直流母线电容还存着电，几分钟才自放完。", "Off, its DC-link capacitors still hold charge for minutes."],
	"cx_inverter_c": ["断开直流输入，等放电或接放电点，验电后拆。", "Isolate its DC input, wait or bleed it down, test, then remove."],
	"cx_inverter_x": ["逆变器把直流斩成交流驱动电机。直流母线电容是它的“蓄水池”，额定电压常在 600–800 V，自带的泄放电阻要几分钟才能把它放到安全电压。", "An inverter chops DC into AC for a motor. Its DC-link capacitors are its reservoir, rated 600–800 V, and its own bleed resistors take minutes to bring them down to a safe level."],
	"cx_fuelcell": ["燃料电池", "FUEL CELL STACK"],
	"cx_fuelcell_a": ["上百片双极板夹在端板之间，拉杆紧固，配鼓风机和加湿器。", "Hundreds of bipolar plates between end plates and tie rods, with blower and humidifier."],
	"cx_fuelcell_b": ["只要还有氢和氧，它就在发电：关了总线它照样带电。", "With hydrogen and oxygen left, it generates: kill the bus and it's still live."],
	"cx_fuelcell_c": ["断它自己的开关，关燃料阀、抽空氢气，再拆。", "Switch it off at its own switch, shut and draw off the hydrogen, then remove it."],
	"cx_fuelcell_x": ["每片电池约 0.7 V，几百片串联到几百伏。电堆内的氢气即使阀门关了也会残留，泄漏到舱里就形成可燃云（氢的燃烧范围 4–75%，点火能极低）。", "Each cell gives about 0.7 V; hundreds in series make hundreds of volts. Hydrogen stays in the stack after the valves shut, and leaked into a room it makes a flammable cloud (4–75 % in air, the smallest of sparks lights it)."],
	"cx_charger": ["充电桩", "CHARGING STATION"],
	"cx_charger_a": ["给无人机或车辆充电的模块，带枪头和线缆。", "A charging unit for drones or vehicles, with its connector and cable."],
	"cx_charger_b": ["接着充电线时，两头都可能带电。", "With the cable plugged in, both ends may be live."],
	"cx_charger_c": ["断开充电开关，拔掉充电线，再动它充的东西。", "Switch the charger off and unplug the lead before touching what it charges."],
	"cx_charger_x": ["充电桩自己从总线取电，又把电送进被充的设备；被充的设备若自带电池，拔线时电池一侧也带电。", "A charger takes power from the bus and puts it into what it charges; if that has its own battery, the battery end of the lead is live too."],
	"cx_dump_res": ["泄能电阻", "DUMP RESISTOR"],
	"cx_dump_res_a": ["一排排来回折叠的不锈钢带，接在超导磁体的泄能回路上。", "Banks of stainless ribbon folded back and forth, on a superconducting magnet's dump circuit."],
	"cx_dump_res_b": ["泄能时它把磁能变成热，满负荷时发红；拆了它磁体就无处泄能。", "Dumping, it turns stored field energy into heat and glows; take it away and the magnet has nowhere to dump."],
	"cx_dump_res_c": ["磁体泄完能之前，别动它和它的母排。", "Leave it and its busbars alone until the magnets are run down."],
	"cx_dump_res_x": ["线圈电流经泄能电阻衰减：I = I₀·e^(−t/τ)，τ = L/R。电阻越大泄得越快，但线圈两端电压 = I·R 也越高。几十吉焦的储能在几十秒内变成热，电阻带温度可升到几百度。", "The coil's current falls through the resistor as I = I₀·e^(−t/τ), τ = L/R. More resistance dumps faster but puts more voltage (I·R) across the coil. Tens of gigajoules become heat in tens of seconds; the ribbon reaches hundreds of degrees."],
	"cx_slip_ring": ["滑环", "SLIP RING"],
	"cx_slip_ring_a": ["旋转侧的一叠铜环和固定侧的电刷，给转动的环供电。", "A stack of rings on the turning side and brushes on the fixed side: power into something spinning."],
	"cx_slip_ring_b": ["环带电时刹车，电机回馈电流穿过滑环会烧毁它。", "Brake a ring while its bus is live and the motor's regenerated current burns the slip ring."],
	"cx_slip_ring_c": ["先断环上的负载，再刹车消旋。", "Take the ring's loads off before braking it."],
	"cx_slip_ring_x": ["电刷在铜环上滑动导电，电流密度有限；回馈电流和起弧会在环面烧出凹坑。它是旋转居住环唯一的电力通路。", "The brushes slide on the rings to carry current, which has a limit; regenerated current and arcing pit the ring faces. It's the habitat ring's only way in for power."],
	"cx_tray": ["电缆桥架", "CABLE TRAY"],
	"cx_tray_a": ["顶板下的梯式桥架，里面成捆的电缆，配灯和喷头。", "A ladder tray under the deckhead, cables bundled in it, lights and sprinklers along it."],
	"cx_tray_b": ["桥架里的电缆一根带电，整捆都不能切。", "One live cable in the bundle and none of it can be cut."],
	"cx_tray_c": ["断开它承载的电路，再拆桥架。", "Isolate the circuits it carries, then take the tray."],
	"cx_tray_x": ["桥架本身只是金属结构，危险来自它承载的线：动力、信号、控制混在一起，拆之前按电路层把每路都确认掉。", "The tray is just metalwork; the danger is what it carries — power, signal and control mixed together. Check every circuit in it on the drawing before it comes out."],
	"cx_module": ["可更换单元（ORU）", "ORBITAL REPLACEMENT UNIT"],
	"cx_module_a": ["为整件更换设计的密封箱：两个抓手、自锁螺钉、盲插接头。", "A sealed box made to be swapped whole: two grab handles, captive fasteners, blind-mate connectors."],
	"cx_module_b": ["接头面插着时硬拽，会撕坏背板的接头。", "Pulled while still mated, it rips the connectors off the backplane."],
	"cx_module_c": ["松开自锁螺钉，断电后整件拔出。", "Undo the captive fasteners and pull it whole once power is off."],
	"cx_module_x": ["ORU 是航天器“整件更换”的思路：机械臂或宇航员戴手套就能操作，所以它是最好拆的设备之一，完整价值也最高。", "The ORU is how spacecraft are maintained by swapping whole units — a robot arm or a gloved hand can do it — which makes it one of the easiest things to recover whole."],
	# ---------------------------------------------------------------- devices: fluids, gases, heat
	"cx_pump": ["离心泵组", "CENTRIFUGAL PUMP SET"],
	"cx_pump_a": ["蜗壳、轴承架、联轴器和电机装在同一底座上。", "Volute, bearing frame, coupling and motor on one baseplate."],
	"cx_pump_b": ["进出口管还满着、电机还带电：切管漏液，拔线起弧。", "Its lines still full, its motor still live: cut a line and it leaks, pull the lead and it arcs."],
	"cx_pump_c": ["断电、从排放口抽空，拔线拔管后整件拆下。", "Isolate, drain at the low point, uncouple lines and lead, then lift it whole."],
	"cx_pump_x": ["离心泵靠叶轮把液体甩向蜗壳外缘，速度变成压力。它最怕干转：没有液体冷却和润滑，机械密封几十秒内就会烧坏。完整的泵价值远高于废金属。", "The impeller flings liquid to the volute's rim, turning speed into pressure. It hates running dry: with no liquid to cool and lubricate it, the mechanical seal burns within tens of seconds. Whole, a pump is worth far more than its metal."],
	"cx_hx": ["管壳式换热器", "SHELL-AND-TUBE HEAT EXCHANGER"],
	"cx_hx_a": ["壳体里的管束，两种介质隔着管壁换热。", "A tube bundle in a shell: two fluids trading heat through the tube walls."],
	"cx_hx_b": ["壳程和管程是两套液体，常常一套空了另一套还满。", "Shell side and tube side are two fluids; one emptied, the other may still be full."],
	"cx_hx_c": ["两侧都排空，再拆它的管口。", "Drain both sides before opening its nozzles."],
	"cx_hx_x": ["折流板让壳程液体来回横穿管束，提高换热系数。一台换热器里两侧的压力、温度、介质都不同，它的四个管口要分开处理。", "Baffles send the shell-side fluid back and forth across the bundle to raise the heat transfer. Each side has its own pressure, temperature and medium, and its four nozzles are four separate jobs."],
	"cx_radiator": ["散热板", "RADIATOR PANEL"],
	"cx_radiator_a": ["两端集管之间排满流道管的散热面，靠辐射把热排进太空。", "Flow tubes between two headers across a fin sheet, radiating heat to space."],
	"cx_radiator_b": ["管里还有冷却液；系统还热时收拢或拆下，板会变形。", "Its tubes still hold coolant; folded or removed while the system is hot, it deforms."],
	"cx_radiator_c": ["等冷却回路把热带走、排空后再拆。", "Let the loop carry the heat away and drain it before you take it."],
	"cx_radiator_x": ["太空中散热只能靠辐射：P = εσAT⁴。在 300 K，每平方米约排 400 W，所以散热板要做得很大。板面薄而轻，铰链接在吊杆上，抓住它要轻。", "In space heat only leaves by radiation: P = εσAT⁴. At 300 K a square metre sheds about 400 W, which is why radiators are big. The panels are thin and light, hinged to their booms; handle them gently."],
	"cx_chiller": ["制冷机组", "CHILLER"],
	"cx_chiller_a": ["压缩机、冷凝器、膨胀阀和蒸发器组成的制冷回路。", "Compressor, condenser, expansion valve and evaporator in one refrigeration loop."],
	"cx_chiller_b": ["一停或一切坏，它保冷的货舱或设备就开始回温。", "Stopped or cut, whatever it keeps cold starts to warm."],
	"cx_chiller_c": ["先接上船坞供冷或处理完冷货，再停它。", "Plug in berth cooling or deal with the cold cargo before stopping it."],
	"cx_chiller_x": ["制冷剂在蒸发器里吸热沸腾，被压缩后在冷凝器里放热凝结。回路里的制冷剂要从储液罐回收口闭环回收，不能放空。", "The refrigerant boils in the evaporator taking heat in, is compressed, and condenses in the condenser giving it out. It's recovered in a closed loop from the receiver's port, never vented."],
	"cx_freezer": ["超低温冷柜", "ULTRA-LOW FREEZER"],
	"cx_freezer_a": ["−80 °C 的样品或药品冷柜：保温门、控制器、压缩机舱。", "A −80 °C freezer for samples or medicine: insulated door, controller, compressor bay."],
	"cx_freezer_b": ["断电后里面的东西慢慢回温，有的样品一回温就作废。", "Off, its contents slowly warm, and some samples are lost the moment they do."],
	"cx_freezer_c": ["带电整件送设备口，或先确认里面没有需要保冷的东西。", "Send it whole while powered, or check nothing in it needs the cold."],
	"cx_freezer_x": ["保温良好的冷柜断电后每小时回温几度；门一开就快得多。冷链货物的价值往往取决于它从没超过某个温度。", "A well-insulated freezer warms a few degrees an hour unpowered, much faster with the door open. Cold-chain goods are often worth what they are only if they never went above a set temperature."],
	"cx_env": ["空气处理机", "AIR HANDLING UNIT"],
	"cx_env_a": ["进风阀、过滤器、冷却盘管、离心风机和送风箱。", "Intake damper, filter, cooling coil, centrifugal fan and discharge plenum."],
	"cx_env_b": ["盘管里有冷却液，接水盘可能有积水；风机由总线供电。", "Its coil holds coolant and its drain pan may hold water; the fan runs off the bus."],
	"cx_env_c": ["断电、排空盘管，再拆风管和底座螺栓。", "Isolate, drain the coil, then the ducts and the base bolts."],
	"cx_env_x": ["空气处理机让舱里的空气循环、降温、除湿。它是舱室里最大的设备之一，沿气流方向一段段排开；舱里的空气压力和它无关，放气要走舱的接口。", "It circulates, cools and dries a room's air. It's one of the biggest things in a room, laid out along its airflow; the room's pressure is nothing to do with it — vent through the room's own port."],
	"cx_duct_fan": ["风道轴流风机", "AXIAL DUCT FAN"],
	"cx_duct_fan_a": ["风道里的电机、叶片和导流叶。", "A motor, blades and straightener vanes inside a duct."],
	"cx_duct_fan_b": ["带电拆接线盒会起弧；叶轮可能还在惯性转动。", "Its terminal box arcs if opened live; the impeller may still be coasting."],
	"cx_duct_fan_c": ["断电，等叶轮停下，再拆法兰。", "Isolate, let it spin down, then unbolt the flanges."],
	"cx_duct_fan_x": ["风机断电后叶轮靠惯性还能转一阵，真空里没有空气阻力，会转得更久。", "An unpowered fan coasts on; in vacuum, with no air to slow it, for longer still."],
	"cx_filter": ["过滤器", "CARTRIDGE FILTER"],
	"cx_filter_a": ["壳体里的折叠滤芯，进出口、压差表和排放阀。", "A pleated element in a housing, with inlet, outlet, a differential gauge and a drain valve."],
	"cx_filter_b": ["滤芯截留的东西可能有毒、有污染、或带放射性。", "What the element caught may be toxic, contaminated or radioactive."],
	"cx_filter_c": ["先排空，带污染的滤芯封好送危险品口。", "Drain it; a contaminated element is sealed and sent to the hazard mouth."],
	"cx_filter_x": ["压差表读滤芯两侧的压降，堵得越多压降越大。隔离舱、核设施、生物舱的过滤器本身就是危险品。", "The differential gauge reads the drop across the element, rising as it clogs. In isolation rooms, reactors and bio bays the filter is itself a hazard."],
	"cx_trap": ["疏水器", "CONDENSATE TRAP"],
	"cx_trap_a": ["倒置浮桶式疏水器：排出冷凝水、留住蒸汽。", "An inverted-bucket trap: lets condensate out, keeps steam in."],
	"cx_trap_b": ["蒸汽管路里的它可能又热又带压。", "On a steam line it may be hot and under pressure."],
	"cx_trap_c": ["测温、泄压后再拆。", "Measure the temperature, relieve the pressure, then remove it."],
	"cx_trap_x": ["浮桶里有蒸汽时浮起关阀，有冷凝水时下沉开阀。失重下它靠的是压差和流动，不是浮力——船上的疏水器都是改过的。", "Steam floats the bucket and shuts the valve, water sinks it and opens it. Without gravity it works on pressure difference and flow rather than buoyancy — ship traps are modified for it."],
	"cx_manifold": ["阀组（总管）", "VALVE MANIFOLD"],
	"cx_manifold_a": ["一根总管上分出多路支管，每路一个隔离阀。", "One header with several branches, each with its isolating valve."],
	"cx_manifold_b": ["每路支管里的介质、压力可能不同，拆总管时各路一起漏。", "Each branch may hold a different medium at a different pressure; take the header off and they all leak."],
	"cx_manifold_c": ["逐路关阀、排空、测过，再拆总管。", "Shut, drain and check branch by branch, then the header."],
	"cx_manifold_x": ["阀组让一台泵服务多个罐。开着的支路之间是连通的：抽一个罐时其它罐的阀没关，会一起被抽，或者在总管里混料。", "A manifold lets one pump serve many tanks. Open branches are connected: draw one tank with the others' valves open and they're drawn too, or mixed in the header."],
	"cx_aux": ["调节阀", "CONTROL VALVE"],
	"cx_aux_a": ["球形阀体、阀盖、膜片执行器和定位器：自动调节流量的阀。", "Globe body, bonnet, diaphragm actuator and positioner: a valve that sets a flow by itself."],
	"cx_aux_b": ["执行器断气断电时会自动走到“故障位”，可能开也可能关。", "With its air or power gone it goes to its fail position, which may be open or shut."],
	"cx_aux_c": ["别靠它隔离；用手动阀隔离后再拆。", "Don't rely on it to isolate; isolate with hand valves, then remove it."],
	"cx_aux_x": ["调节阀按控制信号连续开度，阀芯有间隙，本来就不是密封用的。故障开（FO）的阀在断电后全开。", "A control valve throttles continuously to its signal; its trim has clearances and was never meant to seal. A fail-open valve goes fully open when the power goes."],
	"cx_relief": ["安全阀", "PRESSURE RELIEF VALVE"],
	"cx_relief_a": ["弹簧压着阀芯，超压时自动开启泄放。", "A spring holds the disc shut; over its set pressure it lifts and vents."],
	"cx_relief_b": ["冻住、堵住的安全阀不会开：罐压会一直升到爆。", "Frozen or blocked, it won't lift: the pressure climbs until the vessel bursts."],
	"cx_relief_c": ["测阀体温度，冻住的先解冻，或从接口抽低压力。", "Read its body temperature; thaw a frozen one, or draw the pressure down at a port."],
	"cx_relief_x": ["安全阀是压力容器最后一道保护，整定压力通常是设计压力的 1.0–1.1 倍；起跳后压力降到回座压力才重新关闭。低温罐的安全阀出口会被泄放的冷气冻上冰塞。", "The relief valve is a pressure vessel's last line, set at 1.0–1.1 × its design pressure; once lifted it reseats only below its reseat pressure. On a cryogenic tank, the cold gas it vents can freeze an ice plug in its own outlet."],
	"cx_pipe": ["管路", "PIPE RUN"],
	"cx_pipe_a": ["带法兰、保温和吊架的一段管道。", "A length of pipe with flanges, lagging and hangers."],
	"cx_pipe_b": ["满管切开会漏液或喷出可燃物。", "Cut full, it leaks or sprays something flammable."],
	"cx_pipe_c": ["上下游关阀、从低点排空，再拆法兰。", "Valve it off both ends, drain from the low point, then unbolt the flanges."],
	"cx_pipe_x": ["拆法兰比切管干净：法兰螺栓松开后管段完整，可以整段回收。管段里残留的液体在失重下不会自己流出来，要靠抽。", "Unbolting a flange is cleaner than cutting: the spool comes away whole. What's left inside won't run out by itself without gravity; it has to be drawn."],
	"cx_hpu": ["液压站", "HYDRAULIC POWER UNIT"],
	"cx_hpu_a": ["油箱、电机泵、蓄能器、电磁阀块和压力表。", "Reservoir, motor-pump, accumulators, solenoid valve block, pressure gauge."],
	"cx_hpu_b": ["蓄能器里存着高压油：断电后压力还在，管一切就喷。", "Its accumulators hold oil under pressure: off, the pressure stays, and a cut line sprays."],
	"cx_hpu_c": ["开泄压阀把蓄能器压力放到 0，再拆管和机构。", "Open the dump valve, bring the accumulators to zero, then the lines and what they drive."],
	"cx_hpu_x": ["液压系统常在 20 MPa 以上工作：一个 20 L 的蓄能器在 20 MPa 时存约 200 kJ。它驱动的缸、夹钳、机械臂只要还保着压，就是一根压缩着的弹簧。", "Hydraulics often run above 20 MPa: a 20 L accumulator at 20 MPa holds about 200 kJ. Every cylinder, clamp and arm it drives is a compressed spring while it holds pressure."],
	"cx_actuator": ["直线作动器", "LINEAR ACTUATOR"],
	"cx_actuator_a": ["电机、皮带、滚珠丝杠和推杆：把转动变成直线推力。", "Motor, belt, ball screw and rod: rotation turned into a straight push."],
	"cx_actuator_b": ["带电时控制线一断，推杆可能猛地一动；它顶着的东西没锁会掉。", "Live, a cut control line can jerk the rod; what it holds up drops if unlocked."],
	"cx_actuator_c": ["先锁住它或它支撑的东西，断电后再拆。", "Lock it or what it carries, kill its supply, then remove it."],
	"cx_actuator_x": ["滚珠丝杠效率高，反过来也能被推动：断电后没有刹车的作动器会被负载推着倒转。精密场合（镜片促动器）有专门的锁定机构。", "A ball screw is efficient enough to be back-driven: unpowered and unbraked, the load pushes it round. Precision uses — a mirror's actuators — have their own locks."],
	"cx_gastank": ["气瓶", "GAS CYLINDER"],
	"cx_gastank_a": ["带瓶阀和手轮的高压气瓶，色环标出气体种类。", "A high-pressure cylinder with valve and handwheel, coloured bands naming the gas."],
	"cx_gastank_b": ["高压气瓶被切开才会爆裂：气体冲进舱里或漂散，瓶阀断掉时整瓶像火箭一样飞出去。", "A full cylinder only bursts when cut: the gas floods the room or drifts off, and with its valve sheared it flies like a rocket."],
	"cx_gastank_c": ["密封完好的满瓶整瓶送设备回收口；要放气就从它的 -V 接口放，别切。", "A sealed full cylinder goes whole to the equipment mouth; to empty it, vent at its -V port. Never cut it."],
	"cx_gastank_x": ["一只 50 L、200 bar 的气瓶储存约 1.5 MJ 的压缩能。瓶阀断掉时，喷口推力可达瓶重的几十倍。氧气瓶还会让周围的东西更容易燃烧。", "A 50 L cylinder at 200 bar holds about 1.5 MJ. With its valve sheared off, the jet's thrust is tens of times its weight. An oxygen cylinder also makes everything round it burn more readily."],
	"cx_fueltank": ["推进剂 / 工艺储罐", "PROPELLANT TANK"],
	"cx_fueltank_a": ["卧在鞍座上的压力容器，内有防晃隔板，顶部管口和液位计。", "A pressure vessel in its saddles, with baffles inside, nozzles on top and a level gauge."],
	"cx_fueltank_b": ["还有液或带压就切会爆；漏出的燃料成可燃云。", "Cut with liquid or pressure in it, it bursts; leaked fuel makes a flammable cloud."],
	"cx_fueltank_c": ["从回收口抽空、泄掉罐顶气，整件送危险品口。", "Draw it empty at its port, vent the ullage, take it whole to the hazard mouth."],
	"cx_fueltank_x": ["储罐上方的气垫（罐顶气）保持罐压，让泵吸得进液体。抽液时要么维持增压，要么让空气补进来；在真空里只抽不补，罐会被抽瘪。", "The gas cushion above the liquid (the ullage) keeps the tank pressurised so the pump can draw. Drawing off, either keep the pressurisation on or let gas in; in vacuum, drawing alone can collapse the tank."],
	"cx_sphere_tank": ["球形压力罐", "SPHERICAL TANK"],
	"cx_sphere_tank_a": ["赤道环焊缝、安装耳、推进剂管理叶片和顶部加注阀。", "A girth weld, mounting tabs, propellant management vanes and a fill valve on top."],
	"cx_sphere_tank_b": ["球罐承压最高：切开就是一次爆炸。", "Spheres carry the highest pressures: cutting one is an explosion."],
	"cx_sphere_tank_c": ["测压，从接口泄压到安全，再拆安装耳。", "Measure, relieve it at the port, then unbolt its tabs."],
	"cx_sphere_tank_x": ["同样壁厚，球的承压能力是圆筒的两倍，所以高压气体和推进剂常装在球罐里。失重下推进剂管理叶片靠毛细作用把液体引到出口。", "For the same wall a sphere holds twice the pressure of a cylinder, so high-pressure gas and propellant go in spheres. In free fall the vanes wick the liquid to the outlet by capillary action."],
	"cx_cryotank": ["低温储罐", "CRYOGENIC TANK"],
	"cx_cryotank_a": ["真空夹套里的内罐：液氢、液氮或液化天然气在沸点下储存。", "An inner tank in a vacuum jacket: liquid hydrogen, nitrogen or LNG stored at its boiling point."],
	"cx_cryotank_b": ["一直在蒸发升压；安全阀冻住就会爆罐。", "It boils off all the time and its pressure climbs; with its relief valve frozen it bursts."],
	"cx_cryotank_c": ["保持制冷，边抽边降压，最后再断电。", "Keep it refrigerated, draw it down to lower the pressure, cut the power last."],
	"cx_cryotank_x": ["液氢在 −253 °C、液氮在 −196 °C 沸腾。热量每漏进一点，就蒸发一点液体变成气体，体积膨胀几百倍——这就是低温罐压力不断上升的原因。真空夹套一破，漏热增加十倍。", "Liquid hydrogen boils at −253 °C, nitrogen at −196 °C. Every bit of heat that leaks in boils some liquid off, expanding hundreds of times — which is why a cryogenic tank's pressure keeps rising. Lose the vacuum jacket and the heat leak goes up tenfold."],
	"cx_water": ["水箱", "WATER TANK"],
	"cx_water_a": ["带人孔、通气管、防晃板和液位镜的水箱。", "A tank with manway, vent, baffles and a sight glass."],
	"cx_water_b": ["切开后水漂出来，碰到带电设备就短路。", "Cut open, the water drifts out and shorts what it touches."],
	"cx_water_c": ["从出水阀或接口抽空，再拆。", "Draw it off at the outlet or a port, then remove it."],
	"cx_water_x": ["水在真空里先剧烈沸腾，蒸发吸热让剩下的水在几秒内结冰，成为缓慢升华的冰球。水是船上值钱的货：几立方米的水按合同价计。", "In vacuum water boils hard at first; the evaporation chills the rest into a slowly subliming ball of ice within seconds. Water is worth money: cubic metres of it are paid into the contract."],
	"cx_extinguisher": ["灭火瓶", "FIRE SUPPRESSION BOTTLE"],
	"cx_extinguisher_a": ["带释放头、压力表和电磁启动器的灭火剂瓶。", "A suppressant bottle with discharge head, gauge and solenoid actuator."],
	"cx_extinguisher_b": ["启动器带电时误触发会喷放；瓶本身是高压容器。", "Its actuator, if live, can fire it; the bottle itself is a pressure vessel."],
	"cx_extinguisher_c": ["需要灭火时用它；不用就断电后整瓶送危险品口。", "Use it if there's a fire; otherwise isolate it and send it whole to the hazard mouth."],
	"cx_extinguisher_x": ["船上常用 CO₂、哈龙替代品或泡沫。在密闭舱里喷放 CO₂ 能把氧浓度降到燃烧下限以下，但也意味着这个舱里的气体不能再按空气回收。有的船上灭火瓶早已空了——测一下压力表。", "Ships carry CO₂, halon replacements or foam. Discharged in a closed room CO₂ takes the oxygen below what burns, though the room's gas is no longer clean air to recover. Some ships' bottles are long empty — read the gauge."],
	"cx_o2cab": ["应急氧气柜", "EMERGENCY OXYGEN CABINET"],
	"cx_o2cab_a": ["玻璃门里两只氧气瓶、减压器和面罩。", "Two oxygen cylinders behind a glass door, a regulator and a mask."],
	"cx_o2cab_b": ["高压纯氧：附近动激光会让火势猛增。", "High-pressure pure oxygen: a laser near it makes any fire far fiercer."],
	"cx_o2cab_c": ["关瓶阀，整柜送危险品口。", "Shut the cylinder valves and send the cabinet whole to the hazard mouth."],
	"cx_o2cab_x": ["氧气本身不燃，但能让几乎所有东西燃烧得更快、更热；浸过氧的织物、油脂甚至金属屑都可能被点燃。", "Oxygen doesn't burn itself but makes almost anything burn faster and hotter; oxygen-soaked fabric, grease, even metal swarf can light."],
	"cx_co2_scrubber": ["CO₂ 洗涤器", "CO₂ SCRUBBER"],
	"cx_co2_scrubber_a": ["双床胺吸收（或沸石）罐、切换阀和鼓风机。", "Twin amine (or zeolite) beds, switching valves and a blower."],
	"cx_co2_scrubber_b": ["吸附床里富集着 CO₂，再生管线通向真空。", "The beds hold concentrated CO₂; the regeneration line opens to vacuum."],
	"cx_co2_scrubber_c": ["断电，关切换阀，再拆。", "Isolate it, close the switching valves, then remove it."],
	"cx_co2_scrubber_x": ["两个床交替工作：一个吸附舱里的 CO₂，另一个对真空解吸再生。人呼出的 CO₂ 浓度过 1% 就会头痛，过 5% 有生命危险。", "The beds take turns: one absorbs the cabin's CO₂ while the other desorbs to vacuum. Above 1 % CO₂ people get headaches; above 5 % it's dangerous."],
	"cx_psa": ["变压吸附分离器", "PRESSURE-SWING ADSORPTION"],
	"cx_psa_a": ["两根吸附塔和上下切换阀组：从混合气里分离出某种气体。", "Two adsorber columns and switching manifolds: one gas separated out of a mixture."],
	"cx_psa_b": ["塔里有压力，分离出的可能是纯氧、纯氮或氢。", "The columns are under pressure, and what they separate may be pure oxygen, nitrogen or hydrogen."],
	"cx_psa_c": ["关进气，从接口泄压，再拆。", "Shut the feed, relieve it at a port, then remove it."],
	"cx_psa_x": ["分子筛在高压下多吸附某种分子、低压下放出，两塔交替加压减压，就能连续产出纯气。纯氮环境会让人无预兆地窒息。", "A molecular sieve takes up one kind of molecule at high pressure and lets it go at low; two columns swinging in turn make a steady stream of pure gas. Pure nitrogen suffocates without warning."],
	"cx_electrolyser": ["电解制氧机", "WATER ELECTROLYSER"],
	"cx_electrolyser_a": ["电解槽、氢氧气液分离器、循环泵和整流器。", "Cell stack, hydrogen and oxygen separators, circulation pump and rectifier."],
	"cx_electrolyser_b": ["同时有氢、有氧、有电：泄漏就是爆鸣气。", "Hydrogen, oxygen and power in one place: a leak is a detonating mixture."],
	"cx_electrolyser_c": ["断电，两侧气体分别放空，再拆。", "Isolate it, vent each gas separately, then remove it."],
	"cx_electrolyser_x": ["电解 1 kg 水产生约 1.24 m³ 氢气和 0.62 m³ 氧气，耗电约 5 kWh。氢氧以 2:1 混合是最猛烈的爆鸣气。", "Splitting 1 kg of water gives about 1.24 m³ of hydrogen and 0.62 m³ of oxygen for some 5 kWh. Mixed two to one they make the most violent of detonating gases."],
	"cx_humidifier": ["加湿器", "STEAM HUMIDIFIER"],
	"cx_humidifier_a": ["电极沸腾筒、进排水阀、蒸汽软管和控制盒。", "Electrode boiling cylinder, fill and drain valves, steam hose, control box."],
	"cx_humidifier_b": ["筒里是热水和带电的电极。", "Hot water and live electrodes in the cylinder."],
	"cx_humidifier_c": ["断电，排水，再拆。", "Isolate, drain, then remove it."],
	"cx_humidifier_x": ["电极式加湿器让电流直接穿过水把它烧开：水的导电性决定功率。断电后筒里的水仍然很烫。", "An electrode humidifier boils water by passing current straight through it; the water's conductivity sets the power. The water stays hot after it's switched off."],
	"cx_uv_steriliser": ["紫外消毒器", "UV STERILISER"],
	"cx_uv_steriliser_a": ["不锈钢腔体中间一根紫外灯管，配强度传感器和镇流器。", "A stainless chamber with a UV lamp down its axis, intensity sensor and ballast."],
	"cx_uv_steriliser_b": ["灯管含汞，石英套管易碎；腔体里是水。", "The lamp holds mercury and its quartz sleeve breaks easily; the chamber is full of water."],
	"cx_uv_steriliser_c": ["断电、排空，整件送设备口。", "Isolate, drain, send it whole to the equipment bay."],
	"cx_uv_steriliser_x": ["254 nm 紫外线破坏微生物的 DNA。灯管破碎会释放汞蒸气。", "254 nm ultraviolet breaks microbes' DNA. A broken lamp releases mercury vapour."],
	"cx_separator_3ph": ["三相分离器", "THREE-PHASE SEPARATOR"],
	"cx_separator_3ph_a": ["卧式容器里用堰板把油、水、气分开，各有出口。", "A horizontal vessel whose weir splits oil, water and gas, each to its own outlet."],
	"cx_separator_3ph_b": ["容器里常留有残压和三种介质。", "It usually keeps some pressure and all three phases."],
	"cx_separator_3ph_c": ["从塔上的接口泄压，三路分别排空，再拆。", "Relieve it at its port, drain the three outlets, then remove it."],
	"cx_separator_3ph_x": ["地面上分离靠重力；船上的分离器靠旋流或离心力代替重力，结构类似但更紧凑。", "On the ground separation runs on gravity; aboard ship it's done with swirl or centrifuge instead, similar in layout but more compact."],
	"cx_coriolis": ["科氏流量计", "CORIOLIS FLOW METER"],
	"cx_coriolis_a": ["两根弯管在激振器驱动下振动，测出质量流量。", "Two bent tubes driven to vibrate; their twist gives the mass flow."],
	"cx_coriolis_b": ["它装在管路里：拆它等于断开那条管。", "It sits in the line: taking it out opens the line."],
	"cx_coriolis_c": ["先排空它所在的管路，再拆法兰。", "Drain its line first, then unbolt the flanges."],
	"cx_coriolis_x": ["流体流过振动的管子时受科里奥利力，两端振动出现相位差，相位差正比于质量流量。精度可达 0.1%，很贵。", "Fluid in a vibrating tube feels a Coriolis force; the two ends fall out of phase in proportion to the mass flow. Good to 0.1 %, and expensive."],
	"cx_level_radar": ["雷达液位计", "RADAR LEVEL GAUGE"],
	"cx_level_radar_a": ["从罐顶法兰伸进罐里的喇叭天线和电子头。", "A horn antenna through a tank's top flange, with its electronics head."],
	"cx_level_radar_b": ["它装在罐口上：罐里有压，拆它就开了一个口。", "It's in the tank's roof: pressurised, taking it off opens a hole."],
	"cx_level_radar_c": ["读它的液位，罐空了再拆。", "Read its level; take it off once the tank is empty."],
	"cx_level_radar_x": ["雷达测量电磁波到液面再反射回来的时间。失重下液面不平，船上的液位计读的是平均值。", "It times a radar pulse to the surface and back. Without gravity the surface isn't flat, so a ship's gauge reads an average."],
	"cx_gauge_box": ["载荷传感器（应变片）", "LOAD CELL"],
	"cx_gauge_box_a": ["弹性体上贴着金属箔应变片，读结构里的受力。", "Foil strain gauges on a flexure body, reading the load in a structure."],
	"cx_gauge_box_b": ["读数高说明这里在承受大力：此时切开会弹开。", "A high reading means this point is carrying a big load: cut now and it springs."],
	"cx_gauge_box_c": ["动手前读一遍，读数降下来再拆。", "Read it before you work; wait for it to come down."],
	"cx_gauge_box_x": ["应变片的电阻随拉伸变化，惠斯通电桥把它变成电压。承力件、拉杆、铰链上的载荷表告诉你哪里还“绷着”。", "A strain gauge's resistance changes as it stretches; a Wheatstone bridge turns that into a voltage. Load readings on members, tie rods and hinges tell you what's still under tension."],
	"cx_insp": ["现场仪表与传感器", "FIELD INSTRUMENTS"],
	"cx_insp_a": ["带显示窗的仪表、传感器节点、探测头。", "Instruments with display windows, sensor nodes, detector heads."],
	"cx_insp_b": ["本身危险不大，但常接在带压管路或带电回路上。", "Harmless themselves, but often on a pressurised line or a live circuit."],
	"cx_insp_c": ["读它的数，再按它所在的管路或电路处理。", "Read it, then deal with it as part of its line or circuit."],
	"cx_insp_x": ["仪表让你知道船现在的状态；它们的读数和面板记录不同，是实时的（只要你自己去读）。", "Instruments tell you the ship's state now; unlike a panel's records, their readings are live — as long as you read them yourself."],
	"cx_screw_comp": ["螺杆压缩机", "TWIN-SCREW COMPRESSOR"],
	"cx_screw_comp_a": ["一对阴阳转子、电机、油分离器和油冷却器。", "A pair of male and female rotors, motor, oil separator and oil cooler."],
	"cx_screw_comp_b": ["排气侧和油分里有压力和热油。", "Its discharge side and oil separator hold pressure and hot oil."],
	"cx_screw_comp_c": ["停机、泄压、排油，再拆。", "Stop it, relieve it, drain the oil, then remove it."],
	"cx_screw_comp_x": ["两根螺旋转子啮合，把吸进的气体沿轴向挤压到排气端。氦压缩机为低温系统提供高压氦气，氦很贵，要回收。", "Two meshing helical rotors squeeze the gas along to the discharge end. A helium compressor feeds a cryogenic plant; helium is dear and recovered."],
	"cx_axial_comp": ["轴流压缩机", "AXIAL COMPRESSOR"],
	"cx_axial_comp_a": ["一排排动叶和静叶交错，机匣向后收窄。", "Rows of rotor blades between rows of stator vanes in a casing that narrows aft."],
	"cx_axial_comp_b": ["转子可能还在惯性转动；进气口还连着工艺气。", "The rotor may still be coasting; its inlet is still on the process gas."],
	"cx_axial_comp_c": ["等转子停稳、进口隔离后再拆。", "Wait for the rotor to stop and isolate the inlet, then remove it."],
	"cx_axial_comp_x": ["每一级把气体压力提高约 1.2–1.4 倍。叶尖线速度可达每秒几百米，叶片断裂时像弹片一样飞出。", "Each stage raises the pressure about 1.2–1.4 times. Blade tips run at hundreds of metres a second; a broken blade leaves like shrapnel."],
	"cx_turboexpander": ["透平膨胀机", "TURBOEXPANDER"],
	"cx_turboexpander_a": ["膨胀透平和制动压缩机装在一根气体轴承轴上。", "An expansion turbine and a brake compressor on one shaft in gas bearings."],
	"cx_turboexpander_b": ["转速几万转；里面是极冷的工艺气。", "It runs at tens of thousands of rpm, full of very cold process gas."],
	"cx_turboexpander_c": ["停机、回温、泄压后再拆。", "Stop it, let it warm up, relieve it, then remove it."],
	"cx_turboexpander_x": ["气体膨胀对外做功，温度骤降——这是低温制冷和液化的核心。小型透平转速可超过 10 万 rpm。", "Gas expanding through it does work and its temperature drops sharply — the heart of cryogenic refrigeration and liquefaction. Small ones exceed 100,000 rpm."],
	"cx_turbo_pump": ["分子泵", "TURBOMOLECULAR PUMP"],
	"cx_turbo_pump_a": ["一叠转子和定子叶片，高速转动把气体分子打向出口。", "A stack of rotor and stator blades spinning fast to knock gas molecules to the outlet."],
	"cx_turbo_pump_b": ["转子每分钟几万转，突然进气会让它损毁。", "The rotor runs at tens of thousands of rpm; a sudden inrush of gas wrecks it."],
	"cx_turbo_pump_c": ["停机等它慢下来，再放气、拆法兰。", "Stop it, let it run down, then vent and unbolt it."],
	"cx_turbo_pump_x": ["分子泵叶尖速度接近气体分子的热运动速度，只能在高真空下工作，前级要有别的泵。完全停下要好几分钟。", "Its blade tips move about as fast as the gas molecules, so it only works in high vacuum, backed by another pump. It takes minutes to stop."],
	"cx_scroll_pump": ["涡旋泵", "SCROLL PUMP"],
	"cx_scroll_pump_a": ["一对互相嵌套的螺旋，一个固定一个公转。", "Two interleaved spirals, one fixed, one orbiting."],
	"cx_scroll_pump_b": ["它循环的可能是昂贵的 ³He 混合气。", "What it circulates may be costly ³He mixture."],
	"cx_scroll_pump_c": ["先回收它回路里的气，再停机拆。", "Recover the gas in its loop before stopping and removing it."],
	"cx_scroll_pump_x": ["涡旋泵无油，不会污染气体，所以用来循环稀释制冷机的 ³He/⁴He 混合气。", "Scroll pumps are oil-free and don't contaminate the gas, which is why they circulate a dilution refrigerator's ³He/⁴He mixture."],
	"cx_dry_cooler": ["干式冷却器", "DRY COOLER"],
	"cx_dry_cooler_a": ["V 形翅片盘管和一排风机：把冷却液的热散出去。", "Finned coils in a V under a row of fans: shedding the coolant's heat."],
	"cx_dry_cooler_b": ["盘管里满是冷却液。", "Its coils are full of coolant."],
	"cx_dry_cooler_c": ["排空回路再拆。", "Drain the loop before removing it."],
	"cx_dry_cooler_x": ["干冷器只靠空气散热，不蒸发水。真空里它没有空气可吹，只能当辐射面用——船上的“干冷器”其实大多是在有气的舱里。", "A dry cooler sheds heat to air with no water evaporated. In vacuum there's no air to blow, so aboard ship they sit in rooms that hold air."],
	"cx_cdu": ["冷却液分配单元", "COOLANT DISTRIBUTION UNIT"],
	"cx_cdu_a": ["板式换热器、两台泵、过滤器、膨胀罐和控制器。", "Plate heat exchanger, two pumps, filter, expansion vessel and controller."],
	"cx_cdu_b": ["它连着整排机柜的冷却液。", "It's connected to a whole row of racks' coolant."],
	"cx_cdu_c": ["排空它所在的回路，断电后再拆。", "Drain its loop and isolate it before removing it."],
	"cx_cdu_x": ["CDU 把机房的冷却水和机柜的二次冷却液隔开，一台可以服务几百千瓦的计算负载。", "A CDU keeps the facility water apart from the racks' secondary coolant; one can serve hundreds of kilowatts of computing."],
	# ---------------------------------------------------------------- devices: propulsion
	"cx_eng_core": ["液体火箭发动机", "LIQUID ROCKET ENGINE"],
	"cx_eng_core_a": ["涡轮泵、燃气发生器、喷注器和再生冷却燃烧室。", "Turbopump, gas generator, injector and a regeneratively cooled chamber."],
	"cx_eng_core_b": ["输送管和冷却夹套里还留着推进剂，有的有毒、有的自燃。", "Its feed lines and cooling jacket still hold propellant, some toxic, some self-igniting."],
	"cx_eng_core_c": ["关主阀，从排放口排空推进剂，再拆它的推力架。", "Close the main valves, drain the propellant at the drains, then unbolt its thrust frame."],
	"cx_eng_core_x": ["燃料先流过燃烧室壁里的冷却通道再进喷注器，所以停机后壁里还有一层推进剂。肼类推进剂有毒，与氧化剂接触即自燃。发动机是船上最重最值钱的设备之一，常要沿法兰分段。", "Fuel runs through the channels in the chamber wall before the injector, so a layer of it stays in the wall after shutdown. Hydrazines are toxic and ignite on contact with their oxidiser. Engines are among the heaviest and most valuable things aboard and often come apart at their flanges."],
	"cx_engine_s": ["挤压式小发动机", "PRESSURE-FED ENGINE"],
	"cx_engine_s_a": ["靠贮箱气压挤出推进剂的小发动机：阀门、喷注头、燃烧室和喷管。", "A small engine fed by tank pressure: valves, injector head, chamber and bell."],
	"cx_engine_s_b": ["贮箱还有压，阀一开推进剂就喷出来。", "With its tanks still pressurised, a valve opened sprays propellant."],
	"cx_engine_s_c": ["先泄掉贮箱的增压气，再拆发动机。", "Vent the tanks' pressurant before removing the engine."],
	"cx_engine_s_x": ["没有涡轮泵，结构简单可靠，但贮箱要做得耐高压。小飞船、着陆器、作业艇多用这种。", "No turbopump, simple and reliable, but its tanks must take high pressure. Small craft, landers and work tugs use them."],
	"cx_nozzle": ["喷管", "NOZZLE"],
	"cx_nozzle_a": ["钟形喷管：加强环、冷却管和喉部集管。", "A bell nozzle: stiffening rings, coolant tubes and the manifold at its throat."],
	"cx_nozzle_b": ["很大但很薄，撞一下就变形；冷却管里可能有残液。", "Big but thin, it dents at a knock; its coolant tubes may hold residue."],
	"cx_nozzle_c": ["排空冷却管，沿法兰拆，慢慢拖运。", "Drain the tubes, unbolt it at its flange, tow it slowly."],
	"cx_nozzle_x": ["喷管把燃气的热能变成速度：截面比越大，真空中的比冲越高。真空喷管的扩张比可达 100 以上，壁薄如纸。", "The nozzle turns the gas's heat into speed; the bigger its area ratio, the higher its specific impulse in vacuum. Vacuum bells reach area ratios over 100, with paper-thin walls."],
	"cx_rcs_quad": ["姿控推力器组", "RCS THRUSTER QUAD"],
	"cx_rcs_quad_a": ["一个安装块上四个小推力器，配加热片和电磁阀。", "Four small thrusters on one block, with heater pad and valves."],
	"cx_rcs_quad_b": ["阀门带电时一误动就喷火；管里有推进剂。", "Its valves, if live, can fire; its lines hold propellant."],
	"cx_rcs_quad_c": ["断电、关贮箱阀、排空管路后再拆。", "Isolate, shut the tank valves and drain the lines before removing it."],
	"cx_rcs_quad_x": ["单组元肼推力器靠催化床分解肼产生推力，几十牛到几百牛。加热片让催化床保持预热。", "Monopropellant thrusters decompose hydrazine on a catalyst bed for tens to hundreds of newtons; the heater keeps the bed warm."],
	"cx_turbopump": ["涡轮泵", "TURBOPUMP"],
	"cx_turbopump_a": ["燃料泵和氧化剂泵装在一根轴上，中间是涡轮。", "Fuel and oxidiser pumps on one shaft with the turbine between."],
	"cx_turbopump_b": ["两种推进剂在同一台机器里，泵壳里有残液。", "Two propellants in one machine, residue in both pump casings."],
	"cx_turbopump_c": ["两侧分别排空后再拆。", "Drain both sides separately, then remove it."],
	"cx_turbopump_x": ["涡轮泵功率密度极高：几十公斤的机器输出几兆瓦，转速每分钟几万转。轴封把燃料和氧化剂隔开，封坏了就是爆炸。", "A turbopump is power-dense: tens of kilograms putting out megawatts at tens of thousands of rpm. The shaft seals keep fuel and oxidiser apart; when they fail, it explodes."],
	"cx_apu": ["辅助动力装置", "AUXILIARY POWER UNIT"],
	"cx_apu_a": ["小型燃气轮机加齿轮箱和发电机。", "A small gas turbine with its gearbox and generator."],
	"cx_apu_b": ["燃料管里有油，发电机端可能带电。", "Fuel in its lines, and its generator may be live."],
	"cx_apu_c": ["关燃油、断电、排空后再拆。", "Fuel off, isolated, drained, then remove it."],
	"cx_apu_x": ["APU 在主发动机不工作时提供电力和气源，自己就是一台完整的小涡轮发动机。", "An APU provides power and air when the main engines don't run; it's a complete little turbine engine itself."],
	"cx_ntr_core": ["核热火箭堆芯", "NUCLEAR THERMAL ROCKET CORE"],
	"cx_ntr_core_a": ["六角燃料元件、铍反射层和控制鼓：用核裂变加热氢气推进。", "Hexagonal fuel elements, a beryllium reflector and control drums: fission heating hydrogen for thrust."],
	"cx_ntr_core_b": ["停堆后仍有强辐射和衰变热；切开包壳会污染全船。", "Shut down, it is still intensely radioactive and hot; break its cladding and the whole ship is contaminated."],
	"cx_ntr_core_c": ["在屏蔽阴影里工作，等它冷却，锁好控制鼓后整件吊走。", "Work in a shield's shadow, let it cool, lock the drums, lift it out whole."],
	"cx_ntr_core_x": ["核热火箭把氢气加热到 2,500 K 以上从喷管喷出，比冲约 900 s，是化学火箭的两倍。停堆后衰变热约为满功率的 1%，并随时间缓慢下降。", "It heats hydrogen past 2,500 K and expands it through the nozzle, for a specific impulse around 900 s — twice a chemical rocket's. After shutdown the decay heat is about 1 % of full power, falling slowly."],
	# ---------------------------------------------------------------- devices: computing, sensing
	"cx_nav_rack": ["设备机架", "EQUIPMENT RACK"],
	"cx_nav_rack_a": ["19 英寸机架：配线架、交换机、服务器和底部的 UPS。", "19-inch racks: patch panel, switch, servers and a UPS at the foot."],
	"cx_nav_rack_b": ["底部的 UPS 是一路独立电源：断了总线它照样带电。", "The UPS at its foot is a supply of its own: kill the bus and it's still live."],
	"cx_nav_rack_c": ["断开 UPS 的输出，再拔线拆机架。", "Switch the UPS output off, then unplug and remove the rack."],
	"cx_nav_rack_x": ["不间断电源平时充着电，主电一断立刻接管，能撑几分钟到几小时。数据设备价值高，整架拆下比拆散好卖。", "A UPS charges while the mains is on and takes over the moment it goes, for minutes or hours. Data hardware is valuable and sells better as a whole rack."],
	"cx_nav": ["航电单元", "AVIONICS UNIT"],
	"cx_nav_a": ["带显示屏、旋钮和底部接插件的机载电子盒。", "A flight electronics box with display, selectors and connectors along its foot."],
	"cx_nav_b": ["价值高、怕撞，接插件带电时拔会损坏。", "Valuable and fragile; pulled live, its connectors are damaged."],
	"cx_nav_c": ["断电后拔插头，轻拿轻放送设备口。", "Unplug once isolated, handle gently to the equipment bay."],
	"cx_nav_x": ["航电单元按 ARINC 等标准做成可整件更换的盒子，前面板两个把手，后面盲插。", "Avionics are built to standards like ARINC as whole replaceable boxes: two handles on the front, blind-mate connectors at the back."],
	"cx_console": ["操作台", "OPERATOR CONSOLE"],
	"cx_console_a": ["底座、桌面、倾斜的显示面板、键盘和操纵杆。", "Pedestal, desk, sloped display panel, keyboard and joystick."],
	"cx_console_b": ["显示的状态可能早已过期。", "What it shows may be long out of date."],
	"cx_console_c": ["别信它的屏幕，自己测；断电后整件拆下。", "Don't trust its screens, measure; isolate and remove it whole."],
	"cx_console_x": ["控制台是指令的入口，不是状态的真相：它显示的是传感器最后一次上报的值。", "A console is where commands go in, not where truth comes out: it shows what the sensors last reported."],
	"cx_blackbox": ["黑匣子（飞行记录仪）", "FLIGHT RECORDER"],
	"cx_blackbox_a": ["装甲存储筒、水下定位信标和接插件。", "An armoured memory drum, an underwater locator beacon and a connector."],
	"cx_blackbox_b": ["合同常要求完整送回；切到它就违约。", "Contracts usually want it back whole; cut it and you've broken the contract."],
	"cx_blackbox_c": ["拧下来整件送设备口。", "Unbolt it and take it whole to the equipment bay."],
	"cx_blackbox_x": ["抗坠毁存储器能承受 3,400 g 冲击和 1,100 °C 火烧一小时。它记录的是事故前最后的数据——船出过什么事，答案常在这里。", "A crash-survivable memory takes 3,400 g and an hour at 1,100 °C. It holds the last data before the accident: what happened to the ship is usually in there."],
	"cx_imu": ["惯性基准单元", "INERTIAL MEASUREMENT UNIT"],
	"cx_imu_a": ["三个正交的环形激光陀螺和加速度计，装在减振座上。", "Three ring-laser gyros on orthogonal faces and accelerometers, on isolators."],
	"cx_imu_b": ["精密而贵，撞一下就失准。", "Precise and dear; one knock and it's out of calibration."],
	"cx_imu_c": ["断电后整件慢慢运走。", "Isolate it and move it whole, slowly."],
	"cx_imu_x": ["环形激光陀螺测两束反向激光的频差（萨格纳克效应）来测转动，没有运动部件。", "A ring-laser gyro measures rotation from the frequency split between two counter-running beams (the Sagnac effect), with no moving parts."],
	"cx_star_tracker": ["星敏感器", "STAR TRACKER"],
	"cx_star_tracker_a": ["长遮光罩、光学头和电子箱：拍星空定姿态。", "A long sun baffle, optical head and electronics box: photographs the stars to know its attitude."],
	"cx_star_tracker_b": ["光学头怕污染和撞击。", "Its optics hate contamination and knocks."],
	"cx_star_tracker_c": ["远离它切割，整件拆下。", "Cut well away from it and remove it whole."],
	"cx_star_tracker_x": ["把拍到的星点图案和星表比对，姿态精度可达角秒级。遮光罩挡住太阳和亮天体的杂散光。", "It matches the star pattern it sees against a catalogue, to arc-second accuracy. The baffle keeps out stray light from the sun and bright bodies."],
	"cx_radar": ["抛物面天线", "DISH ANTENNA"],
	"cx_radar_a": ["反射面、馈源支架、副反射面和方位俯仰轴。", "Reflector, feed on its struts, subreflector, azimuth and elevation axes."],
	"cx_radar_b": ["反射面大而薄，一撞就变形；发射机可能带高压。", "The dish is big and thin and dents at a touch; its transmitter may hold high voltage."],
	"cx_radar_c": ["断开发射机，整件拆下，慢慢拖。", "Isolate the transmitter, remove it whole, tow it slowly."],
	"cx_radar_x": ["反射面的面形误差要小于波长的 1/16 才能聚焦，X 波段就是约 2 mm。变形的天线只值铝价。", "The surface has to be true to a sixteenth of the wavelength to focus — about 2 mm at X band. A dented dish is worth its aluminium."],
	"cx_xray_scanner": ["X 光扫描仪", "X-RAY SCANNER"],
	"cx_xray_scanner_a": ["射线发生器、探测器阵列、铅帘和传送带。", "X-ray generator, detector array, lead curtains and conveyor."],
	"cx_xray_scanner_b": ["发生器带高压，通电时有射线。", "The generator runs at high voltage and emits while powered."],
	"cx_xray_scanner_c": ["断电放电后再拆。", "Isolate and discharge it before removing it."],
	"cx_xray_scanner_x": ["X 光管用 100–300 kV 加速电子撞击靶材产生射线。断电即停止发射，但高压电源的电容要放电。", "The tube accelerates electrons at 100–300 kV into a target. It stops emitting when unpowered, but its high-voltage supply's capacitors need discharging."],
	"cx_biometric": ["生物识别终端", "BIOMETRIC PANEL"],
	"cx_biometric_a": ["掌纹仪、虹膜摄像头、键盘和门锁状态灯。", "Palm reader, iris camera, keypad and the door strike's lights."],
	"cx_biometric_b": ["它控制的门锁可能另有备用电源。", "The lock it controls may have a backup supply of its own."],
	"cx_biometric_c": ["查清门锁的每一路电源再处理门。", "Trace every supply of the lock before dealing with the door."],
	"cx_biometric_x": ["终端只是钥匙；锁本身靠电磁铁或电机，断电失效还是断电锁死（fail-secure），决定了门要怎么开。", "The panel is only a key; the lock is a solenoid or motor, and whether it fails open or fails secure decides how the door has to be opened."],
	# ---------------------------------------------------------------- devices: machinery
	"cx_hook": ["吊钩组", "HOOK BLOCK"],
	"cx_hook_a": ["夹板、滑轮、旋转接头和带安全扣的吊钩。", "Cheek plates, sheaves, a swivel and a hook with its safety latch."],
	"cx_hook_b": ["钢丝绳还绷着时拆它，绳子会抽回来。", "Free it with the rope still taut and the rope whips back."],
	"cx_hook_c": ["先松绞车刹车让绳放松，再拆。", "Slack the rope at the winch brake first, then remove it."],
	"cx_hook_x": ["多根绳穿过滑轮组可以省力（倍率），但每根绳里的张力都储存着弹性能。", "Reeving the rope over several sheaves multiplies the pull, but every fall of rope stores elastic energy."],
	"cx_reel": ["绞盘与卷筒", "WINCH AND REEL"],
	"cx_reel_a": ["卷筒、法兰、缠着的缆、轮毂和带式刹车。", "Drum, flanges, the cable wound on it, hub and band brake."],
	"cx_reel_b": ["缆还受力时拆轴，卷筒会甩出去。", "Take its shaft out with the cable under load and the drum flies."],
	"cx_reel_c": ["拔刹车销、看张力表归零，再拆轴。", "Pull the brake pins, watch the tension gauge reach zero, then the shaft."],
	"cx_reel_x": ["钢缆受拉储存弹性能 E = F²L/(2EA)：一根几十千牛的长缆存着足以抽坏设备的能量。张力表告诉你它是不是还绷着。", "A taut cable stores E = F²L/(2EA): a long wire at tens of kilonewtons holds enough to smash equipment. The tension gauge tells you whether it's still taut."],
	"cx_arm": ["机械臂", "MANIPULATOR ARM"],
	"cx_arm_a": ["底座转台、肩、大臂小臂和油缸、腕部与夹爪。", "Base and turntable, shoulder, upper and lower arm with their cylinders, wrist, gripper."],
	"cx_arm_b": ["折叠着的臂靠液压或预紧撑着，拆枢轴会弹开。", "Folded, it's held by hydraulics or preload; take a pivot out and it springs."],
	"cx_arm_c": ["泄掉它的蓄能器，拔每个关节的锁销，最后拆枢轴。", "Bleed its accumulator, pull each joint's pin, the pivots last."],
	"cx_arm_x": ["收折的机械臂像一把张开的折刀：每个关节里都可能存着力。正确的顺序总是先卸能，再卸锁，最后卸结构。", "A folded arm is a jack-knife held open: any joint may hold force. The order is always energy off, locks off, structure last."],
	"cx_dock": ["对接口", "DOCKING PORT"],
	"cx_dock_a": ["带螺栓圈的环形法兰、捕获锁、导向瓣和舱门。", "A ring flange on its bolt circle, capture latches, guide petals and the hatch."],
	"cx_dock_b": ["舱门后面可能是有压的舱。", "Behind the hatch may be a room still under pressure."],
	"cx_dock_c": ["先测后面的舱压，放气后再拆。", "Measure the room behind it and vent it first."],
	"cx_dock_x": ["对接口要同时承受结构载荷和气密：一圈几十颗螺栓加双道密封圈。导向瓣在对接时把两船对正。", "A docking port carries structural load and holds air: a ring of tens of bolts and a double seal. The petals line the two ships up as they meet."],
	"cx_brake": ["盘式制动器", "DISC BRAKE"],
	"cx_brake_a": ["跨在制动盘边上的卡钳、活塞、刹车片和油管。", "A caliper straddling the disc, with pistons, pads and hydraulic line."],
	"cx_brake_b": ["干刹会过热烧坏；它管着的东西可能还在转。", "Braked dry it overheats and burns out; what it holds may still be turning."],
	"cx_brake_c": ["先开制动冷却再刹；停稳后再拆。", "Turn the brake cooling on before braking; remove it once things have stopped."],
	"cx_brake_x": ["刹车把动能变成热：一个 20,000 rpm 的飞轮里存着的能量，要刹车片一点点磨成热。冷却不够，刹车片温度超过极限就失效，从此停不下来。", "A brake turns motion into heat: everything a flywheel at 20,000 rpm stores has to be ground into heat by the pads. Without cooling the pads pass their limit and fail, and then it can't be stopped."],
	"cx_lift": ["升降台", "SCISSOR LIFT"],
	"cx_lift_a": ["剪叉腿、平台和底座。", "Crossed legs, deck and base."],
	"cx_lift_b": ["升起时的液压缸保着压。", "Raised, its cylinder holds pressure."],
	"cx_lift_c": ["降到底、泄压后再拆。", "Lower it fully and relieve it before removing it."],
	"cx_lift_x": ["剪叉机构展开时力臂变短，油缸推力要很大，所以它降到底时最安全。", "As the scissors open the lever shortens and the cylinder pushes hard; fully lowered is where it's safe."],
	"cx_hold_crane": ["货舱吊车", "HOLD CRANE"],
	"cx_hold_crane_a": ["在桥轨上走的小车、卷扬电机和吊钩。", "A trolley on its bridge rail, hoist motor and hook."],
	"cx_hold_crane_b": ["吊着东西时拆它，吊的东西会掉；拉杆还紧着切它会抽坏它。", "Take it while it holds a load and the load drops; cut a tie rod still tight and it whips."],
	"cx_hold_crane_c": ["先放下吊物、松开拉杆，再拆。", "Set its load down and slack the tie rods first."],
	"cx_hold_crane_x": ["失重下吊车不是用来提重的，而是用来控制大件的位置和速度。", "In free fall a crane doesn't lift weight; it controls where big things go and how fast."],
	"cx_machine_tool": ["机床", "MACHINE TOOL"],
	"cx_machine_tool_a": ["车床或铣床：床身、主轴、刀架或工作台。", "A lathe or mill: bed, spindle, tool post or table."],
	"cx_machine_tool_b": ["很重，地脚螺栓多；电机带电。", "Heavy, many hold-down bolts, a live motor."],
	"cx_machine_tool_c": ["断电后拆地脚螺栓，超重就沿标线分段。", "Isolate it, undo its hold-downs, split it on its lines if too heavy."],
	"cx_machine_tool_x": ["机床的价值在精度：导轨磨损或撞弯就只剩铸铁的价。", "A machine tool's value is its accuracy: knock the ways out of true and it's worth its cast iron."],
	"cx_vehicle": ["车辆", "VEHICLE"],
	"cx_vehicle_a": ["绑在甲板上的汽车、叉车、牵引车或作业车。", "A car, forklift, tractor or work vehicle lashed to the deck."],
	"cx_vehicle_b": ["车里有电池或燃料，绑带松了会在舱里滑动撞坏东西。", "It carries a battery or fuel, and loose lashings let it slide into things."],
	"cx_vehicle_c": ["整车运走，或先处理电池燃料再拆。", "Take it whole, or deal with its battery and fuel before taking it apart."],
	"cx_vehicle_x": ["车辆是整件货物，价值远高于废金属；绑带和轮挡在失重下才是真正拉住它的东西。", "A vehicle is cargo, worth far more whole than as metal; in free fall the lashings and chocks are what really hold it."],
	"cx_cargo": ["货柜与货箱", "CONTAINERS AND CRATES"],
	"cx_cargo_a": ["标准集装箱或木框货箱，按货物申报计价。", "Standard containers or framed crates, paid by their declared cargo."],
	"cx_cargo_b": ["又大又重，拖动时惯性大；冷藏箱、住人箱里可能有压。", "Big and heavy, with momentum to match; reefers and accommodation boxes may hold pressure."],
	"cx_cargo_c": ["看质量，必要时用搬运无人机或升级抓钩；有压的先放气。", "Check its mass; use the hauler or a bigger grapple if needed; vent a pressurised one first."],
	"cx_cargo_x": ["集装箱四角的角件是唯一的承力点，扭锁把箱子锁在一起。整箱货物的价值远高于箱子本身。", "A container's corner castings are its only load points; twist-locks lock them together. What's inside is worth far more than the box."],
	"cx_uav": ["维护无人机", "MAINTENANCE DRONE"],
	"cx_uav_a": ["停在机位里的小型无人机：机体环、四个旋翼、传感器眼。", "A small drone parked in its bay: body ring, four rotor wells, sensor eye."],
	"cx_uav_b": ["自带电池：船断电了它还能“醒”过来乱飞。", "It carries its own battery: the ship dead, it can still wake up and fly."],
	"cx_uav_c": ["断机位充电和它自己的电池开关，摘电池包再搬。", "Switch off its charger and its own battery, take the pack out, then move it."],
	"cx_uav_x": ["无人机的飞控在掉电保护逻辑下会尝试起飞返航；被松开时如果电池还接着，旋翼一转就会把自己甩出去。", "A drone's flight controller tries to take off and return when its link drops; released with its battery still connected, its rotors spin up and throw it about."],
	"cx_stator": ["直线电机定子", "LINEAR MOTOR STATOR"],
	"cx_stator_a": ["叠片铁芯、槽里的线圈和两端翻出的端部绕组。", "Laminated core, coils in its slots, end turns curling out both ends."],
	"cx_stator_b": ["它的电来自电容组：断主电后仍可能带几百伏。", "It runs off a capacitor bank: off the main supply, it may still hold hundreds of volts."],
	"cx_stator_c": ["先给电容组放电，再拆线圈。", "Discharge the capacitor bank first, then the coils."],
	"cx_stator_x": ["直线电机是“展开”的旋转电机：定子沿轨道铺开，行波磁场推动动子。电磁弹射靠它在几秒内把载荷加速到几百米每秒。", "A linear motor is a rotary motor unrolled: the stator laid along the track, a travelling field pushing the mover. An electromagnetic launcher uses it to reach hundreds of metres a second in seconds."],
	"cx_launch_cradle": ["发射滑架", "LAUNCH CRADLE"],
	"cx_launch_cradle_a": ["在轨道上滑行的滑橇、托垫和释放锁。", "A sled on its rails, saddle pads and release latches."],
	"cx_launch_cradle_b": ["轨道还有预紧，释放锁一开它就会窜出。", "With the rails still preloaded, open the latches and it lurches off."],
	"cx_launch_cradle_c": ["轨道泄完预紧后再拆滑架。", "Take the preload off the rails before removing the cradle."],
	"cx_launch_cradle_x": ["滑架承受发射时几十 g 的加速度，结构厚重。", "The cradle takes tens of g at launch and is built heavy for it."],
	"cx_flywheel_rotor": ["飞轮储能器", "FLYWHEEL STORE"],
	"cx_flywheel_rotor_a": ["真空壳里的复合材料轮缘、磁悬浮轴承和电动/发电机。", "A composite rim in a vacuum housing on magnetic bearings, with a motor-generator."],
	"cx_flywheel_rotor_b": ["还在高速旋转：松开或切开，轮子甩出去。", "Still spinning fast: free or cut it and the wheel flies."],
	"cx_flywheel_rotor_c": ["开刹车冷却再上刹车，转速降到 300 rpm 以下再拆。", "Brake cooling on, then the brake; under 300 rpm, remove it."],
	"cx_flywheel_rotor_x": ["飞轮储能 E = ½Iω²，与转速的平方成正比：20,000 rpm 时储能是 2,000 rpm 的一百倍。真空和磁悬浮让它几乎没有摩擦，自己能转好几天。", "A flywheel holds E = ½Iω², the square of its speed: at 20,000 rpm a hundred times what it holds at 2,000. Vacuum and magnetic bearings leave it almost no friction; on its own it spins for days."],
	"cx_reaction_wheel": ["反作用飞轮", "REACTION WHEEL"],
	"cx_reaction_wheel_a": ["壳体里的飞轮、轮毂轴承和定子线圈：用来转动整艘船。", "A wheel on its hub bearings with stator coils in a housing: for turning the ship."],
	"cx_reaction_wheel_b": ["停用后也可能还在转。", "Even idle it may still be turning."],
	"cx_reaction_wheel_c": ["读转速，停稳后再拆。", "Read its speed and wait for it to stop."],
	"cx_reaction_wheel_x": ["电机让飞轮朝一个方向加速，船就朝反方向转（角动量守恒）。转速常在几千 rpm。", "Spin the wheel up one way and the ship turns the other (conservation of angular momentum). They run at thousands of rpm."],
	"cx_despin_brake": ["消旋制动器", "DESPIN BRAKE"],
	"cx_despin_brake_a": ["旋转居住环轮毂上的制动盘、卡钳和散热片。", "The disc, calipers and cooling fins on a habitat ring's hub."],
	"cx_despin_brake_b": ["环上负载带电时刹车，回馈电流会烧滑环；干刹会烧刹车。", "Brake with the ring's loads live and the regenerated current burns the slip ring; brake dry and the brake burns."],
	"cx_despin_brake_c": ["断环上负载、开冷却，两个环一起刹。", "Loads off the ring, cooling on, brake both rings together."],
	"cx_despin_brake_x": ["电机-制动器把环的动能转成电存进电容（再生制动），电容满了要放电才能继续刹。只刹一个环，船体会被另一个环的角动量拧扭。", "The motor-brake turns the ring's energy into charge in a capacitor (regenerative braking); full, it has to be dumped before braking goes on. Brake only one ring and the other's angular momentum twists the hull."],
	"cx_rotary_seal": ["旋转气密封", "ROTARY SEAL"],
	"cx_rotary_seal_a": ["转动的轮毂和固定主轴之间的迷宫密封。", "A labyrinth seal between the turning hub and the fixed spine."],
	"cx_rotary_seal_b": ["环还在转时打开过渡气闸，会撕开它。", "Open the transfer airlock while the ring turns and it tears."],
	"cx_rotary_seal_c": ["环停稳、轴承锁上后再动它。", "Only once the ring has stopped and its bearing is locked."],
	"cx_rotary_seal_x": ["迷宫密封靠一圈圈齿的节流减少泄漏，加缓冲气槽隔开两侧，本身不接触——所以它能在转动中密封，但挡不住真正的开口。", "A labyrinth seal throttles leakage through ring after ring of teeth with a buffer-gas groove between, without touching — sealing while it turns, but no use against a real opening."],
	"cx_spoke_lift": ["轮辐电梯", "SPOKE ELEVATOR"],
	"cx_spoke_lift_a": ["沿导轨齿条升降的轿厢：门、驱动电机和安全钳。", "A car on its rack and pinion: doors, drive motor, safety gear."],
	"cx_spoke_lift_b": ["环在转时轿厢受离心力，导轨一断它会甩出去。", "With the ring turning the car feels the spin; cut its rail and it's flung."],
	"cx_spoke_lift_c": ["环消旋后再拆。", "Only after the ring is despun."],
	"cx_spoke_lift_x": ["旋转环用离心力造“重力”：半径 100 m、3 rpm 时约 1 g。轿厢从轮毂走到环上，感受到的重力从零升到 1 g。", "A rotating ring makes gravity from its spin: about 1 g at 100 m radius and 3 rpm. The car's ride from hub to rim goes from nothing to a full g."],
	"cx_tether_damper": ["系绳阻尼器", "TETHER DAMPER"],
	"cx_tether_damper_a": ["液压缸、弹簧和气囊：吸收系绳的振动。", "A hydraulic cylinder, spring and gas reservoir: soaking up the tether's vibration."],
	"cx_tether_damper_b": ["系绳还绷着，阻尼器里压着弹簧和气压。", "With the tether taut, the damper holds spring and gas pressure."],
	"cx_tether_damper_c": ["系绳停转、张紧器松开之后再拆。", "Once the tether has stopped and its tensioner is slack."],
	"cx_tether_damper_x": ["长系绳会像琴弦一样振动，阻尼器把振动能量变成热。", "A long tether rings like a string; the damper turns that motion into heat."],
	"cx_hyd_clamp": ["液压夹钳", "HYDRAULIC CLAMP"],
	"cx_hyd_clamp_a": ["固定钳口、液压缸推动的活动钳口和底板。", "A fixed jaw, a moving jaw pushed by its cylinder, and the base plate."],
	"cx_hyd_clamp_b": ["保着压整件拆下，钳口会弹开砸坏东西。", "Removed while it holds pressure, its jaw springs open."],
	"cx_hyd_clamp_c": ["先开它的保压开关泄压，再拆。", "Release its holding switch to bleed it, then remove it."],
	"cx_hyd_clamp_x": ["夹钳靠液压锁保持夹紧力，即使泵停了也能保压很久。一组夹钳共同承担载荷时，松开的顺序决定剩下的夹钳受力。", "A clamp's lock valve holds its grip long after the pump stops. When several share a load, the order they're released in decides what the rest must carry."],
	"cx_iso_table": ["隔振台", "VIBRATION ISOLATION TABLE"],
	"cx_iso_table_a": ["蜂窝台面、气动隔振腿和水平阀。", "A honeycomb top on pneumatic legs with levelling valves."],
	"cx_iso_table_b": ["没锁时，附近的切割和撞击会通过它震坏精密件。", "Unlocked, a cut or knock nearby shakes the precision parts on it."],
	"cx_iso_table_c": ["先锁住隔振台，再在附近动刀。", "Lock the table before any cutting nearby."],
	"cx_iso_table_x": ["隔振台把几赫兹以上的振动衰减到百分之一以下；锁住后它就成了刚性的，不再放大冲击。", "It cuts vibration above a few hertz to under a hundredth; locked, it's rigid and stops amplifying shocks."],
	"cx_escape_pod": ["救生舱", "ESCAPE POD"],
	"cx_escape_pod_a": ["发射架上的救生舱：防热罩、侧舱门、座椅、制动火箭和发射夹。", "A pod in its cradle: heat shield, hatch, seats, retro pack and launch clamps."],
	"cx_escape_pod_b": ["发射夹上装着火工品，待发电路带电就可能走火弹出。", "Its clamps carry pyrotechnics; with the arming circuit live, they can fire and throw it."],
	"cx_escape_pod_c": ["断开待发开关，再拆发射夹和火工品。", "Disarm it at the pod control panel before touching the clamps or charges."],
	"cx_escape_pod_x": ["爆炸螺栓里装着少量炸药，起爆电流只需几安培、几毫秒。发射电容是一路独立电源，专门为它供电。", "An explosive bolt holds a little charge; it needs a few amps for a few milliseconds to fire. The launch capacitor is a supply of its own, there for that alone."],
	"cx_safe_deposit": ["保管箱墙与库门", "VAULT AND DEPOSIT BOXES"],
	"cx_safe_deposit_a": ["一墙密封保管箱，或带锁栓的厚壁库门。", "A wall of sealed deposit boxes, or a thick vault door with locking bolts."],
	"cx_safe_deposit_b": ["库门带电锁死；库里可能有压。", "The vault door locks while powered; the vault may hold pressure."],
	"cx_safe_deposit_c": ["断开门锁的所有电源，放气后开门，保管箱整件运走。", "Kill every supply of the lock, vent the vault, open it, take the boxes whole."],
	"cx_safe_deposit_x": ["库门的锁栓由电磁铁顶住：通电时锁死，断电后锁栓仍在原位，要扳动机械释放杆才收回。只要电磁铁还有任何一路电，释放杆就扳不动。", "The vault's bolts are held by a solenoid: powered, locked; unpowered, the bolts stay where they are until a mechanical release lever draws them. While the solenoid has any supply at all, the lever won't move."],
	# ---------------------------------------------------------------- devices: nuclear
	"cx_pwr_core": ["压水堆", "PRESSURISED-WATER REACTOR"],
	"cx_pwr_core_a": ["压力容器、顶盖螺栓环、控制棒驱动管、堆芯和下腔室。", "Vessel, closure head on its stud ring, rod drive housings, core and lower plenum."],
	"cx_pwr_core_b": ["停堆后仍有强辐射和衰变热，一回路高温高压。", "Shut down it is still radioactive and hot, its primary loop at high temperature and pressure."],
	"cx_pwr_core_c": ["保持冷却、等它降温，屏蔽下作业，整件走危险品口。", "Keep it cooled, let it come down, work behind shielding, send it whole to the hazard mouth."],
	"cx_pwr_core_x": ["一回路约 15.5 MPa、315 °C，水在高压下不沸腾。停堆一小时后衰变热约为额定功率的 1.5%，一天后约 0.5%——一座 100 MW 的堆一天后仍在发 0.5 MW 的热。", "The primary runs about 15.5 MPa and 315 °C, water held liquid by pressure. An hour after shutdown the decay heat is about 1.5 % of rated power, after a day about 0.5 % — a 100 MW reactor still putting out half a megawatt."],
	"cx_crdm": ["控制棒驱动机构", "CONTROL ROD DRIVE"],
	"cx_crdm_a": ["耐压外壳、提升与保持线圈、棒位指示和驱动杆。", "Pressure housing, lift and hold coils, rod position indicator and drive rod."],
	"cx_crdm_b": ["它是一回路压力边界的一部分。", "It's part of the primary pressure boundary."],
	"cx_crdm_c": ["一回路泄压、冷却后再拆。", "Only with the primary depressurised and cool."],
	"cx_crdm_x": ["磁力提升式驱动机构断电时，控制棒靠自身释放落入堆芯（失电安全）。", "With a magnetic-jack drive, losing power drops the rods into the core by themselves (fail-safe)."],
	"cx_rcp": ["主冷却剂泵", "REACTOR COOLANT PUMP"],
	"cx_rcp_a": ["屏蔽电机、飞轮、密封组件和泵壳。", "Canned motor, flywheel, seal package and casing."],
	"cx_rcp_b": ["它是冷却堆芯的唯一手段：先断它，堆芯就开始升温。", "It's what cools the core: cut it first and the core heats up."],
	"cx_rcp_c": ["堆芯冷下来之前别断它的电。", "Leave its power on until the core is cool."],
	"cx_rcp_x": ["泵上的飞轮让断电后的冷却流量缓慢下降，给堆芯多几十秒的冷却。", "Its flywheel makes the flow coast down slowly after a power loss, buying the core tens of seconds of cooling."],
	"cx_pressurizer": ["稳压器", "PRESSURISER"],
	"cx_pressurizer_a": ["高大的容器，上部蒸汽空间、喷淋头、电加热器和安全阀。", "A tall vessel: steam space above the water, spray head, heaters, relief valves."],
	"cx_pressurizer_b": ["它维持一回路的压力：里面是高压饱和水和蒸汽。", "It holds the primary's pressure: saturated water and steam at high pressure."],
	"cx_pressurizer_c": ["一回路泄压冷却后再拆。", "Only after the primary is relieved and cool."],
	"cx_pressurizer_x": ["加热器烧出蒸汽升压，喷淋冷水降压。15.5 MPa 下水的饱和温度约 345 °C。", "Heaters raise the pressure by boiling, cold spray lowers it. At 15.5 MPa water saturates at about 345 °C."],
	"cx_steam_turbine": ["汽轮机", "STEAM TURBINE"],
	"cx_steam_turbine_a": ["高压缸和低压缸同轴，叶片一级比一级长。", "High- and low-pressure cylinders on one shaft, blades growing longer stage by stage."],
	"cx_steam_turbine_b": ["极重，转子可能还在盘车。", "Very heavy, and its rotor may still be turning on its gear."],
	"cx_steam_turbine_c": ["停稳、隔离蒸汽后，沿法兰分段拆。", "Stopped and isolated from steam, it comes apart at its flanges."],
	"cx_steam_turbine_x": ["蒸汽每经过一级膨胀一点、体积变大，所以后面的叶片更长。整机常重几十吨。", "The steam expands a little at every stage and takes more room, so the blades lengthen. A whole set weighs tens of tonnes."],
	"cx_condenser": ["凝汽器", "CONDENSER"],
	"cx_condenser_a": ["壳体、管束、水室和热井：把乏汽凝成水。", "Shell, tube bundle, waterboxes and hotwell: exhaust steam back to water."],
	"cx_condenser_b": ["管束里有冷却水，热井里有凝结水。", "Cooling water in its tubes, condensate in its hotwell."],
	"cx_condenser_c": ["两侧排空后再拆。", "Drain both sides before removing it."],
	"cx_condenser_x": ["凝汽器在真空下工作：蒸汽凝结体积缩小上千倍，自己就把壳内抽成低压。", "It works in vacuum: condensing, the steam shrinks a thousandfold and pulls the shell down to low pressure by itself."],
	"cx_control_drum": ["控制鼓", "CONTROL DRUM"],
	"cx_control_drum_a": ["一面贴着碳化硼吸收体的铍鼓，由电机转动。", "A beryllium drum faced on one side with boron carbide, turned by a motor."],
	"cx_control_drum_b": ["没锁就吊堆芯，鼓会滑转，吸收体转开，附近一阵剂量。", "Lift the core with it unlocked and it slips, the absorber turns away, and a burst of dose goes out."],
	"cx_control_drum_c": ["吊堆芯前把每个控制鼓机械锁死。", "Lock every drum mechanically before the core is lifted."],
	"cx_control_drum_x": ["鼓转到吸收体朝向堆芯，吸收中子、压低反应性；转到铍面朝内，反射中子、提高反应性。", "Turned absorber-in, it soaks up neutrons and holds the reactor down; beryllium-in, it reflects them back and raises it."],
	"cx_shadow_shield": ["阴影屏蔽板", "SHADOW SHIELD"],
	"cx_shadow_shield_a": ["钨和氢化锂交替叠层的屏蔽板，挡住堆芯的直射辐射。", "Layers of tungsten and lithium hydride stacked across the core's line of sight."],
	"cx_shadow_shield_b": ["它后面才是安全区；把它拆走前，先想好你在哪里干活。", "Only behind it is safe; before moving it, know where you'll work."],
	"cx_shadow_shield_c": ["吊着它挡在堆芯前，在它的阴影里作业。", "Hang it in front of the core and work in its shadow."],
	"cx_shadow_shield_x": ["钨挡伽马射线，氢化锂慢化并吸收中子。阴影里的剂量率只剩约 1%。航天堆不做全包屏蔽，只屏蔽乘员方向以省质量。", "Tungsten stops gamma, lithium hydride slows and absorbs neutrons. In its shadow the dose rate falls to about 1 %. Space reactors shield only towards the crew to save mass."],
	# ---------------------------------------------------------------- devices: fusion
	"cx_tf_coil": ["超导纵场线圈", "SUPERCONDUCTING TF COIL"],
	"cx_tf_coil_a": ["钢壳里的铠装导体绕组，每匝中心通液氦。", "A winding pack of cable-in-conduit turns in a steel case, liquid helium through each turn."],
	"cx_tf_coil_b": ["带着几十亿焦的磁能：失冷或切支撑会失超，能量瞬间释放。", "It holds gigajoules of field: lose its cooling or cut its supports and it quenches, all at once."],
	"cx_tf_coil_c": ["开泄能开关、保持制冷，储能泄完再拆。", "Close the dump switch, keep it cold, take it out only once it's run down."],
	"cx_tf_coil_x": ["Nb₃Sn 超导体在约 18 K 以下无电阻，平时用 4.5 K 液氦冷着。失超时局部变成有电阻的导体，电流 × 电阻 = 热，热又让更多导体失超——几秒内整个线圈的储能变成热和力。", "Nb₃Sn has no resistance below about 18 K and is kept at 4.5 K in liquid helium. In a quench a patch turns resistive, current times resistance makes heat, the heat takes more conductor normal — and in seconds the coil's whole store becomes heat and force."],
	"cx_cs_stack": ["中心螺线管", "CENTRAL SOLENOID"],
	"cx_cs_stack_a": ["饼式绕组叠在拉紧板之间，中间是孔，上下预压法兰。", "Pancake windings stacked between tie plates, the bore down its middle, pre-compression flanges."],
	"cx_cs_stack_b": ["和纵场线圈一样储着磁能，会失超。", "Like the TF coils it stores field energy and can quench."],
	"cx_cs_stack_c": ["泄能完成后再拆预压结构。", "Remove its pre-compression only after it's dumped."],
	"cx_cs_stack_x": ["中心螺线管靠变化的磁通在等离子体里感应出电流（变压器原理），它自己承受巨大的电磁力，要预压住。", "The central solenoid drives current in the plasma by changing its flux, like a transformer; it carries huge electromagnetic forces and is held under pre-compression."],
	"cx_grav_support": ["线圈支撑", "COIL SUPPORT"],
	"cx_grav_support_a": ["两个端块之间一叠薄柔性板：让线圈冷缩时不拉坏底座。", "A stack of thin flexible plates between two blocks: lets the coil shrink as it cools."],
	"cx_grav_support_b": ["线圈带场时切或拆它，线圈失超。", "Cut or free it while the coil is energised and the coil quenches."],
	"cx_grav_support_c": ["线圈泄完能再拆。", "Only after the coil is dumped."],
	"cx_grav_support_x": ["从室温冷到 4 K，几米长的钢结构会缩短几毫米；柔性板在一个方向软、另一个方向硬，吸收收缩又能承重。", "From room temperature to 4 K a few metres of steel shrinks by millimetres; the plates are soft one way and stiff the other, taking up the shrinkage and still carrying the load."],
	"cx_vv_wall": ["真空室壁", "VACUUM VESSEL WALL"],
	"cx_vv_wall_a": ["内外两层壳之间夹着加强肋，夹层里流屏蔽水。", "Inner and outer shells with ribs between; shielding water runs in the gap."],
	"cx_vv_wall_b": ["夹层里可能还有水；内壁被中子活化。", "The gap may still hold water; the inner shell is activated by neutrons."],
	"cx_vv_wall_c": ["排空夹层，按标线分段。", "Drain the gap and cut it on its marked lines."],
	"cx_vv_wall_x": ["真空室是等离子体的第一道包络，也是氚的屏障。聚变中子会把结构钢活化，退役后要按低放废物处理。", "The vacuum vessel is the plasma's first enclosure and a tritium barrier. Fusion neutrons activate its steel; retired, it's low-level waste."],
	"cx_blanket": ["包层模块", "BLANKET MODULE"],
	"cx_blanket_a": ["贴在真空室内壁上的模块：面向等离子体的第一壁和后面的屏蔽块。", "Modules lining the vessel: a plasma-facing first wall and a shield block behind."],
	"cx_blanket_b": ["铍瓦面怕撞；冷却管里有水。", "Its beryllium face hates knocks; its pipes hold water."],
	"cx_blanket_c": ["排空冷却管，拆螺栓整块取出。", "Drain its pipes, unbolt it and lift it out whole."],
	"cx_blanket_x": ["第一壁表面承受每平方米几兆瓦的热流。铍粉有毒，切割会产生铍尘。", "The first wall takes megawatts per square metre. Beryllium dust is toxic, and cutting it makes some."],
	"cx_divertor": ["偏滤器", "DIVERTOR"],
	"cx_divertor_a": ["钢体上竖着钨单块的内外靶板，中间是穹顶，带冷却管。", "A steel cassette with tungsten monoblock targets at each end, a dome between, and coolant pipes."],
	"cx_divertor_b": ["很重，冷却管里有高压水。", "Heavy, with high-pressure water in its pipes."],
	"cx_divertor_c": ["排空冷却管后整盒拆下。", "Drain it and take the cassette out whole."],
	"cx_divertor_x": ["偏滤器把等离子体边缘的热和杂质引到靶板上，靶板热流可达每平方米 10–20 MW，接近火箭喉部。", "It leads the plasma edge's heat and impurities onto its targets, which take 10–20 MW per square metre — rocket-throat territory."],
	"cx_gyrotron": ["回旋管", "GYROTRON"],
	"cx_gyrotron_a": ["电子枪、超导磁体里的谐振腔、输出窗和顶部收集极。", "Electron gun, cavity inside a superconducting magnet, output window, collector on top."],
	"cx_gyrotron_b": ["自带超导磁体；电子枪和收集极带几十千伏高压。", "It has its own superconducting magnet; its gun and collector run at tens of kilovolts."],
	"cx_gyrotron_c": ["高压放电、磁体泄能后整件拆下。", "Discharge its high voltage and dump its magnet, then remove it whole."],
	"cx_gyrotron_x": ["电子在强磁场里回旋，把能量交给毫米波：一支回旋管输出约 1 MW、170 GHz 的微波。输出窗是一片人造金刚石。", "Electrons gyrating in a strong field hand their energy to millimetre waves: one tube puts out about 1 MW at 170 GHz. Its output window is a disc of synthetic diamond."],
	"cx_ech": ["电子回旋加热天线", "EC LAUNCHER"],
	"cx_ech_a": ["波纹波导束、固定聚焦镜和可转向的反射镜。", "A bundle of corrugated waveguides, a fixed focusing mirror and a steering mirror."],
	"cx_ech_b": ["反射镜精密易损；波导里可能有绝缘气体。", "Its mirrors are precise and fragile; its waveguides may hold insulating gas."],
	"cx_ech_c": ["远离它切割，整件拆下。", "Cut well away and remove it whole."],
	"cx_ech_x": ["转向镜把微波束打到等离子体里特定的磁面上，加热或驱动电流。", "The steering mirror aims the beam onto a chosen magnetic surface in the plasma, to heat it or drive current."],
	"cx_nbi": ["中性束注入器", "NEUTRAL BEAM INJECTOR"],
	"cx_nbi_a": ["离子源、加速栅极、中和室、偏转磁铁和低温泵。", "Ion source, accelerator grids, neutraliser, bending magnet and cryopumps."],
	"cx_nbi_b": ["栅极带近百万伏高压，低温泵里冷凝着氢。", "Its grids run near a megavolt; its cryopumps hold condensed hydrogen."],
	"cx_nbi_c": ["高压放电、低温泵回温泄气后再拆。", "Discharge it and let the cryopumps warm and vent before removing it."],
	"cx_nbi_x": ["把氘离子加速到上百 keV，再中和成不受磁场约束的中性原子，射进等离子体加热。低温泵一回温，冷凝在上面的氢会全部变回气体。", "Deuterium ions accelerated to hundreds of keV, neutralised so the field doesn't stop them, fired into the plasma. Warm the cryopumps and all the hydrogen frozen on them turns back to gas."],
	"cx_pellet": ["弹丸注入器", "PELLET INJECTOR"],
	"cx_pellet_a": ["在冷头下冻结氘冰的螺杆挤出机、切刀和气枪管。", "A screw extruder freezing deuterium ice under a cold head, a cutter and a gas gun."],
	"cx_pellet_b": ["里面是冻着的氘，回温就变成可燃气体。", "It holds frozen deuterium that turns into flammable gas as it warms."],
	"cx_pellet_c": ["回温泄气后再拆。", "Let it warm and vent before removing it."],
	"cx_pellet_x": ["毫米级的冰弹丸以每秒几百米射进等离子体，从里面补充燃料。", "Millimetre ice pellets fired in at hundreds of metres a second fuel the plasma from inside."],
	"cx_port_plug": ["窗口插件", "PORT PLUG"],
	"cx_port_plug_a": ["填满窗口的屏蔽块，里面有让光线穿过的反射镜迷宫。", "A shielding block filling a port, with a mirror labyrinth for the light to thread."],
	"cx_port_plug_b": ["极重，正面被活化。", "Very heavy, its face activated."],
	"cx_port_plug_c": ["按标线分段吊出。", "Cut on its lines and lift it out in sections."],
	"cx_port_plug_x": ["迷宫让诊断光路拐几次弯，中子沿直线走不出来。", "The labyrinth bends the diagnostic light path several times; neutrons, going straight, can't follow."],
	"cx_coldbox": ["制冷机冷箱（氦）", "CRYOPLANT COLD BOX"],
	"cx_coldbox_a": ["真空容器里的板翅式换热器和透平膨胀机：生产 4.5 K 液氦。", "Plate-fin exchangers and turboexpanders in a vacuum vessel: making 4.5 K helium."],
	"cx_coldbox_b": ["它停了，超导线圈就开始升温。", "Stop it and the superconducting coils start to warm."],
	"cx_coldbox_c": ["磁体泄完能之前保持它运行（要有电）。", "Keep it running (it needs power) until the magnets are dumped."],
	"cx_coldbox_x": ["从室温到 4.5 K 要经过几级换热和膨胀，每取走 1 W 的 4 K 热量，要在室温端花几百瓦电。", "Room temperature to 4.5 K takes several stages of exchange and expansion; every watt taken out at 4 K costs hundreds of watts at room temperature."],
	"cx_cold_box_h2": ["氢冷箱", "HYDROGEN COLD BOX"],
	"cx_cold_box_h2_a": ["真空夹套里一串板翅式换热器、透平和节流阀：液化氢气。", "Plate-fin exchangers, turbines and a Joule-Thomson valve in a vacuum jacket: liquefying hydrogen."],
	"cx_cold_box_h2_b": ["它一停，低温罐就开始升压。", "Stop it and the cryogenic tanks start to climb."],
	"cx_cold_box_h2_c": ["抽液期间保持它运行，最后再断电。", "Keep it running while you draw the cargo off; cut its power last."],
	"cx_cold_box_h2_x": ["氢在 −253 °C 液化。冷箱同时负责把罐里蒸发的气体重新液化，所以它就是罐压的“刹车”。", "Hydrogen liquefies at −253 °C. The cold box also reliquefies what boils off the tanks — it's the brake on their pressure."],
	# ---------------------------------------------------------------- devices: cryogenic physics
	"cx_dr_stage": ["稀释制冷机冷板", "DILUTION FRIDGE STAGE"],
	"cx_dr_stage_a": ["镀金铜板一级级吊着：50 K、4 K、蒸馏室、冷板、混合室。", "Gold-plated copper plates hung one below the other: 50 K, 4 K, still, cold plate, mixing chamber."],
	"cx_dr_stage_b": ["混合室还在毫开时动它，下面的芯片会裂。", "Touch the stack while the mixing chamber is still at millikelvin and the chip cracks."],
	"cx_dr_stage_c": ["按顺序回温，全部回到室温附近再拆。", "Warm it up in order and take it apart only near room temperature."],
	"cx_dr_stage_x": ["³He 从富 ⁴He 相“溶解”到稀相要吸热，这就是混合室能降到 10 mK 的原因。冷板之间用细同轴线和低导热支撑隔开，一层比一层冷。", "³He dissolving from the concentrated phase into the dilute one takes heat in — how the mixing chamber reaches 10 mK. The plates are joined only by thin coax and low-conductance supports, each colder than the last."],
	"cx_qpu": ["量子处理器封装", "QUANTUM PROCESSOR PACKAGE"],
	"cx_qpu_a": ["铜样品盒里的超导量子芯片，边缘一排 SMA 接头。", "A superconducting qubit chip in its copper sample box, SMA connectors round its edge."],
	"cx_qpu_b": ["极冷时极脆：热冲击、振动、碰撞都会让它开裂。", "At base temperature it's brittle: thermal shock, vibration or a knock cracks it."],
	"cx_qpu_c": ["等它按序回温、锁住隔振台，再取。", "Wait for an ordered warm-up and lock the isolation table before taking it."],
	"cx_qpu_x": ["超导量子比特工作在约 10 mK，任何热、振动、杂散光都会破坏量子态。芯片本身是全船最贵的单件之一。", "Superconducting qubits work at about 10 mK, where any heat, vibration or stray light destroys their state. The chip is among the dearest single items aboard."],
	"cx_pulse_tube": ["脉管制冷机冷头", "PULSE-TUBE COLD HEAD"],
	"cx_pulse_tube_a": ["旋转阀、回热器、脉管和两级冷台：把系统预冷到 4 K。", "Rotary valve, regenerators, pulse tubes and two stages: pre-cooling the system to 4 K."],
	"cx_pulse_tube_b": ["它一停，整台稀释制冷机开始回温。", "Stop it and the whole dilution fridge starts warming."],
	"cx_pulse_tube_c": ["混合气回收完之后再停它。", "Stop it only after the mixture is recovered."],
	"cx_pulse_tube_x": ["脉管制冷机冷端没有运动部件，振动小，所以适合量子计算。压缩机通过柔性氦管供气。", "A pulse tube has no moving parts at its cold end and so little vibration — why quantum computers use it. Its compressor feeds it through flexible helium lines."],
	"cx_ghs": ["气体处理系统", "GAS HANDLING SYSTEM"],
	"cx_ghs_a": ["³He/⁴He 回路的模拟面板、压力表、冷阱和泵。", "The ³He/⁴He circuit's mimic panel, gauges, cold trap and pumps."],
	"cx_ghs_b": ["回路里是极贵的 ³He；没回收就停机，它会沸掉。", "The circuit holds very costly ³He; stop the fridge before recovering it and it boils off."],
	"cx_ghs_c": ["停循环、把混合气收回储罐，再停冷头。", "Stop the circulation, recover the mixture to its tank, then stop the cold head."],
	"cx_ghs_x": ["一台稀释制冷机约用几十升（标准状态）³He，每升价格数千美元。混合气收回储罐后压力会升到储罐的平衡值。", "A dilution fridge uses some tens of standard litres of ³He at thousands of dollars a litre. Recovered, the mixture settles at its storage tank's pressure."],
	"cx_instrument_rack": ["室温测控机柜", "ROOM-TEMPERATURE ELECTRONICS"],
	"cx_instrument_rack_a": ["任意波形发生器、数字化仪，一排 SMA 输出。", "Arbitrary waveform generators and digitisers, rows of SMA outputs."],
	"cx_instrument_rack_b": ["价值高、怕撞；接着进制冷机的同轴线。", "Valuable and fragile; coax runs from it into the fridge."],
	"cx_instrument_rack_c": ["断电拔线，整柜送设备口。", "Isolate, unplug, send it whole to the equipment bay."],
	"cx_instrument_rack_x": ["每个量子比特要几路微波控制和读出线，几十个比特就是几百根同轴线。", "Each qubit needs several microwave lines for control and readout; tens of qubits mean hundreds of coax runs."],
	# ---------------------------------------------------------------- devices: optics and instruments
	"cx_mirror": ["镜片（主镜 / 副镜）", "MIRROR SEGMENT"],
	"cx_mirror_a": ["镀膜镜面和背后的轻量化肋板坯体。", "A coated face on a ribbed, lightweighted blank."],
	"cx_mirror_b": ["附近切割的金属粉尘会污染镜面；促动器没锁就拆会掉落碎裂。", "Cutting nearby dusts its face; freed with its actuators unlocked, it drops and cracks."],
	"cx_mirror_c": ["先放防尘罩、锁促动器，从外圈往里拆。", "Run the dust cover down, lock the actuators, take the rings from the outside in."],
	"cx_mirror_x": ["望远镜镜面的面形精度在几十纳米，镀膜只有约 100 nm 厚（铝或金）。一粒金属粉尘就是一个散射点。每块镜片由三到六个促动器支撑，外圈镜片的边缘搭在内圈上。", "A telescope mirror is true to tens of nanometres; its coating is about 100 nm of aluminium or gold. A grain of metal dust is a scattering spot. Each segment sits on three to six actuators, and the outer ring's edges rest on the inner."],
	"cx_hexapod": ["六足调整机构", "HEXAPOD"],
	"cx_hexapod_a": ["上下平台之间六根交叉的直线作动器：六个自由度调姿。", "Six crossing linear actuators between two plates: positioning in six degrees of freedom."],
	"cx_hexapod_b": ["它托着副镜；拆它之前副镜要先固定。", "It carries the secondary mirror; secure the mirror before you touch it."],
	"cx_hexapod_c": ["锁住负载，断电后整件拆下。", "Lock its load, isolate it, remove it whole."],
	"cx_hexapod_x": ["Stewart 平台：六根杆的长度组合唯一决定上平台的位置和姿态，定位精度可达微米。", "A Stewart platform: the six legs' lengths fix the top plate's position and attitude, to micrometres."],
	"cx_aft_optics": ["后光学平台", "AFT OPTICS BENCH"],
	"cx_aft_optics_a": ["三镜、折转镜和精密指向镜排在光学平台上，光路通向仪器。", "Tertiary, fold and steering mirrors on a bench, the beam threading them to the instruments."],
	"cx_aft_optics_b": ["整个平台的对准精度极高，撞一下全部失准。", "The whole bench is aligned to fine tolerances; one knock and it's all out."],
	"cx_aft_optics_c": ["远离切割，整台慢慢运走。", "No cutting nearby; move the whole bench, slowly."],
	"cx_aft_optics_x": ["平台用低膨胀材料（碳化硅、殷钢）做成，温度变化也不让光路偏移。", "The bench is low-expansion material (silicon carbide, Invar) so temperature doesn't shift the beam."],
	"cx_fsm": ["精密指向镜", "FAST STEERING MIRROR"],
	"cx_fsm_a": ["柔性铰链上的小镜子，背后三根压电堆。", "A small mirror on a flexure with three piezo stacks behind it."],
	"cx_fsm_b": ["压电堆带高压；镜面怕污染。", "Its piezo stacks carry high voltage; its face hates dust."],
	"cx_fsm_c": ["断电后整件拆下。", "Isolate it and remove it whole."],
	"cx_fsm_x": ["每秒上千次修正指向，抵消船体抖动；行程只有几毫弧度。", "It corrects the pointing thousands of times a second against the ship's jitter, over a few milliradians."],
	"cx_fgs": ["精密导星仪", "FINE GUIDANCE SENSOR"],
	"cx_fgs_a": ["取光镜、中继光学和两个导星探测器。", "Pick-off mirror, relay optics and two guide detectors."],
	"cx_fgs_b": ["精密光学，怕撞怕尘。", "Precision optics; hates knocks and dust."],
	"cx_fgs_c": ["远离切割，整件拆下。", "Cut away from it, remove it whole."],
	"cx_fgs_x": ["盯住一颗导星，把望远镜的指向稳定在毫角秒级。", "It locks onto a guide star and holds the telescope's pointing to milliarcseconds."],
	"cx_wfs": ["波前传感器", "WAVEFRONT SENSOR"],
	"cx_wfs_a": ["微透镜阵列把光分成点阵，相机测每个点的偏移。", "A lenslet array splits the light into spots; a camera measures how each one moves."],
	"cx_wfs_b": ["精密光学与相机，怕撞。", "Precision optics and a camera; fragile."],
	"cx_wfs_c": ["断电后整件运走。", "Isolate and move it whole."],
	"cx_wfs_x": ["夏克-哈特曼传感器：点的偏移就是波前的局部斜率，据此算出镜面要怎么调。", "A Shack-Hartmann sensor: each spot's shift is the wavefront's local slope, from which the mirror corrections are computed."],
	"cx_recoater": ["镜片镀膜舱", "MIRROR RECOATER"],
	"cx_recoater_a": ["真空腔、蒸发源和挡板，镜片面朝下装在夹具里。", "A vacuum chamber, evaporation sources and shutter, a segment held face-down."],
	"cx_recoater_b": ["腔里可能有镜片；蒸发源带电。", "A segment may be inside; its sources are electrically heated."],
	"cx_recoater_c": ["断电，取出里面的镜片单独处理。", "Isolate it and deal with any segment inside separately."],
	"cx_recoater_x": ["在真空中把铝加热蒸发，原子沉积在镜面上形成约 100 nm 的反射膜。", "Aluminium evaporated in vacuum condenses on the mirror into a reflective film about 100 nm thick."],
	"cx_ir_camera": ["红外相机", "INFRARED CAMERA"],
	"cx_ir_camera_a": ["真空杜瓦、冷指、滤光轮、镜筒和背后的制冷机。", "A vacuum dewar, cold finger, filter wheel, lens barrel and the cryocooler on its back."],
	"cx_ir_camera_b": ["探测器在低温下，杜瓦有真空；制冷机带电。", "The detector is cold, the dewar under vacuum, the cooler live."],
	"cx_ir_camera_c": ["断电回温后整件拆下。", "Isolate it, let it warm, remove it whole."],
	"cx_ir_camera_x": ["红外探测器要冷到几十开尔文以下，否则自己的热辐射会淹没信号。", "An infrared detector has to be cooled to tens of kelvin, or its own glow drowns the signal."],
	"cx_spectrograph": ["光谱仪", "SPECTROGRAPH"],
	"cx_spectrograph_a": ["狭缝、准直镜、衍射光栅、相机镜头和探测器。", "Slit, collimator, diffraction grating, camera optics and detector."],
	"cx_spectrograph_b": ["光栅刻线极密，摸一下就毁。", "The grating's ruling is so fine a touch ruins it."],
	"cx_spectrograph_c": ["盖着遮光罩整件运走。", "Move it whole under its cover."],
	"cx_spectrograph_x": ["光栅每毫米上千条刻线，把光按波长分开；从谱线能读出元素和速度。", "A grating with thousands of lines a millimetre spreads light by wavelength; the lines in the spectrum give elements and velocities."],
	"cx_coronagraph": ["日冕仪", "CORONAGRAPH"],
	"cx_coronagraph_a": ["镜筒入口的遮挡盘挡住恒星本体，只看它周围的日冕。", "An occulting disc at the tube's mouth blots out the star to see the corona round it."],
	"cx_coronagraph_b": ["刚从近日点回来，可能还很烫；光学精密。", "Just back from perihelion it may be hot; its optics are precise."],
	"cx_coronagraph_c": ["测温，冷下来再整件拆。", "Measure its temperature, wait for it to cool, remove it whole."],
	"cx_coronagraph_x": ["日冕亮度只有日面的百万分之一，杂散光必须压到极低，所以镜筒里一圈圈都是挡光环。", "The corona is a millionth as bright as the disc, so stray light is driven down with vane after vane inside the tube."],
	"cx_particle_det": ["粒子探测器", "PARTICLE DETECTOR"],
	"cx_particle_det_a": ["准直器后面一叠硅探测器平面和吸收板。", "A stack of silicon detector planes and absorbers behind a collimator."],
	"cx_particle_det_b": ["精密、怕撞，偏压电源带高压。", "Precise and fragile, its bias supply at high voltage."],
	"cx_particle_det_c": ["断电后整件拆下。", "Isolate it and remove it whole."],
	"cx_particle_det_x": ["粒子穿过每层硅时损失能量，按损失的多少和穿透深度分辨粒子种类和能量。", "A particle loses energy in each silicon layer; how much and how deep it gets tell its kind and energy."],
	"cx_magnetometer": ["磁强计", "MAGNETOMETER"],
	"cx_magnetometer_a": ["三个正交绕组的磁通门传感头和电子箱。", "A fluxgate head with three orthogonal windings, and its electronics."],
	"cx_magnetometer_b": ["精密，装在伸杆根部。", "Precise, mounted at the root of its boom."],
	"cx_magnetometer_c": ["整件拆下送设备口。", "Remove it whole to the equipment bay."],
	"cx_magnetometer_x": ["磁强计要远离船上的磁性材料和电流，所以装在长杆末端；电子箱留在根部。", "It has to be far from the ship's magnetic materials and currents, hence the boom; its electronics stay at the root."],
	"cx_lab": ["分析仪器", "LABORATORY INSTRUMENTS"],
	"cx_lab_a": ["气相色谱、质谱仪、显微镜这类实验室仪器。", "Gas chromatographs, mass spectrometers, microscopes and the like."],
	"cx_lab_b": ["价值高、怕撞；质谱仪有真空泵和高压。", "Valuable and fragile; a mass spectrometer has vacuum pumps and high voltage."],
	"cx_lab_c": ["断电，整件轻运送设备口。", "Isolate it and carry it whole and gently to the equipment bay."],
	"cx_lab_x": ["色谱柱按沸点和极性把混合气分开，质谱按质荷比称出每种分子。", "A chromatograph's column separates a mixture by boiling point and polarity; a mass spectrometer weighs each molecule by mass to charge."],
	# ---------------------------------------------------------------- devices: data centre
	"cx_immersion_rack": ["浸没式服务器机柜", "IMMERSION RACK"],
	"cx_immersion_rack_a": ["竖插的刀片服务器整个泡在绝缘冷却液槽里。", "Blade servers stood on edge, all of them under a tank of dielectric fluid."],
	"cx_immersion_rack_b": ["槽里还有液就吊出来，液体泼出，短路相邻机柜。", "Lift it with the tank still full and the fluid spills, shorting the racks beside it."],
	"cx_immersion_rack_c": ["先从槽的接口把冷却液抽干，再吊机柜。", "Draw the tank dry at its port, then lift the rack."],
	"cx_immersion_rack_x": ["绝缘液（氟化液或合成油）直接接触芯片带走热量，比风冷高效得多。它本身很贵，泼掉就是损失；失重下泼出的液团会漂到隔壁机柜上。", "The dielectric (a fluorinated fluid or synthetic oil) touches the chips directly and carries heat far better than air. It's expensive in its own right; spilt, it's lost, and in free fall the globules drift onto the next rack."],
	"cx_storage_array": ["存储阵列与交换机", "STORAGE AND SWITCHING"],
	"cx_storage_array_a": ["一层层硬盘托架和控制器，或带线卡的核心交换机。", "Shelves of drive carriers and their controllers, or a core switch with its line cards."],
	"cx_storage_array_b": ["硬盘里可能是客户的监管数据。", "The drives may hold the client's data under custody."],
	"cx_storage_array_c": ["先把监管盘锁进运输箱，再拆阵列。", "Latch the custody drives into their transport bays before the array."],
	"cx_storage_array_x": ["数据的价值和硬件无关：一个硬盘的硬件值几百块，里面的数据可能牵扯合同违约。", "Data's worth has nothing to do with the hardware: the drive is worth a few hundred, what's on it may be a breach of contract."],
	"cx_drive_carrier": ["监管硬盘", "CUSTODY DRIVE"],
	"cx_drive_carrier_a": ["托架里的硬盘，带锁扣把手和活动灯。", "A drive in its carrier, with latch handle and activity light."],
	"cx_drive_carrier_b": ["没锁进屏蔽运输箱就带走，算违约，罚款。", "Taken out without being latched into the shielded transport bay, it's a breach: fined."],
	"cx_drive_carrier_c": ["先拨它的监管锁扣，再整件运走。", "Throw its custody latch first, then take it."],
	"cx_drive_carrier_x": ["“监管链”要求数据从离开机柜到交给客户，每一步都可证明没有被读取或复制。", "Chain of custody means every step from rack to client must show the data was never read or copied."],
	# ---------------------------------------------------------------- devices: drilling
	"cx_top_drive": ["顶驱", "TOP DRIVE"],
	"cx_top_drive_a": ["吊在游车下的钻井电机：齿轮箱、主轴、两个内防喷阀和吊卡。", "The drilling motor under the travelling block: gearbox, main shaft, two IBOP valves, elevator."],
	"cx_top_drive_b": ["它连着钻杆，钻杆里可能还有扭矩和泥浆压力。", "It's on the string, which may still hold torque and mud pressure."],
	"cx_top_drive_c": ["钻杆泄扭泄压之后再动它。", "Only after the string's torque and pressure are bled."],
	"cx_top_drive_x": ["顶驱从上方直接旋转钻杆，同时从鹅颈管注入泥浆。功率常在 1 MW 以上。", "A top drive turns the string from above and pumps mud in through its gooseneck, often at over a megawatt."],
	"cx_drawworks": ["绞车", "DRAWWORKS"],
	"cx_drawworks_a": ["缠着大绳的卷筒、盘式刹车、电机和齿轮箱。", "A grooved drum with the drill line, disc brakes, motor and gearbox."],
	"cx_drawworks_b": ["大绳承受着整串钻具的拉力。", "Its line carries the whole string's pull."],
	"cx_drawworks_c": ["钻具卸完、大绳松弛后再拆。", "Only once the string is out and the line slack."],
	"cx_drawworks_x": ["大绳经天车和游车穿成多股，绞车拉一股，就能吊起几百吨。", "The line is reeved through crown and travelling blocks; one pull at the drum lifts hundreds of tonnes."],
	"cx_blocks": ["天车与游车", "CROWN AND TRAVELLING BLOCKS"],
	"cx_blocks_a": ["井架顶部的一排滑轮（天车）和上下移动的滑轮组（游车）。", "The sheaves atop the derrick (crown) and the block that rides up and down (travelling)."],
	"cx_blocks_b": ["大绳绷着时它们是一套张紧的滑轮组。", "With the line taut they're a tensioned tackle."],
	"cx_blocks_c": ["松了大绳再拆。", "Slack the line first."],
	"cx_blocks_x": ["10 股大绳的滑轮组，绞车拉力乘以约 10 就是吊重。", "With ten lines strung, the hook load is about ten times the drum's pull."],
	"cx_rotary_table": ["转盘", "ROTARY TABLE"],
	"cx_rotary_table_a": ["钻台上的转盘：齿圈、方补心和驱动小齿轮。", "The turntable in the drill floor: ring gear, master bushing, drive pinion."],
	"cx_rotary_table_b": ["它的刹车锁着钻杆里的残余扭矩。", "Its brake holds the residual torque in the string."],
	"cx_rotary_table_c": ["关转盘刹车泄扭，扭矩表读到接近 0。", "Release the rotary brake to bleed the torque until the gauge reads near zero."],
	"cx_rotary_table_x": ["几千米的钻杆像一根扭簧：转盘停下时，钻杆里还扭着几圈。", "Kilometres of pipe act as a torsion spring: when the table stops, the string is still wound up by several turns."],
	"cx_drillpipe": ["钻杆", "DRILL PIPE"],
	"cx_drillpipe_a": ["三根一立的钻杆，接头处有耐磨带；排放架上一层层码着。", "Stands of three joints, hardbanding at the tool joints; racked in rows."],
	"cx_drillpipe_b": ["还在井里的钻杆带着扭矩和泥浆压力。", "Pipe still in the hole holds torque and mud pressure."],
	"cx_drillpipe_c": ["泄扭泄压后自上而下逐节卸扣。", "Bleed it, then break the stands out from the top down."],
	"cx_drillpipe_x": ["钻杆接头是锥形螺纹，上扣扭矩几万牛·米。排放架上的钻杆是普通货物。", "Tool joints are tapered threads made up to tens of thousands of newton-metres. Racked pipe is ordinary cargo."],
	"cx_bha": ["钻具组合", "BOTTOM-HOLE ASSEMBLY"],
	"cx_bha_a": ["钻铤、扶正器、随钻测量工具、取芯筒和钻头。", "Drill collars, stabiliser, MWD tool, core barrel and bit."],
	"cx_bha_b": ["最重的一段，随钻工具里有电池，取芯筒里有岩芯。", "The heaviest part; the MWD tool carries batteries, the core barrel a core."],
	"cx_bha_c": ["电池按危险品处理，岩芯单独回收。", "Treat the batteries as hazards and recover the core separately."],
	"cx_bha_x": ["钻铤给钻头加压，扶正器让井眼保持笔直。岩芯是钻井的“产品”，常是合同指定件。", "Collars put weight on the bit; the stabiliser keeps the hole straight. The core is what drilling is for, often a named item."],
	"cx_mud_pump": ["泥浆泵", "MUD PUMP"],
	"cx_mud_pump_a": ["三缸往复泵：动力端、十字头、液力端和脉动阻尼器。", "A triplex pump: power end, crossheads, fluid end and pulsation dampener."],
	"cx_mud_pump_b": ["排出管和阻尼器里有高压泥浆；阻尼器预充着氮气。", "Its discharge and dampener hold mud under pressure; the dampener is precharged with nitrogen."],
	"cx_mud_pump_c": ["泄掉排出管压力和阻尼器的氮气，再拆。", "Bleed the discharge and the dampener's nitrogen, then remove it."],
	"cx_mud_pump_x": ["泥浆泵排压可达 35 MPa。脉动阻尼器的氮气囊吸收每一冲程的压力波动。", "Mud pumps discharge at up to 35 MPa. The dampener's nitrogen bladder absorbs each stroke's pressure surge."],
	"cx_shaker": ["振动筛", "SHALE SHAKER"],
	"cx_shaker_a": ["弹簧上倾斜的筛箱，两台振动电机，筛出钻屑。", "A tilted basket on springs with two vibrator motors, screening the cuttings out."],
	"cx_shaker_b": ["筛箱里是黏糊糊的泥浆。", "Its basket is full of sticky mud."],
	"cx_shaker_c": ["断电后整件拆下。", "Isolate it and remove it whole."],
	"cx_shaker_x": ["失重下没有重力让钻屑滑下筛面，船上的振动筛靠振动方向把钻屑“抛”出去。", "Without gravity cuttings don't slide off the screen; a ship's shaker throws them off along its vibration."],
	"cx_mud_clean": ["泥浆净化设备", "MUD TREATMENT"],
	"cx_mud_clean_a": ["除砂器、除气器、离心机、液气分离器和搅拌器。", "Desander, degasser, centrifuge, mud-gas separator and agitator."],
	"cx_mud_clean_b": ["里面有泥浆，除气器和液气分离器里可能有可燃气。", "They hold mud, and the degasser and separator may hold flammable gas."],
	"cx_mud_clean_c": ["排空、通风后再拆。", "Drain and vent them before removing them."],
	"cx_mud_clean_x": ["钻到含气地层时，泥浆会带着天然气返回；除气器在真空下把气体分出来送去燃烧或放空。", "Drilling through gas, the mud comes back carrying it; the degasser draws it out under vacuum to flare or vent."],
	"cx_roughneck": ["铁钻工", "IRON ROUGHNECK"],
	"cx_roughneck_a": ["轨道上的小车、折叠臂和上下两套扳手头。", "A carriage on its rail, folding arm, spinner and torque wrench heads."],
	"cx_roughneck_b": ["液压驱动，保着压时动作会很猛。", "Hydraulic, and violent if it moves while pressurised."],
	"cx_roughneck_c": ["泄压后拆。", "Relieve it before removing it."],
	"cx_roughneck_x": ["铁钻工代替人上卸钻杆螺纹：上面旋扣，下面用几万牛·米扭矩紧扣或松扣。", "It makes and breaks the pipe connections in place of a crew: spinning above, up to tens of thousands of newton-metres below."],
	"cx_bop": ["防喷器组", "BLOWOUT PREVENTER"],
	"cx_bop_a": ["环形防喷器加三道闸板防喷器（含剪切闸板），侧出口阀。", "An annular preventer over three ram preventers (one blind-shear), with side outlet valves."],
	"cx_bop_b": ["关着的闸板下面可能憋着井压。", "Pressure may be trapped below closed rams."],
	"cx_bop_c": ["从节流/压井管线泄压，确认无压后再拆。", "Bleed it through the choke or kill line and confirm it's dead before removing it."],
	"cx_bop_x": ["井涌时防喷器在几秒内封住井口；剪切闸板能剪断钻杆封井。它是井控的最后一道屏障，也是钻井船上最贵的设备之一。", "In a kick the BOP shuts the well in seconds; the shear rams cut the pipe and seal. It's the last barrier of well control and one of a drillship's dearest items."],
	"cx_well_manifold": ["立管与节流管汇", "STANDPIPE AND CHOKE MANIFOLD"],
	"cx_well_manifold_a": ["立管、闸阀、节流阀、压力表和防喷器蓄能器组。", "Standpipe, gate valves, adjustable choke, gauges and the BOP accumulator unit."],
	"cx_well_manifold_b": ["管汇和蓄能器里都有高压。", "Both the manifold and the accumulators hold high pressure."],
	"cx_well_manifold_c": ["经泄压阀放压，蓄能器泄到 0 再拆。", "Bleed it through its valves, bring the accumulators to zero, then remove it."],
	"cx_well_manifold_x": ["防喷器蓄能器（Koomey）在 21 MPa 下储存足够关闭全部闸板的液压能，断电也能工作。", "The BOP accumulators (a Koomey unit) store enough fluid at 21 MPa to close every ram, power or no power."],
	# ---------------------------------------------------------------- devices: gas plant
	"cx_ortho_para": ["正仲氢转化器", "ORTHO-PARA CONVERTER"],
	"cx_ortho_para_a": ["换热器通道里填着氧化铁催化剂，泡在冷浴里。", "Hydrous iron oxide catalyst packed in a heat exchanger's passages, in a cold bath."],
	"cx_ortho_para_b": ["里面是极冷的氢。", "Full of very cold hydrogen."],
	"cx_ortho_para_c": ["回温泄压后再拆。", "Warm it and relieve it before removing it."],
	"cx_ortho_para_x": ["常温氢 75% 是正氢；液化后它会自发转成仲氢并放热，足以把一罐液氢蒸掉大半，所以液化时就要用催化剂转化掉。", "Room-temperature hydrogen is 75 % ortho; liquefied, it slowly converts to para and gives off enough heat to boil away most of a tank — so it's converted on a catalyst as it's liquefied."],
	"cx_precooler": ["液氮预冷器", "LN₂ PRECOOLER"],
	"cx_precooler_a": ["液氮浴槽里的盘管，工艺气从中穿过预冷。", "A coiled bundle in a liquid nitrogen bath, the process gas running through it."],
	"cx_precooler_b": ["槽里有液氮，一直在蒸发。", "It holds liquid nitrogen, always boiling off."],
	"cx_precooler_c": ["抽空液氮、放掉蒸发气后再拆。", "Draw off the nitrogen and vent the boil-off before removing it."],
	"cx_precooler_x": ["先用 77 K 的液氮把气体预冷，后面的透平才能高效地冷到 20 K。", "Pre-cooling the gas with 77 K nitrogen lets the turbines downstream reach 20 K efficiently."],
	# ---------------------------------------------------------------- devices: industry
	"cx_arc_furnace": ["电弧炉炉芯", "ARC FURNACE CORE"],
	"cx_arc_furnace_a": ["耐火衬里的炉壳、三根石墨电极和水冷炉顶。", "A refractory-lined shell, three graphite electrodes and a water-cooled roof."],
	"cx_arc_furnace_b": ["停机不等于冷却：几百度的炉芯断了冷却会热震开裂。", "Stopped isn't cold: cut the cooling on a core still at hundreds of degrees and thermal shock cracks it."],
	"cx_arc_furnace_c": ["保持冷却直到它冷透，再整件吊出。", "Keep the cooling on until it's cold through, then lift it out whole."],
	"cx_arc_furnace_x": ["耐火材料导热差，内外温差大时热应力会把它震裂。炉芯从 760 °C 降到 150 °C，在冷却回路工作时约需两分半。", "Refractory conducts heat badly; a big temperature difference through it cracks it. With the loop running, the core comes down from 760 °C to 150 °C in about two and a half minutes."],
	"cx_sorter": ["分选机", "SORTER"],
	"cx_sorter_a": ["涡电流分选机或磁选滚筒：把金属按种类分开。", "An eddy-current sorter or magnetic drum: separating metals by kind."],
	"cx_sorter_b": ["转子里是强永磁体，会吸铁屑和无人机。", "Its rotor is strong permanent magnets that pull steel swarf and the drone."],
	"cx_sorter_c": ["断电、等转子停，再拆。", "Isolate it, let the rotor stop, then remove it."],
	"cx_sorter_x": ["高速旋转的磁极在铝、铜里感应涡流，产生的斥力把有色金属“弹”过分料板，铁则被磁吸走。", "Spinning magnets induce eddy currents in aluminium and copper whose repulsion flicks them over the splitter, while iron is held by the magnet."],
	"cx_scrubber": ["尾气洗涤塔", "WET SCRUBBER"],
	"cx_scrubber_a": ["填料床、喷淋头、除雾器和循环泵。", "Packed bed, spray header, mist eliminator and recirculation pump."],
	"cx_scrubber_b": ["塔底的液体吸收了有害气体，有腐蚀性。", "The sump liquid has taken up the off-gas and is corrosive."],
	"cx_scrubber_c": ["排空塔底液，再拆。", "Drain the sump, then remove it."],
	"cx_scrubber_x": ["碱液喷淋吸收尾气里的酸性气体（SO₂、HCl）。", "An alkaline spray absorbs the acid gases (SO₂, HCl) from the off-gas."],
	"cx_crusher": ["破碎头", "CRUSHER"],
	"cx_crusher_a": ["圆锥破碎机：动锥在碗形衬板里偏心摆动。", "A cone crusher: a mantle gyrating inside a bowl liner."],
	"cx_crusher_b": ["料仓里还有矿时，它连着矿堆的重量。", "With ore still in the hopper, it bears the heap's load."],
	"cx_crusher_c": ["先卸空料仓，再拆。", "Empty the hopper first."],
	"cx_crusher_x": ["偏心轴让动锥一张一合，矿石在狭缝里被挤碎；很重，常要分段。", "An eccentric opens and closes the gap and the ore is crushed in it; heavy, often taken out in sections."],
	# ---------------------------------------------------------------- devices: weapons
	"cx_turret": ["炮塔与炮座", "GUN TURRET"],
	"cx_turret_a": ["多面体炮室、炮管、耳轴、回转座圈和下方的弹药提升机。", "Faceted gunhouse, barrel, trunnion, slewing ring and the hoist below."],
	"cx_turret_b": ["提升机和炮膛里可能还有弹药。", "Rounds may still be in the hoist and the breech."],
	"cx_turret_c": ["先清空弹药，再按标线拆炮塔。", "Clear the ammunition first, then take it apart on its lines."],
	"cx_turret_x": ["炮塔很重，座圈的滚道承受全部重量和后坐力；炮管是厚壁高强钢。", "A turret is heavy; its roller race carries the whole weight and the recoil. The barrel is thick high-strength steel."],
	"cx_launcher": ["箱式发射架", "BOX LAUNCHER"],
	"cx_launcher_a": ["并排的发射箱，各有易碎盖；或诱饵弹发射筒。", "Canisters side by side with frangible covers; or decoy tubes."],
	"cx_launcher_b": ["箱里可能有弹：切、烤、撞都会让它起爆。", "A canister may still be loaded: cut, heated or knocked, it goes off."],
	"cx_launcher_c": ["别在附近切割；弹药按危险品整件送。", "Don't cut near it; send the munitions whole as hazards."],
	"cx_launcher_x": ["导弹的固体发动机和战斗部都是含能材料，受热到一定温度会自燃（烤燃）。", "A missile's solid motor and warhead are energetic materials that ignite on their own above a certain temperature (cook-off)."],
	"cx_ciws": ["近防炮", "CLOSE-IN WEAPON SYSTEM"],
	"cx_ciws_a": ["旋转多管炮、上方的雷达罩和底座。", "A rotary cannon, its radar dome above, and the mount."],
	"cx_ciws_b": ["弹鼓里可能有弹，电容带电。", "Its drum may hold rounds and its capacitors charge."],
	"cx_ciws_c": ["放电、清空弹鼓后再拆。", "Discharge it and empty the drum before removing it."],
	"cx_ciws_x": ["射速每分钟几千发，弹鼓装上千发——一个弹鼓就是一座小弹药库。", "It fires thousands of rounds a minute from a drum of over a thousand — the drum is a small magazine."],
	# ---------------------------------------------------------------- mechanisms: stored energy
	"cx_m_munitions": ["弹药：烤燃与殉爆", "MUNITIONS: COOK-OFF AND CHAIN"],
	"cx_m_munitions_a": ["弹库里的炮弹和导弹：受热、撞击都会起爆，一发引一串。", "Shells and missiles in the magazine: heat or a knock sets one off, and one sets off the rest."],
	"cx_m_munitions_b": ["在弹药附近切割会把它烤到起爆；一发炸了，附近的接连殉爆。", "Cutting near a round cooks it off; one goes, and those near it follow one by one."],
	"cx_m_munitions_c": ["先开注水阀淹掉弹库（弹药报废但安全），或远离弹药作业。", "Open the flood valve to wet the magazine (the rounds are scrap, but safe), or keep the laser well away."],
	"cx_m_munitions_x": ["激光在弹药一定范围内工作会持续加热它，到达烤燃温度就起爆；以超过一定速度撞到东西也会起爆。弹库的热测点读出最烫的那一发。注水后的弹药既不怕热也不怕撞，但也不值钱了。", "The beam working near a round keeps heating it until it reaches its cook-off temperature; hitting something fast enough sets it off too. The magazine's heat test point reads its hottest round. Wetted rounds fear neither heat nor knocks — and are worth nothing."],
	"cx_m_quench": ["超导磁体失超", "SUPERCONDUCTING MAGNET QUENCH"],
	"cx_m_quench_a": ["八组超导线圈储着磁能，靠液氦和冷箱保持超导。", "Eight coil packs holding field energy, kept superconducting by liquid helium and the cold box."],
	"cx_m_quench_b": ["失冷超过临界温度、或带场切支撑，线圈失超：能量瞬间释放，并连锁到相邻线圈。", "Lose the cooling past the critical temperature, or cut a support while energised, and it quenches — all at once, and the coils beside it follow."],
	"cx_m_quench_c": ["合上泄能开关、保持冷箱有电，储能读数降到安全值再断冷却、拆线圈。", "Close the dump switch, keep the cold box powered, wait for the stored energy to fall to safe, only then the cooling and the coils."],
	"cx_m_quench_x": ["泄能时电流经泄能电阻按 e^(−t/τ) 衰减，几个时间常数后降到安全值以下，这时线圈升温也无害。顺序反过来（先断冷却），线圈在满能量时升温越过临界温度，失超释放的热和电磁力会毁掉线圈和周围设备，还会烧掉一部分昂贵的液氦。", "Dumping, the current decays through the resistor as e^(−t/τ) and after a few time constants is below safe; then the coil can warm harmlessly. The other way round — cooling off first — it warms past critical while full, and the quench's heat and forces wreck it and what's near, boiling off costly helium."],
	"cx_m_flywheel": ["还在转的飞轮", "A FLYWHEEL STILL SPINNING"],
	"cx_m_flywheel_a": ["飞轮开局 20,000 rpm；刹车、冷却和转速表管着它。", "The flywheel comes in at 20,000 rpm; brake, brake cooling and a tachometer go with it."],
	"cx_m_flywheel_b": ["不开冷却干刹，8 秒后卡钳烧坏，从此停不下来；300 rpm 以上松开，轮子甩出去。", "Brake it dry and the caliper burns out in 8 s and it can't be stopped; free it above 300 rpm and it's thrown."],
	"cx_m_flywheel_c": ["先开刹车冷却再上刹车，等到 300 rpm 以下再拆；轨道预紧从尾往头松。", "Brake cooling on, then the brake; under 300 rpm, take it out. Slack the rail preloads from the tail forward."],
	"cx_m_flywheel_x": ["开着冷却时刹车每秒降 250 rpm，从 20,000 降下来约 80 秒；干刹降速减半。飞轮能量与转速平方成正比，300 rpm 时只剩开局的 0.02%。两组电容断主电后仍带 400 V，喂着上轨的直线电机：先放电。", "With cooling on the brake takes 250 rpm off a second, about 80 s down from 20,000; dry, half as fast. The energy goes with the square of the speed: at 300 rpm, 0.02 % of what it started with. Two capacitor banks keep 400 V on the upper rail's linear motor after the mains is off: discharge them first."],
	"cx_m_pyro": ["救生舱火工品", "ESCAPE POD PYROTECHNICS"],
	"cx_m_pyro_a": ["每个救生舱两个发射夹，前夹装着爆炸螺栓，接着它自己的发射电容。", "Each pod has two launch clamps; the front one carries an explosive bolt fed by its own launch capacitor."],
	"cx_m_pyro_b": ["待发电路还带电时拆发射夹或火工品，螺栓走火，救生舱被弹出去。", "Free the clamp or the charge with the arming circuit live and the bolt fires: the pod is thrown out."],
	"cx_m_pyro_c": ["在竖井的救生舱控制面板断开待发开关，再拆夹子；火工品送危险品口。", "Disarm it at the pod control panel in the shaft, then the clamps; the charges go to the hazard mouth."],
	"cx_m_pyro_x": ["发射电容是一路独立电源，主开关管不到它。爆炸螺栓本身是危险品，不能进熔炉。某些合同里会有一个救生舱的发射电路仍然带电（“救生舱待发”事故）。", "The launch capacitor is a supply of its own, beyond the main switch. The bolts are hazards and never go to the furnace. Some contracts have one pod whose circuit is still armed."],
	"cx_m_magnet": ["残磁", "RESIDUAL MAGNETISM"],
	"cx_m_magnet_a": ["磁力牵引头断电后还留着磁场。", "The magnetic towing head keeps a field after its power is off."],
	"cx_m_magnet_b": ["范围内会把无人机和散落的钢件吸过去撞上。", "It pulls the drone and loose steel in range onto itself."],
	"cx_m_magnet_c": ["在线圈电源断开后，用退磁控件消磁，再靠近。", "With its coil supply dead, degauss it at its control before going near."],
	"cx_m_magnet_x": ["铁磁材料磁化后会保留剩磁；退磁是用逐渐衰减的交变磁场把磁畴打乱。退磁要求线圈本身没电，否则会重新磁化。", "Ferromagnetic material keeps some magnetisation; degaussing scrambles its domains with a decaying alternating field — which needs the coil's own supply dead, or it simply re-magnetises."],
	"cx_m_preload": ["预紧机构", "PRELOADED MECHANISMS"],
	"cx_m_preload_a": ["靠液压蓄能器或锁销撑着、储着力的臂、轴、铰链和缆。", "Arms, shafts, hinges and cables held under load by accumulators or locking pins."],
	"cx_m_preload_b": ["锁销还在、或液压还有压就拆枢轴，它会弹开，砸坏它和它撞上的东西。", "Take the pivot out with a pin still in or pressure still on, and it springs, smashing itself and what it hits."],
	"cx_m_preload_c": ["先泄蓄能器的压，再拔全部锁销，张力表归零，最后拆枢轴。", "Bleed the accumulator, pull every pin, see the tension gauge reach zero, then the pivot."],
	"cx_m_preload_x": ["预紧储存的是弹性能和液压能：拉缆 E = F²L/2EA，蓄能器 E ≈ pV·ln(p/p₀)。卸能的顺序总是“能量—锁—结构”。拆完锁销但没泄压，力全落在枢轴上，枢轴一松就释放。", "Preload stores elastic and hydraulic energy: a cable E = F²L/2EA, an accumulator roughly pV·ln(p/p₀). The order is always energy, then locks, then structure. Pins out but pressure still on, all the force sits on the pivot, released the moment it goes."],
	"cx_m_drones": ["各自带电的无人机", "DRONES WITH THEIR OWN POWER"],
	"cx_m_drones_a": ["机库里每个机位、每架无人机都有自己的电池。", "Every bay and every drone in the hangar has a battery of its own."],
	"cx_m_drones_b": ["断了主电池它们照样带电；电池还在机身上就松开，无人机醒来把自己甩进机位。", "Kill the main battery and they're still live; release one with its pack aboard and it wakes and throws itself into its bay."],
	"cx_m_drones_c": ["断机位充电开关、断机身电池开关，拔两根线，摘电池包，再整机运走。", "Charger off at the rack, battery off on the airframe, both leads out, pack off — then the drone, whole."],
	"cx_m_drones_x": ["无人机的飞控在失去链路时会尝试自主起飞；只有电池物理断开才算安全。整机交付设备口价值远高于熔成废料。", "A drone's controller tries to take off on its own when its link drops; only a physically disconnected battery is safe. Delivered whole it's worth far more than melted."],
	# ---------------------------------------------------------------- mechanisms: cryogenics
	"cx_m_cryo_tank": ["低温货罐", "CRYOGENIC CARGO TANKS"],
	"cx_m_cryo_tank_a": ["真空夹套里的低温货罐，压力跟着温度走。", "Cold cargo tanks in vacuum jackets, their pressure following their temperature."],
	"cx_m_cryo_tank_b": ["回温升压；安全阀冻住时压力冲到爆罐。夹套破了漏热快十倍。", "Warming raises the pressure; with the relief frozen it climbs to burst. A broken jacket leaks heat ten times faster."],
	"cx_m_cryo_tank_c": ["保持制冷机运行，从货罐接口抽液；冻住的阀先加热解冻。", "Keep the chillers running, draw the cargo at each tank's port, thaw a frozen valve with its heater."],
	"cx_m_cryo_tank_x": ["有液体时罐的蒸气压随温度升高大约每 20 °C 翻一倍。真空夹套完好时漏热很慢，一单合同里升不到 10 °C；夹套一破就快得多。", "With liquid in it the vapour pressure roughly doubles every 20 °C. A sound vacuum jacket lets heat in slowly — under 10 °C in a contract's time; broken, far faster."],
	"cx_m_boiloff": ["蒸发升压", "BOIL-OFF"],
	"cx_m_boiloff_a": ["低温罐一直在蒸发，罐压持续上升；制冷运转时压力保持。", "The tanks boil off and their pressure keeps climbing; with refrigeration running it holds."],
	"cx_m_boiloff_b": ["先断电，制冷一停，压力爬到安全阀放空（货物损失）或爆罐。", "Cut the power first and the cooling stops: the pressure climbs to the relief (cargo lost) or to burst."],
	"cx_m_boiloff_c": ["边制冷边从软管抽液，抽得越多压力越低；最后才断电。", "Refrigerate while you draw the cargo off at the hose — the more drawn, the lower the pressure — and cut the power last."],
	"cx_m_boiloff_x": ["蒸发的气体占液体几百倍的体积，所以一点点漏热就让压力明显上升；保温层破损处升得更快。安全阀起跳放掉的就是货物本身。", "Boil-off gas takes hundreds of times the liquid's volume, so a little heat leak raises the pressure fast, faster where the insulation is torn. What the relief vents is the cargo itself."],
	"cx_m_frozen_valve": ["冻住的安全阀", "A FROZEN RELIEF VALVE"],
	"cx_m_frozen_valve_a": ["某个罐的安全阀出口结了冰塞，打不开。", "One tank's relief valve has an ice plug in its outlet and won't lift."],
	"cx_m_frozen_valve_b": ["压力过了起跳值它也不泄放，一直升到爆罐。", "Past its set pressure it doesn't relieve; the tank climbs on until it bursts."],
	"cx_m_frozen_valve_c": ["测各罐安全阀的温度：异常冷的那个开加热解冻，或先把它的罐抽低。", "Read each relief valve's temperature: thaw the abnormally cold one with its heater, or draw its tank down first."],
	"cx_m_frozen_valve_x": ["泄放的低温气体在出口膨胀降温，空气或水汽在出口冻成冰塞。测温探针能发现它：冻住的阀比其它阀冷得多。", "Cold gas venting through the outlet expands and chills it, freezing moisture into an ice plug. The probe shows it: the frozen valve reads far colder than the rest."],
	"cx_m_dilution": ["稀释制冷机按序回温", "DILUTION FRIDGE WARM-UP"],
	"cx_m_dilution_a": ["量子芯片在毫开级的混合室里；制冷机一层层冷板吊着它。", "The qubit chip sits in the mixing chamber at millikelvin, hung under stage after stage."],
	"cx_m_dilution_b": ["混合气没收回就停冷头，混合气沸掉、冷板受损；极冷时加热或动它，芯片热震开裂。", "Stop the cold head before recovering the mixture and it boils off; heat it or touch it while still at millikelvin and the chip cracks."],
	"cx_m_dilution_c": ["停循环泵 → 回收混合气 → 停脉管冷头 → 冷板自然回温，过了极冷再开加热；锁住隔振台再动刀。", "Stop circulation → recover the mixture → stop the pulse tube → let the stages warm, heaters only past the coldest → lock the isolation table before any cutting."],
	"cx_m_dilution_x": ["混合室最冷、回温最慢。在低于热震温度时打开加热器，芯片表面和内部温差太大，硅片会裂；低于脆性温度时任何振动都能让它碎。隔振台没锁，附近的切割会通过台面震到芯片。", "The mixing chamber is coldest and warms slowest. Heaters switched on below the shock temperature put too much difference between the chip's surface and its body and the silicon cracks; below the brittle temperature any shake breaks it. With the isolation table unlocked, a nearby cut shakes the chip."],
	"cx_m_coldchain": ["冷链不能断", "THE COLD CHAIN"],
	"cx_m_coldchain_a": ["三个冷舱 −25 °C，靠冷机和制冷主机保温。", "Three cold holds at −25 °C, held there by the chillers and the refrigeration plant."],
	"cx_m_coldchain_b": ["断电或切坏制冷，冷舱回温；过了 −5 °C 货物解冻，只剩 45% 价值。", "Cut the power or the plant and the holds warm; past −5 °C the cargo thaws and keeps 45 % of its value."],
	"cx_m_coldchain_c": ["先在外部面板插上“船坞临时供冷”，再断电、再动制冷系统。", "Plug in berth cooling at the outside panel first, then cut the power and work the plant."],
	"cx_m_coldchain_x": ["冷冻货物的价值来自“从未解冻”：一次回温就不可逆。制冷剂从储液罐回收口闭环回收；开舱顶货舱口前先放气。", "Frozen cargo is worth what it is because it never thawed: one warm-up can't be undone. The refrigerant is recovered at the receiver's port; vent each hold before opening its roof hatch."],
	"cx_m_ice": ["冰体", "THE ICE"],
	"cx_m_ice_a": ["整座冰山就是货：每块冰 0.6 m³ 水，靠加热垫逐块融化。", "The iceberg is the cargo: each block 0.6 m³ of water, melted block by block with the heater pads."],
	"cx_m_ice_b": ["融水积到 3 m³ 不抽、总线带电，发动机舱短路；鞍座夹着时切裂纹处的冰，冰体裂开。", "Let 3 m³ of melt pile up with the bus live and the engine room shorts; cut the cracked blocks with the saddles still clamped and the ice splits."],
	"cx_m_ice_c": ["开加热垫，边融边从水总管接口抽走；冰剩一半以下再松鞍座。", "Heaters on, draw the melt off at the water header as it comes; release the saddles only once less than half the ice is left."],
	"cx_m_ice_x": ["融化 1 kg 冰要 334 kJ。冰切得很慢——切口会重新冻上。应变表读冰体裂纹的扩展程度（开局 90%）。", "Melting a kilogram of ice takes 334 kJ. Ice cuts very slowly, its kerf freezing over again. The strain gauge reads how far the crack has run (90 % at the start)."],
	# ---------------------------------------------------------------- mechanisms: fluids
	"cx_m_drill_torque": ["钻杆残余扭矩与泥浆压力", "TRAPPED TORQUE AND MUD PRESSURE"],
	"cx_m_drill_torque_a": ["八节立根还扭着残余扭矩，管里憋着泥浆压力。", "Eight stands still wound with residual torque, mud pressure trapped inside."],
	"cx_m_drill_torque_b": ["带扭矩卸扣，钻杆反弹扭断、甩打钻台；带压卸扣，泥浆喷出污染设备。", "Break a stand with torque on and it whips round, smashing the drill floor; with pressure on, the mud blows out over the equipment."],
	"cx_m_drill_torque_c": ["关转盘刹车泄扭（扭矩表 < 5%），开泄压阀放泥浆（可回收），再卸扣。", "Release the rotary brake to bleed the torque (gauge under 5 %), open the relief and recover the mud, then break out."],
	"cx_m_drill_torque_x": ["扭矩泄放按时间常数指数下降；泥浆从泄压阀放到回收口是有价值的货。扭矩表和压力表都在钻台上。", "The torque bleeds off exponentially; the mud drained through the relief is cargo worth recovering. Both gauges are on the drill floor."],
	"cx_m_drill_slips": ["卡瓦与自上而下", "SLIPS, TOP DOWN"],
	"cx_m_drill_slips_a": ["每节立根下面一副卡瓦，托着它和它下面的整串钻杆。", "Under each stand a set of slips, holding it and everything below it."],
	"cx_m_drill_slips_b": ["先卸下面的，上面的失去支撑掉落；卡瓦没坐好就卸，下面的整串掉进井。", "Break a lower stand first and those above lose their support and drop; break out with the slips open and the string below drops down the hole."],
	"cx_m_drill_slips_c": ["从最上面一节开始，确认下面的卡瓦坐着，逐节往下卸。", "Start with the top stand, check the slips under it are set, and work down."],
	"cx_m_drill_slips_x": ["卡瓦是楔形牙块，钻杆越重咬得越紧。钻台作业的铁律：任何时候钻杆都要被卡瓦或吊卡之一抓着。", "Slips are wedged dies that grip harder the heavier the pipe. The rig floor's rule: at every moment the string is held by either the slips or the elevator."],
	"cx_m_tanknet": ["交叉连通罐", "CROSS-CONNECTED TANKS"],
	"cx_m_tanknet_a": ["三个罐经交叉阀接到一根总管，大泵从泵房回收口抽总管。", "Three tanks on one header through crossover valves; the big pump draws the header at the pump room's port."],
	"cx_m_tanknet_b": ["先断电泵就抽不动；抽干还开着泵干转损坏；先泄罐顶气再抽，罐被吸瘪。", "Cut the power first and the pump can't draw; leave it on dry and it wrecks itself; vent the ullage before drawing and the tank collapses."],
	"cx_m_tanknet_c": ["开交叉阀，带着增压抽完，关回收口，再关增压、泄罐顶气；支管残液从低点排放口抽。", "Crossovers open, draw it off pressurised, close the port, then pressurisation off and ullage vented; drain the branches at their low points."],
	"cx_m_tanknet_x": ["开着交叉阀的罐液位会经总管拉平（连通器）。增压阀开着时，氮气球罐保持罐压，抽液不会抽出真空。有的合同里一个交叉阀显示关、实际内漏：关着时那个罐液位还在降。", "Tanks with open crossovers level out through the header. With the pressurisation open, the nitrogen sphere keeps the ullage pressure up and drawing can't pull a vacuum. In some contracts a crossover reads shut but leaks: that tank's level keeps falling with it closed."],
	"cx_m_immersion": ["浸没冷却", "IMMERSION COOLING"],
	"cx_m_immersion_a": ["十二个机柜各泡在一槽绝缘冷却液里。", "Twelve racks, each standing in a tank of dielectric coolant."],
	"cx_m_immersion_b": ["槽里有液就吊机柜，液体泼洒，短路同一排相邻的机柜。", "Lift a rack with its tank full and the fluid spills, shorting the racks beside it in the row."],
	"cx_m_immersion_c": ["每个槽从接口抽干，再吊机柜。", "Draw each tank dry at its port before lifting its rack."],
	"cx_m_immersion_x": ["冷却液本身很贵，按体积计价；失重下泼出的液团会漂到相邻机柜上。", "The coolant is dear and paid by volume; in free fall what spills drifts onto the next racks."],
	"cx_m_custody": ["数据监管", "DATA CUSTODY"],
	"cx_m_custody_a": ["存储阵列的硬盘是客户的监管物，要锁进屏蔽运输箱。", "The storage drives are the client's property in custody, to be latched into shielded transport bays."],
	"cx_m_custody_b": ["监管锁扣没拨就拔出硬盘，算违约罚款。", "Pull a drive with its custody latch open and it's a breach, fined."],
	"cx_m_custody_c": ["先拨每块盘的监管锁扣，运输箱整件送设备口。", "Throw every drive's latch; take the transport bays whole to the equipment bay."],
	"cx_m_custody_x": ["运输箱本身是合同指定件。锁扣拨上后，硬盘是客户封存的财产，完整计价。", "The transport bays are named items. Latched, the drives are the client's sealed property and pay whole."],
	"cx_m_waterball": ["失重水球", "THE WATER BALL"],
	"cx_m_waterball_a": ["网罩里团着几十立方米的水，里面养着鱼。", "Tens of cubic metres of water held in a net, fish living in it."],
	"cx_m_waterball_b": ["网罩或支架被切、被拆，水球散开：水损失，舱里电气泡水，总线带电就短路，鱼死。", "Cut or free the net or its frame and it bursts: the water lost, the room's electrics soaked (shorted if the bus is live), the fish dead."],
	"cx_m_waterball_c": ["先用泵把水抽到安全量以下（水球会变小），再拆网罩；鱼苗箱是指定件。", "Pump it down below the safe fraction first (the ball shrinks as you go), then the net; the fish holding tank is a named item."],
	"cx_m_waterball_x": ["没有重力，表面张力把水团成球；网罩只是轻轻兜着它。30 m³ 水是 30 吨，散开后的水团以原有的速度四处漂。", "With no gravity surface tension rounds the water into a ball; the net only cradles it. 30 m³ is 30 tonnes, and burst, it drifts apart at whatever speed it had."],
	"cx_m_media": ["外观相同的三种介质", "THREE LOOK-ALIKE MEDIA"],
	"cx_m_media_a": ["溶剂、酸液和乙二醇三只罐，三路管子一样且在途中交叉。", "Solvent, acid and glycol in three tanks; their three identical pipes cross on the way to the header."],
	"cx_m_media_b": ["抽一路时另两路阀没关，三种混成废液，一文不值还要付处理费。", "Draw one with the others' valves open and they mix into waste: worthless, and you pay for its disposal."],
	"cx_m_media_c": ["在总管每个口旁的取样点测一下是什么，关掉另两路的阀再抽。", "Sample at the point beside each header port to see what it is, shut the other two branches, then draw."],
	"cx_m_media_x": ["总管 1 号口出来的是 3 号罐，2 号口是 1 号罐，3 号口是 2 号罐——不测就会接错。支路还有液就拆总管，各路都会漏出来按量罚款。分离器有残压，从塔上的口泄压。", "Header port 1 is tank 3, port 2 is tank 1, port 3 is tank 2 — guess and you're wrong. Take the header off with liquid in the branches and they all leak, fined by volume. The separator keeps some pressure; relieve it at its port."],
	# ---------------------------------------------------------------- mechanisms: atmosphere, fire, contamination
	"cx_m_o2_flash": ["富氧闪燃", "OXYGEN-RICH FLASH FIRE"],
	"cx_m_o2_flash_a": ["舱里氧浓度远高于空气的 21%，各舱各不相同。", "Rooms whose oxygen is well above air's 21 %, each different."],
	"cx_m_o2_flash_b": ["有气压、氧超过阈值时在附近动激光，整舱闪燃，设备烧坏，无人机也被烧。", "With pressure in it and oxygen over the threshold, a laser nearby flashes the whole room: equipment burnt, the drone too."],
	"cx_m_o2_flash_c": ["先读各舱氧浓度，从各自的接口分舱放气，再动激光。", "Read each room's oxygen, vent each through its own port, then use the laser."],
	"cx_m_o2_flash_x": ["氧浓度从 21% 升到 35% 以上，可燃物的点燃温度大幅下降、燃速成倍提高，织物和塑料几乎一点就着。舱门打开，两舱空气会混合。", "From 21 % to over 35 % oxygen, ignition temperatures fall and burning rates multiply; fabric and plastics light at almost nothing. Open a door between two rooms and their air mixes."],
	"cx_m_composite": ["复合材料毒烟", "COMPOSITE FUMES"],
	"cx_m_composite_a": ["机身板件是碳纤维复合材料，用螺栓固定。", "The airframe panels are carbon-fibre composite, bolted on."],
	"cx_m_composite_b": ["在有气的舱旁激光切它，放出有毒烟雾，电子设备掉价、玻璃起雾。", "Cut it with the laser next to a room with air and it fills with toxic smoke: electronics lose value, glass fogs."],
	"cx_m_composite_c": ["拧螺栓整块拆，或先把舱抽成真空再切。", "Unbolt the panels whole, or vent the room to vacuum before cutting."],
	"cx_m_composite_x": ["环氧树脂基体在激光下热解，产生一氧化碳、氰化氢和细碳纤维尘。舱抽成真空时烟雾随空气一起排掉。", "The epoxy matrix pyrolyses under the beam into carbon monoxide, hydrogen cyanide and fine fibre dust. Venting the room takes the smoke out with the air."],
	"cx_m_radiation": ["辐射阴影", "RADIATION SHADOW"],
	"cx_m_radiation_a": ["停了的堆芯 1 m 处 3.2 Sv/h；屏蔽板、掩蔽间和液氢罐后面是阴影。", "The shut-down core reads 3.2 Sv/h at a metre; behind the shield, the shelter and the hydrogen tanks is shadow."],
	"cx_m_radiation_b": ["无人机累积剂量过 150 mSv，电子设备紊乱；切开堆芯包壳全船污染。", "Past 150 mSv the drone's electronics fault; cut the core's cladding and the whole ship is contaminated."],
	"cx_m_radiation_c": ["先把屏蔽板吊到堆芯前，在它的阴影里干活；锁好控制鼓，堆芯整件走危险品口。", "Hang the shield in front of the core and work in its shadow; lock the control drums and send the core whole to the hazard mouth."],
	"cx_m_radiation_x": ["剂量率与距离平方成反比：7 m 外约 65 mSv/h，停一分多钟就会出事（游戏里 1 秒按 2 分钟剂量计）。屏蔽板在哪，阴影就在哪——装着的、吊在吊车上的都算。剂量探头读所在位置的剂量率。", "Dose rate falls with the square of distance: at 7 m about 65 mSv/h, and a minute or so there is trouble (each second counts two minutes' dose). The shadow is wherever the shield is — on its mounts or on the crane. The dose probe reads the rate where it sits."],
	"cx_m_decay_heat": ["停机不等于冷却", "STOPPED ISN'T COLD"],
	"cx_m_decay_heat_a": ["炉芯或堆芯停了还有几百度，只靠冷却回路降温。", "A furnace or reactor core stopped is still hundreds of degrees, cooled only by its loop."],
	"cx_m_decay_heat_b": ["高温时断了冷却，热冲击把它震裂；没冷透就吊出、收散热瓣，同样开裂变形。", "Cut the cooling while it's hot and thermal shock cracks it; lift it or fold its radiator petals before it's cold and it cracks or deforms the same."],
	"cx_m_decay_heat_c": ["保持泵有电、回路满，读温度等它冷透，再断电、再吊出。", "Keep the pump powered and the loop full, watch the temperature down, then cut power and lift it."],
	"cx_m_decay_heat_x": ["冷却回路工作时约每秒降 4 °C。MF-126 的炉芯 350 °C 以上断冷却会裂，150 °C 以上吊出会裂；NR-95 的堆芯 60 °C 以上收散热瓣会变形。", "With the loop running it comes down about 4 °C a second. MF-126's core cracks if the cooling goes above 350 °C and if lifted above 150 °C; NR-95's petals deform if folded above 60 °C."],
	"cx_m_thermal": ["近日点余热", "PERIHELION HEAT"],
	"cx_m_thermal_a": ["刚掠过太阳，隔热瓦和前部壳体分区 300–800 °C。", "Just back from a pass close to the sun: heat tiles and forward hull at 300–800 °C by zone."],
	"cx_m_thermal_b": ["热区切割隔热瓦会碎；从热区取出的设备被烫坏；无人机进最热区会受伤。", "Cut a hot tile and it shatters; equipment taken out of a hot zone is heat-damaged; the drone is burnt in the hottest."],
	"cx_m_thermal_c": ["接上船坞冷却回路加速降温，用测温探针确认各区，冷了再动。", "Plug in the berth's cooling loop to speed it, read each zone with the probe, work it once cool."],
	"cx_m_thermal_x": ["真空中只能辐射散热，各区按自己的速率自然冷却；冷却回路能接到的区冷得快得多。", "In vacuum each zone sheds heat only by radiation, at its own rate; the zones the cooling loop reaches cool much faster."],
	"cx_m_bio": ["负压与生物污染", "NEGATIVE PRESSURE AND BIOHAZARD"],
	"cx_m_bio_a": ["隔离舱压力低于相邻舱；生物废物箱、滤芯和废液罐带污染。", "Isolation rooms kept below their neighbours' pressure; biohazard boxes, filters and waste tanks are contaminated."],
	"cx_m_bio_b": ["切开或未密封就搬，污染散进舱里空气，随气流扩散；干净舱被污染，设备价值降四分之一。", "Cut or moved unsealed, it spills into the air and travels with it; a clean room contaminated marks its equipment down a quarter."],
	"cx_m_bio_c": ["先封好每件生物危险品，经回收软管的滤芯放气，再开门。", "Seal every biohazard item, vent through the recovery hose's filter, then open doors."],
	"cx_m_bio_x": ["负压让空气只往隔离舱里流，污染出不来；负压一撤（门开了、墙切了），流向就反过来。回收软管的过滤器能把空气里的污染滤掉。", "Negative pressure keeps the air flowing into the isolation room so nothing gets out; lose it (a door open, a wall cut) and the flow reverses. The recovery hose's filter takes contamination out of the air."],
	# ---------------------------------------------------------------- mechanisms: loads and motion
	"cx_m_balance": ["按受力顺序释放", "RELEASE IN ORDER OF LOAD"],
	"cx_m_balance_a": ["卷扬机的缆还绷着；两台外挂吊舱一上一下全挂在尾后。", "The winch's cable still taut; two outboard pods hang aft, one above, one below."],
	"cx_m_balance_b": ["刹车没松就拆卷扬轴，卷筒甩出；只拆一台吊舱，船体被另一台拽扭。", "Take the winch shaft with the brake on and the drum flies; take one pod alone and the other twists the hull."],
	"cx_m_balance_c": ["先拔刹车销（张力表归零）；在舰尾设船体支撑，或两台吊舱一起拆。", "Pull the brake pins (tension to zero) first; set the hull support at the stern, or take both pods together."],
	"cx_m_balance_x": ["对称挂着的两个重物互相平衡；去掉一个，剩下那个的力矩全由船体承受，超出就扭坏吊梁和支柱。锁喉夹块受力来自卷扬机的缆，要刹车、锁销、蓄能器三样都处理掉。", "Two weights hung symmetrically balance each other; take one and the hull carries the other's whole moment, twisting its beams and struts. The throat clamp's load comes from the winch cable: brake, pins and accumulator all have to be dealt with."],
	"cx_m_sandwich": ["拆三明治", "UNMAKING THE SANDWICH"],
	"cx_m_sandwich_a": ["上下两条船体用 8 个液压夹钳夹着中间的居住舱。", "Two hulls clamp the habitat between them with eight hydraulic clamps."],
	"cx_m_sandwich_b": ["货舱没放气就松夹钳会弹开；一侧比另一侧多松两个，货舱扭转、裂了的横梁 2 断掉。", "Release a clamp before the hold is vented and it springs open; get two ahead on one side and the hold twists and cracked beam 2 snaps."],
	"cx_m_sandwich_c": ["先放气；交叉成对地松：上1→下4→上4→下1→上2→下3→上3→下2；横梁 2 等上1、下1 松开后再拆。", "Vent first; release in crossed pairs: U1→L4→U4→L1→U2→L3→U3→L2; beam 2 only after U1 and L1 are off."],
	"cx_m_sandwich_x": ["横梁 2 已经开裂，它的载荷表读 192 kN（其余 120 kN）。夹钳还保着压就整件拆下，钳口弹开。三套电路各自独立：上体走主电池，下体和货舱各有自己的电池。", "Beam 2 is already cracked; its load cell reads 192 kN (the others 120 kN). A clamp taken off while still holding pressure springs its jaw. Three separate circuits: the upper hull on the main battery, the lower hull and the hold each on their own."],
	"cx_m_boxbeam": ["货柜就是承力梁", "THE CONTAINERS ARE THE BEAM"],
	"cx_m_boxbeam_a": ["货柜四角扭锁锁在一起，整列货柜就是船体的承力箱梁。", "Containers twist-locked corner to corner: each column of them is the hull's load-bearing box beam."],
	"cx_m_boxbeam_b": ["外侧还满着就卸空里面一列，那里折弯；同列从下面抽，上面压下来；拉杆还紧着切会抽回来。", "Empty an inner column while the outer ones are full and it kinks there; pull from the bottom of a column and the ones above come down; cut a tie rod still tight and it whips."],
	"cx_m_boxbeam_c": ["从两端往中间卸，每列从上往下；先松花篮螺丝（拉力计读 0）再拆拉杆；有压的箱先抽气。", "Unload from the ends inward, each column top down; slack the turnbuckles (gauge at zero) before the tie rods; pump down pressurised boxes first."],
	"cx_m_boxbeam_x": ["船坞夹着第 4 列；每一列的弯曲 = 外侧还在位货柜的量 × 力臂，除以本列的刚度（弦杆 + 在位货柜数）。应变片读本列弯曲占极限的百分比。住人箱 60 kPa、低温箱 450 kPa。", "The berth holds column 4. Each column's bending is the containers still outboard of it times their lever, over its own stiffness (chords plus containers in place). Strain gauges read it as a share of the limit. Accommodation boxes hold 60 kPa, cryo boxes 450 kPa."],
	"cx_m_sail": ["帆的张力网", "THE SAIL'S TENSION NET"],
	"cx_m_sail_a": ["4 台绞盘的刹车各绷着一个象限的薄膜和撑索（每根 12 kN）。", "Four winch brakes each hold a quadrant's film and stays taut (12 kN a stay)."],
	"cx_m_sail_b": ["绷着切薄膜就撕，裂口跑到两边；切撑索，角梁甩向吊舱；没接地就碰薄膜，静电打无人机。", "Cut the film taut and it tears, the tear running on; cut a stay and the corner spar whips at the gondola; touch the film unearthed and static jumps to the drone."],
	"cx_m_sail_c": ["先在左下角接船坞地线，进吊舱松四台绞盘刹车，然后薄膜一块块整块拆，最后撑索和梁。", "Earth it at the bottom-left socket, release all four winch brakes in the gondola, then take the film off panel by panel, stays and spars after."],
	"cx_m_sail_x": ["张力计读每个象限的拉力。右上角那块开局就撕了，挨着它切也会撕穿。帆面面积大、电阻高，太阳风让它积累了大量静电。", "The tension gauges read each quadrant's pull. The top-right panel is already torn, and cutting next to it tears through. A sail is a huge, highly resistive surface; the solar wind has charged it heavily."],
	"cx_m_softshell": ["软壳气囊", "SOFT-SHELL GASBAGS"],
	"cx_m_softshell_a": ["气囊是 30 kPa 的低压容积，形状全靠内压撑着；每个有张紧器和束缚带。", "Each gasbag is a 30 kPa volume whose shape is only its pressure; each has a tensioner and straps."],
	"cx_m_softshell_b": ["鼓着就切，囊壁撕开塌下来砸设备；张紧器开着就拆带子，带子抽回来。", "Cut it inflated and the wall tears and collapses onto the equipment; take a strap with the tensioner on and it whips back."],
	"cx_m_softshell_c": ["每个气囊：抽气到 3 kPa 以下（会折叠）→ 松张紧器 → 拆束缚带 → 拆气囊。", "Each bag: pump below 3 kPa (it folds) → slack its tensioner → its straps → the bag."],
	"cx_m_softshell_x": ["织物壳体只能受拉不能受压：泄了气，它就是一块布。服务舱电池是独立电源，断了脊柱电池它还带电；电容另有放电点。", "A fabric shell carries tension, never compression: deflated, it's cloth. The service bay's battery is independent of the spine's; the capacitor has its own discharge point."],
	"cx_m_tether": ["旋转的系绳", "A SPINNING TETHER"],
	"cx_m_tether_a": ["两个吊舱用系绳连着，整组 2.0 rpm 旋转，张紧器另压着 8 kN。", "Two pods joined by a tether, the whole pair turning at 2.0 rpm, the tensioner adding 8 kN."],
	"cx_m_tether_b": ["转着切系绳，两个吊舱沿切线甩出；干刹 6 秒滚轮打滑，制动器永久失效。", "Cut the tether while it turns and both pods fly off on the tangent; brake it dry and in 6 s the rollers slip and the brake is gone for good."],
	"cx_m_tether_c": ["先开制动冷却再刹，停下后松张紧器，再拆系绳；推进剂先别排（制动失效时要靠 B 舱姿控反喷）。", "Brake cooling on, then the brake; stopped, slack the tensioner, then the tether. Keep B's propellant (if the brake fails, its thrusters are the only way to stop)."],
	"cx_m_tether_x": ["系绳张力 = 40 kN × (rpm/2)² + 张紧器 8 kN。开冷却时制动每秒降 0.025 rpm。磨损段只剩 5/7 股：停了但张紧器没松就切，整根崩断。", "Tension is 40 kN × (rpm/2)² plus the tensioner's 8 kN. With cooling, the brake takes 0.025 rpm off a second. The worn length has 5 of 7 strands: cut it stopped but still tensioned and the whole tether parts."],
	"cx_m_train": ["铰接与单总线", "ARTICULATION AND ONE BUS"],
	"cx_m_train_a": ["七节模块铰接成一列，400 V 总线经每个联轴器串过去；K-4 卡死弯着。", "Seven modules articulated in a train, the 400 V bus running through every coupling; K-4 is jammed and bent."],
	"cx_m_train_b": ["切断上游总线，后面全黑、罐泵抽不动；后面还挂着 75 t 以上就拆 K-4，后半列弹开。", "Cut the bus upstream and everything aft goes dark, the tank pumps dead; take K-4 with more than 75 t still hanging aft and the rear half springs."],
	"cx_m_train_c": ["从尾巴开始拆 M7、M6，最后处理 K-4；后段要电时打开 M6 的备用电池。", "Take M7 and M6 off from the tail first and K-4 last; open M6's backup battery when the aft modules need power."],
	"cx_m_train_x": ["K-4 上的弯矩计读后面还挂着多少吨（满载约 160 t）。冷却液软管：阀开着时切会喷，先关阀、从低点排放口放掉残液。", "K-4's bending gauge reads the tonnes still hanging aft (about 160 t full). The coolant hoses spray if cut with their valves open: shut them and drain the low points first."],
	"cx_m_ore": ["料仓与松散矿石", "THE HOPPER AND LOOSE ORE"],
	"cx_m_ore_a": ["料仓里是一堆细矿和几十块看得见的矿块，从底部放料门放出。", "The hopper holds a heap of fines and tens of visible chunks, let out through the gates in its floor."],
	"cx_m_ore_b": ["料仓还半满以上时把放料门硬撬开或切开，矿一下倒向一边，撕裂料仓焊缝。", "Force or cut a gate open with the hopper still over half full and the ore dumps to one side, tearing its welds."],
	"cx_m_ore_c": ["正常打开放料门，让矿流进长槽按吨计价；张力件先泄力再拆。", "Open the gates properly and let the ore run into the trough, paid by the tonne; take the load off tensioned members before removing them."],
	"cx_m_ore_x": ["细矿以每秒几吨的流量流出，按矿种计价；上面的矿块随着矿堆下降一块块松开跟着走。", "The fines run out at tonnes a second, paid by ore type; the chunks above come loose one by one as the heap sinks and follow it."],
	"cx_m_rails": ["锁轨货物", "RAIL-LOCKED CARGO"],
	"cx_m_rails_a": ["货物和滑轨之间是轨道锁，不是螺栓：扳手卸不掉。", "Cargo sits on its rail behind rail locks, not bolts: no wrench frees it."],
	"cx_m_rails_b": ["门没开就解锁，货撞门；前面一件还锁着就放后面的，后一件撞前一件；切托着货的轨道，货被扯坏。", "Unlock with the doors shut and it hits them; release one behind a locked one and it rams it; cut the rail carrying it and it's torn."],
	"cx_m_rails_c": ["先放气、开货门（门靠总线供电，断电前开），再从最前面一件开始解锁，让货沿轨道开出。", "Vent, open the cargo doors (on bus power — before you cut it), then unlock from the front, letting each piece run out along its rail."],
	"cx_m_rails_x": ["货物出轨道末端后制动到 0.4 m/s 慢慢滑出；前一件没运走就放下一件会撞上。SV-122 的仪器挂在减振吊架上：还有仪器锁着就切主梁或减振连杆，整架砸下。", "Off the rail's end the cargo is braked to 0.4 m/s and drifts out; release the next before the last is moved and they collide. SV-122's instruments hang in a damped frame: cut its beam or links with instruments still locked to it and the whole frame drops."],
	"cx_m_rings": ["还在转的居住环", "HABITAT RINGS STILL TURNING"],
	"cx_m_rings_a": ["两个居住环约 3 rpm 旋转，靠轮毂的电机-制动器消旋。", "Two habitat rings turning at about 3 rpm, despun by the motor-brakes at their hubs."],
	"cx_m_rings_b": ["环上负载带电时刹车会烧滑环；只刹一个环船体被拧；环还转就锁轴承，轴承卡死。", "Brake with the ring's loads live and the slip ring burns; brake only one and the hull twists; lock the bearing while it turns and it seizes."],
	"cx_m_rings_c": ["断环上负载 → 开制动冷却 → 两环一起刹（电容满了放电）→ 停稳后锁轴承 → 再开过渡气闸。", "Ring loads off → brake cooling on → brake both together (dump the capacitor when full) → lock the bearing once still → only then the transfer airlocks."],
	"cx_m_rings_x": ["制动把环的动能回馈进电容，电容满了刹车就不起作用，要放电。两环转速差太大持续太久，船坞夹具过载。环上的门对着压力低得多的一侧打开，冲击会打碎玻璃。", "Braking feeds the ring's energy into a capacitor; full, the brake stops working until it's dumped. Two rings too far apart in speed for too long overload the berth's clamps. A ring room's door opened onto far lower pressure breaks its glass."],
	"cx_m_spine": ["主轴受力", "THE SPINE'S LOAD PATH"],
	"cx_m_spine_a": ["尾部的反应堆、发动机和推进剂挂在 440 m 主轴上，弦杆是传力路径。", "The tail — reactor, engines, propellant — hangs on the 440 m spine; its chords carry the load."],
	"cx_m_spine_b": ["切一根弦杆，剩下的弦杆分担整个尾部；超出能力那一段撕裂，尾部下坠扭转。", "Cut a chord and the rest carry the whole tail; past what they take, that segment tears and the tail sags and twists."],
	"cx_m_spine_c": ["先把尾部的重量拆下来，弦杆最后切。", "Take the weight off the tail first; cut the chords last."],
	"cx_m_spine_x": ["每一段承受它后面还在船上的所有重量，由还完整的弦杆平分。应变探头读各段受力。", "Each segment carries everything still aboard aft of it, shared by its chords that are still whole. Strain probes read each segment's load."],
	"cx_m_workday": ["多日作业", "A JOB OF SEVERAL DAYS"],
	"cx_m_workday_a": ["这艘船太大，一个工作日拆不完。", "This ship is too big for one working day."],
	"cx_m_workday_b": ["每多一天，合同就多一天的运营成本。", "Every extra day adds a day's running cost to the contract."],
	"cx_m_workday_c": ["规划好顺序，减少无用功；收工时一切自动保存，第二天接着干。", "Plan the order to waste nothing; at the end of a day everything is saved and work goes on next day."],
	"cx_m_workday_x": ["工作日按合同的游戏时间计算。收工时整个物理状态保存，下一天在原处继续。", "Days are counted from the contract's play time. At day's end the whole physical state is saved and the next day picks up where it stood."],
	# ---------------------------------------------------------------- mechanisms: precision
	"cx_m_mirror_dust": ["镜面污染", "MIRROR CONTAMINATION"],
	"cx_m_mirror_dust_a": ["主镜镜片极贵、易碎，有一张卷帘式防尘罩。", "The primary's segments are very dear and fragile; there is a roll-down dust cover."],
	"cx_m_mirror_dust_b": ["镜面附近的切割把金属粉尘撒在镜面上，每次切割都掉价值。", "Every cut near an uncovered segment throws metal dust on its face and takes value off."],
	"cx_m_mirror_dust_c": ["先放下防尘罩（电机要有电），再在附近切割。", "Run the dust cover down (its motor needs power) before cutting anywhere near."],
	"cx_m_mirror_dust_x": ["防尘罩是电动卷帘，没电不能放下；跟着卷轴一起拆走就没了。粉尘污染到一定程度后就不再更糟。", "The cover is a motorised blind and won't run without power; taken away with its roller, it's gone. Dust alone can only take a segment down so far."],
	"cx_m_mirror_lock": ["促动器锁与外圈先拆", "ACTUATOR LOCKS, OUTER RING FIRST"],
	"cx_m_mirror_lock_a": ["每圈镜片的促动器有一个锁开关，锁只在镜面控制柜有电时才能锁上。", "Each ring of segments has an actuator lock switch, which only latches while the mirror control cabinet has power."],
	"cx_m_mirror_lock_b": ["促动器没锁就拆镜片，镜片掉出镜座碎裂；外侧还有镜片时拆内侧，外侧的边缘崩掉。", "Free a segment with its ring unlocked and it drops out and cracks; free an inner one with an outer one still on and the outer's edge chips."],
	"cx_m_mirror_lock_c": ["断电前锁好所有圈的促动器，从外圈到内圈拆。", "Lock every ring before the power goes, and take them from the outside in."],
	"cx_m_mirror_lock_x": ["外圈镜片的内缘搭在内圈镜片上，所以必须由外向内。", "An outer segment's inner edge is carried by the one inside it, so it has to go outside-in."],
	"cx_m_glass": ["承压玻璃与烤裂", "GLASS UNDER PRESSURE AND HEAT"],
	"cx_m_glass_a": ["观景玻璃、穹顶玻璃和精密罩板，用压条螺栓固定，背后扛着舱压。", "Viewing glass, dome glass and precision panels, held by clamping strips with the room's pressure behind them."],
	"cx_m_glass_b": ["舱里还有压就拆，玻璃被推出去碎掉；附近 0.7 m 内动激光，玻璃烤裂。", "Unbolt it with pressure inside and it's blown out and shatters; work the laser within 0.7 m and it crazes."],
	"cx_m_glass_c": ["先泄压，远离玻璃切割，拧下压条整块取出。", "Vent first, cut well away, unbolt the strips and lift it out whole."],
	"cx_m_glass_x": ["一块 2 m² 的观景玻璃在 100 kPa 下受 20 吨推力，压条螺栓一松就失去约束。PS-12 的中央竖井两层的门同时开着时，两层成了一个舱，放一边会把另一层一起带走。", "A 2 m² viewing pane at 100 kPa carries twenty tonnes; loosen its strips and nothing holds it. On PS-12, with both of the shaft's doors open on two decks, those decks are one room, and venting one takes the other with it."],
	# ---------------------------------------------------------------- mechanisms: isolation and extraction
	"cx_m_vault": ["双路电锁库门", "THE TWO-SUPPLY VAULT LOCK"],
	"cx_m_vault_a": ["库门电磁铁走两路电：主总线，和检修柜里的门锁备用电源。", "Each vault door's solenoid has two supplies: the main bus and a backup in the service locker."],
	"cx_m_vault_b": ["断了外部主开关，测点读零，门锁和总线照样带电——备用电源经电磁铁倒灌回总线。", "Kill the main switch outside and the test point reads zero, but the lock and the bus are still live — the backup feeds back through the solenoid."],
	"cx_m_vault_c": ["进舰尾检修柜断备用电源，两路都断后扳释放杆，库放气，再开门。", "Go into the stern service locker and kill the backup; with both dead, pull the release lever, vent the vault, open it."],
	"cx_m_vault_x": ["门锁带电时库门打不开，释放杆也扳不动；扳了以后门自己就能开，不需要电。保管箱整件运走。", "While the lock has power the door won't open and the lever won't move; once pulled, the door opens on its own, no power needed. The deposit boxes go out whole."],
	"cx_m_nested": ["船中船", "A SHIP INSIDE A SHIP"],
	"cx_m_nested_a": ["货舱里装着一艘完整的小飞船，合同要它整艘完好取出。", "A whole small ship rides in the hold; the contract wants it out whole."],
	"cx_m_nested_b": ["小船任何一块外壳被切或拆，就不再“完整”，只按零件算；托架锁先松船首侧，它会撞向舱门。", "Cut or take any of its hull and it's no longer whole, only parts; release a bow-side cradle lock first and it lurches into the door."],
	"cx_m_nested_c": ["先处理小船自己的电池、燃料和舱压，从尾到首松托架锁，开首门，开绞车整体拖出。", "Make it safe first — its battery, fuel and air — release the cradle locks stern first, open the bow door, run the winch to slide it out."],
	"cx_m_nested_x": ["整艘完好的小船按一个整体计价，远高于它的零件（溢价约是零件价值的 7 倍）。撞上舱门会扣掉一部分溢价、碰坏它的设备。", "Whole, the small ship is priced as one, far above its parts (about seven times their value). Lurching into the door costs part of that premium and knocks its fittings."],
	"cx_s_ullage": ["带压罐与气垫", "PRESSURISED TANKS AND THE ULLAGE"],
	"cx_s_ullage_a": ["推进剂罐顶部是一层高压气垫（增压气），把液体压向出口。", "Above a propellant tank's liquid sits a cushion of high-pressure gas that drives it to the outlet."],
	"cx_s_ullage_b": ["带压时切开，气垫会把推进剂一起喷出来；整罐切断，几秒内排空。泄压后的罐只会慢慢渗。", "Cut it under pressure and the cushion blows the propellant out with it; sever the tank and it empties in seconds. A vented tank only seeps."],
	"cx_s_ullage_c": ["先关增压，再从排气口放掉气垫，最后才抽液、拆罐。", "Shut the pressurisation off first, vent the ullage at its port, only then draw it down and take it out."],
	"cx_s_ullage_x": ["增压气不断补进来，罐压就降不下去，放气只是白放；所以顺序是先断气源、再放气垫。气垫放掉后，罐里只剩液体自己的蒸气压，破口处只是渗出，不再喷射。", "While the pressurant keeps coming the tank pressure won't fall and venting is wasted, so the order is: cut the supply, then vent the ullage. With it gone only the liquid's own vapour pressure is left, and a hole seeps instead of jetting."],
	"cx_m_hypergolic": ["自燃推进剂", "HYPERGOLIC PROPELLANTS"],
	"cx_m_hypergolic_a": ["甲基肼罐（T-1、T-3）和四氧化二氮罐（T-2）分开装，T-2 不接燃料总管。", "Methylhydrazine in T-1 and T-3, nitrogen tetroxide in T-2; T-2 is not on the fuel manifold."],
	"cx_m_hypergolic_b": ["两种一碰就着，不需要火花，真空里也会爆；爆燃按 TNT 当量计伤害半径。", "The two light the moment they meet, no spark needed, even in vacuum; the blast's reach goes by its TNT equivalent."],
	"cx_m_hypergolic_c": ["T-2 从它自己的排放口 LD-2 单独抽；两种的管线和罐别同时破口。", "Draw T-2 alone at its own drain LD-2; never have both kinds' lines or tanks open at once."],
	"cx_m_hypergolic_x": ["自燃推进剂省掉了点火器，发动机开关几百次都可靠，所以常用于姿控和变轨。代价是两种都剧毒、腐蚀，泄漏的蒸气碰上就起火。拆解时它们必须在不同的时间、从不同的口子出来。", "Hypergolics need no igniter, so an engine relights reliably hundreds of times: that is why they fly in thrusters and orbit-raising stages. The price: both are toxic and corrosive, and their vapours ignite on contact. Taking a ship apart, they leave at different times through different ports."],
	"cx_s_contents": ["先测再切：容器里有什么", "MEASURE BEFORE YOU CUT: WHAT'S INSIDE"],
	"cx_s_contents_a": ["灭火瓶、气瓶、储罐大多不是空的：测量工具扫过去会多一行“内容物”读数。", "Extinguishers, cylinders and tanks are mostly not empty: the measuring tool shows a CONTENTS line for each."],
	"cx_s_contents_b": ["气体端口叫“编号-V”，液体端口叫“编号-D”；装着液体的罐更重，抓不动。", "A gas port is named <tag>-V, a liquid port <tag>-D; a tank with liquid in it is heavier, too heavy to grab."],
	"cx_s_contents_c": ["先测，看清是什么、多少压力，再决定：放、抽，还是整件送走。", "Measure first: what it is, at what pressure. Then decide: vent, draw, or send it whole."],
	"cx_s_contents_x": ["灭火瓶里是约 5.7 MPa 的二氧化碳，氧气瓶是 15 MPa 的氧气，还有氮气、压缩空气、蓄能器、氦气和氢取样瓶；液罐里是水、泥浆、泡沫液、润滑油或服务推进剂。同样的外形，切开后的后果完全不同。", "Extinguishers hold CO2 at about 5.7 MPa, oxygen cylinders 15 MPa of oxygen; there are nitrogen, compressed air, accumulators, helium and hydrogen sample bottles; tanks hold water, mud, foam, lube oil or service propellant. The same shape, cut open, ends very differently."],
	"cx_s_o2_rich": ["富氧助燃", "OXYGEN-RICH AIR"],
	"cx_s_o2_rich_a": ["舱里氧气超过正常空气的 21%：氧气瓶破了，或者舱本来就富氧。", "A room's air with more oxygen than the usual 21 %: a cylinder burst, or the room was rich to begin with."],
	"cx_s_o2_rich_b": ["氧越多，越容易点着、烧得越猛；切口、火花一碰就着。氢气本身也能烧。", "The more oxygen, the easier anything lights and the fiercer it burns: a cut or a spark is enough. Hydrogen burns on its own."],
	"cx_s_o2_rich_c": ["测舱内氧浓度；超标就先把舱放空，再动激光。", "Measure the room's oxygen; over the mark, vent the room before the laser."],
	"cx_s_o2_rich_x": ["空气里的氮气稀释了氧，也吸走燃烧放出的热。氧浓度一旦超过 30%，布料、塑料、润滑油的燃速成倍上升；纯氧环境里连钢丝都能被点燃。", "The nitrogen in air thins the oxygen and soaks up a fire's heat. Above 30 % oxygen, fabric, plastics and oil burn several times faster; in pure oxygen even steel wool will burn."],
	# ---------------------------------------------------------------- (end)
}
